{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Mm7CPEKDon1QHwALt8C8da","type":"tool_result","content":"380\t\n381\t### 3.1 Track system (`20-track.js`)\n382\t\n383\t**TrackDef (data, metres; §4.3 has all four):**\n384\t\n385\t```js\n386\tSN.TRACKS.solenne = {\n387\t  id: 'solenne', name: 'PORT SOLENNE', place: 'RIVIERA SPRAWL · MEDITERRANEAN ZONE', tier: 1, theme: 'coast', song: 'solenne',\n388\t  width: 28,                       // metres, full width between the walls (per control point override: { w })\n389\t  origin: [2048, 2048, 0],         // metres, added to every point (keeps the world inside World3D's terrain square)\n390\t  points: [[x, y, z], ...],        // a closed loop in driving order\n391\t  widths: { 18: 30 },              // optional per control point width overrides (metres), interpolated between points\n392\t  start: 230,                      // metres along the spline from points[0] to the start line (s = 0 after rebasing)\n393\t  jumps:  [{ from: 12, to: 14, kind: 'drop', name: 'THE HARBOUR STEP' }],                 // control-point indices\n394\t  tunnels:[{ a: { cp: 7, d: 30 }, b: { cp: 9, d: 40 }, style: 'stone' }],\n395\t  speedPads:  [{ cp: 1, d: 120, u: 0 }, ...],   // cp + d metres along the track, u metres lateral (+ right)\n396\t  weaponPads: [{ cp: 2, d: 80 }, ...],          // a row of three pads across (u = -8, 0, +8), or { u } for one\n397\t  pit: { a: { cp: 0, d: 20 }, b: { cp: 1, d: 259 }, side: 'right', w: 8 },\n398\t  openEdges: [{ a: {…}, b: {…}, side: 'left' }],  // no wall: a craft can leave the track and fall (rescue)\n399\t  banks: [{ from: 15, to: 20, deg: 28 }],         // manual bank over a run of control points (else auto)\n400\t  scenery: {...}                                  // theme parameters (§4.3, §3.7)\n401\t};\n402\t```\n403\t\n404\t**Build (`SN.Track.build(def)`, deterministic, about 10 ms each):**\n405\t\n406\t1. Convert points to u (`×16`, plus the origin). Build a closed **centripetal Catmull-Rom** (α = 0.5) through them:\n407\t   App. A, the same code as `tools/trackcheck.mjs`. Sample each segment 64 times, accumulate arc length, then\n408\t   **resample at ds = 32 u (2 m)**, giving 1,900–2,520 slices. Record each control point's knot `s` exactly (needed by\n409\t   the `{cp, d}` features).\n410\t2. Rebase so that `s = 0` is at `start`. Every stored `s` is then `(raw − start) mod L`.\n411\t3. Per slice: `C` (centre), `F` (unit tangent from central differences), the plan-view curvature `κ` (signed, from the\n412\t   heading change over ±10 m), the width `w` (interpolated per control point; half width `hw = w/2`), the **bank** and\n413\t   the frame. Auto bank is `b = clamp(1600 / R_m, 0, 28)°`, signed by `κ` and smoothed over ±40 m (a 120 m radius\n414\t   gives 13°, 56 m gives 28°). A manual `banks` entry overrides it with a 60 m blend at each end. Frame:\n415\t   `R0 = normalize(cross(Zup, F))`, `U0 = cross(F, R0)`, then rotate both by the bank (§2.4).\n416\t4. Features → slice flags and lists:\n417\t   - `gap` and `drop` ranges from the jumps;\n418\t   - `tunnel` with its ceiling at 12 m;\n419\t   - `open` per side; `pit` range and side;\n420\t   - pads as rectangles in (s, u): speed pad 8 m long × 6 m wide, weapon pad 6 × 6 m;\n421\t   - **8 sectors** at equal s;\n422\t   - **grid slots**: 8 slots, 2 per row, rows 16 m apart, the first row 10 m behind the line, at `u = ∓4.5 m`,\n423\t     staggered 6 m;\n424\t   - **overpasses**: auto-detected exactly as the checker does (App. C), with the clearance stored.\n425\t5. **2D bucket grid** (cell 32 m) of slice indices for `T.query(x, y, zHint)`. It feeds particles, the terrain carve,\n426\t   scenery placement, trackside cameras and the minimap.\n427\t6. Validation (throws with the track id and the reason):\n428\t   - length within 1 % of §4.3;\n429\t   - every overpass clearance ≥ 12 m;\n430\t   - no unintended overlap;\n431\t   - every drop has a heading change ≤ 25° and every gap ≤ 10°;\n432\t   - no pad in a gap or drop;\n433\t   - a weapon pad row fits inside `hw − 1 m`;\n434\t   - the pit range has no jump.\n435\t\n436\t**Surface model (`T.surface(s, u)`):**\n437\t\n438\t| Slice kind | Surface point P, normal N | Walls |\n439\t| --- | --- | --- |\n440\t| `deck` (normal) | `P = C + R'·u`, `N = U'` | at `±hw`, unless the edge is `open` |\n441\t| `gap` (a void) | none. The craft is airborne. Below `zLip − 40 m` it is a **fall**, and a rescue follows | none |\n442\t| `drop` (step down) | the **lower deck**: flat, at the far edge's height `z1`, following the spline in plan view: `P = (C.x + R'h.x·u, C.y + R'h.y·u, z1 + bank1 tilt)`, where `R'h` is the horizontal part of `R'`, `N = up` tilted by the far edge's bank | at `±hw(s1)` along the plan path |\n443\t| `tunnel` | as deck, plus a ceiling at `h = 12 m`: clamp the craft below `12 m − 1.5 m` and cancel its upward velocity | yes |\n444\t\n445\t**`T.locate(P, sHint)`** runs 3 Newton steps: `s += dot(P − C(s), F(s))` (clamped to ±64 u a step, wrapping at L),\n446\tthen `u = dot(P − C, R')` and `h = dot(P − Psurf, N)`. It is always local to the craft's previous `s`, which makes\n447\toverpasses safe: the lower track is never \"found\" from the upper one. Each craft keeps `s` continuous. Its progress\n448\t`p` adds L on each forward wrap and subtracts on a backward one.\n449\t\n450\t**Racing line and speed profile (per track, per class, built at load):**\n451\t- *Line:* an elastic band. Start with u = 0 everywhere. Repeat 400 times over all slices:\n452\t  `mid = (P[i−1] + P[i+1]) / 2`, `u_i += 0.5·(dot(mid − C_i, R'_i) − u_i)`, clamp `|u_i| ≤ hw_i − 3.5 m`. On a gap\n453\t  approach (150 m before the lip to the far edge) pull u toward 0, weight 0.8. That gives the minimum-curvature line.\n454\t  Then compute its own plan curvature `κL`.\n455\t- *Speed:* `vmax_i = min(top_c, sqrt(alat_c / |κL_i|))`, with\n456\t  `alat_c = gripMax_c × 1.15 × skillK` (gripMax is 40 m/s² at SPARK, §3.2; ×1.15 for the airbrakes the AI uses).\n457\t  Then a forward pass with\n458\t  `a = athr_c·(1 − (v/top_c)²)`, a backward pass with airbrake deceleration `450 u/s² × (top_c/1440)` (28 m/s² at\n459\t  SPARK), repeated 3 times around the loop. On a **gap** approach enforce `v ≥ vJump` (1360 u/s = 85 m/s for the\n460\t  Karakum gorge, whose checked minimum is 75 m/s). Gap and drop slices ignore curvature.\n461\t- These two arrays drive the AI (§3.5), autopilot, the attract mode, the bots in the tests, the medal calibration and\n462\t  the TV director's anticipation.\n463\t\n464\t**Minimap:** the plan-view polyline of `C` every 20 m, fitted to a 72 × 72 px box (aspect kept). Overpass upper\n465\tsections are drawn last and brighter.\n466\t\n467\t### 3.2 Craft physics and handling (`25-ship.js`, `27-collide.js`)\n468\t\n469\t**State per craft:** `P, V` (world, u and u/s), `F` (heading, unit), the frame `U, R`, `s, u, h, p` (track), `lap`,\n470\t`sector`, `grounded`, `airT`, `energy` (0..100), `boostT`, `boostMul`, `weapon`, `charge`, `lockT`, `shieldT`\n471\t(bulwark), `autoT`, `rollT` and `rollDir`, `rollDone`, `shiftCD`, `stagger`, `rescueT`, `elim`, `respawnT`,\n472\t`finished`, `stats` (hits, kills, wall touches, pads, rolls, best lap…), `prev` (last step's `P`, quaternion; for\n473\tdrawing).\n474\t\n475\t**Craft constants.** Length 6 m (96 u). Collision is 2 spheres of r = 22 u at ±26 u along F. Hover height\n476\t`H0 = 14 u`. Ship half width for the walls: 24 u.\n477\t\n478\t**Class (§4.2) × team stats (§4.1) give the effective numbers.** Stats run 1–10:\n479\t- `top = classTop × (0.94 + 0.012·speed)`;\n480\t- `athr = 0.55·top × (0.80 + 0.04·thrust)`;\n481\t- `steer = 1.9 rad/s × (top/1440)^0.5 × (0.82 + 0.035·handling)`;\n482\t- `grip = 5.5/s × (top/1440)^0.5 × (0.82 + 0.035·handling)` (how fast the slide is caught);\n483\t- `gripMax = 640 u/s² × (top/1440)^1.5 × (0.82 + 0.035·handling)`: the most lateral acceleration the hover field gives\n484\t  (40 m/s² at SPARK). This cap is what makes speed, lines and airbrakes matter;\n485\t- `dmgMul = 1.35 − 0.06·shield`;\n486\t- `mass = 0.8 + 0.05·shield`.\n487\t\n488\tAll of them are also multiplied by the Tune sliders.\n489\t\n490\t**The step** (1/120 s, in this order, for each craft in grid order):\n491\t\n492\t1. **Controls in.** From the human mapping (§3.9), the AI, the replay, the autopilot or the bot. Keyboard steering\n493\t   ramps at 6/s toward ±1 so the keys feel analog. The stick passes straight through.\n494\t2. **Yaw.** `yawTarget = steer·steerRate·(1 − 0.35·v/top) + (brakeR − brakeL)·airbrakeYaw` (with\n495\t   `airbrakeYaw = 1.4 rad/s × (top/1440)^0.5`). `yawRate → yawTarget` at `steerResponse` (9/s). Rotate F about U by\n496\t   `yawRate·dt`. While `stagger > 0` (a hit), steering is ignored and the craft wobbles ±0.4 rad/s.\n497\t3. **Thrust and drag**, along F:\n498\t   - `a = thrust·athr·boostK − cd·v² − coast − brakeDrag`;\n499\t   - `cd = athr / top²` (so held thrust settles at `top`);\n500\t   - while boosting, `top·boostMul` replaces `top` in `cd` and the thrust is ×1.8;\n501\t   - `coast = 40 u/s²` when not thrusting;\n502\t   - `brakeDrag = (brakeL + brakeR)/2 × airbrakeDrag × 0.35·top`;\n503\t   - slope: add `−300 u/s² × F.z` (downhill speeds you up);\n504\t   - pitch: nose-down cuts drag by 3 %·pitch.\n505\t4. **Grip and slide.**\n506\t   - Split V into the along-F part and the lateral part `vl = dot(V, R)`.\n507\t   - The lateral grip available is `gmax = gripMax·(1 + 0.6·max(brakeL, brakeR))`: the airbrake flap works as a\n508\t     rudder, which is why airbrakes are the cornering tool.\n509\t   - Reduce `vl` toward 0 by `min(|vl|·(1 − e^(−grip·dt)), gmax·dt)`. A turn that needs more than `gmax` (`v²/R`)\n510\t     slides outward.\n511\t   - **Slip cap:** if the angle between F and V exceeds `slipMax` (35°), rotate F back to 35° from V. The craft\n512\t     slides, never spins.\n513\t   - **Scrub:** speed `−= scrubK·|vl|·dt` (scrubK 0.35/s). Sliding costs speed.\n514\t   - **Side-shift** (a press; grounded; cooldown 0.6 s): a separate lateral velocity `vShift = ±sideShiftSpeed`\n515\t     (768 u/s) that decays at `shiftDecay` (12/s), outside the grip cap. That gives about 4 m of sideways jump in\n516\t     0.3 s. Thruster puffs.\n517\t5. **Hover / air.** Get the surface at the craft's `(s, u)`.\n518\t   - **Grounded:** surface present and `h < captureH` (64 u).\n519\t     - Spring along N: `aN = k·(Ht − h) − c·vN`, clamped to `[−magnetPull, +900]`, with `k = 220/s²`, `c = 28/s`,\n520\t       `magnetPull = 1800 u/s²` and `Ht = H0 − 4·pitch + bob` (bob is `1.2·sin(2.2 t)`).\n521\t     - Gravity is cancelled while grounded: the anti-gravity field is the source's fiction.\n522\t     - The craft's up vector U slerps to N at 12/s.\n523\t     - At crests the spring cannot pull hard enough, so `h` grows past `captureH` and the craft lifts off by itself.\n524\t       Ramps launch the same way.\n525\t   - **Airborne:** `a = −airGravity·(1 + 0.45·pitch)·Zup` (airGravity 640 u/s² = 40 m/s²). U slerps to the surface\n526\t     normal below (if one is within 200 u) or else to Zup at 2/s. `airT += dt`.\n527\t   - **Landing** (surface present, `h < H0 + 4`, `vN < 0`): impact angle `θ = atan(−vN / v)`.\n528\t     - If `θ > 25°`: energy `−(θ − 25)·0.4·dmgMul`, speed `×(1 − min(0.35, (θ − 15°)/60°))`, and a hard-landing event\n529\t       (shake, sparks, a \"THUD\").\n530\t     - Otherwise a soft landing.\n531\t     - Either way, resolve the barrel roll (step 7).\n532\t   - **Bottoming out:** `h < 5 u` → `h = 5`, `vN = max(vN, 0)`, speed `×0.996` per step, a scrape event.\n533\t6. **Integrate** `V += a·dt`, `P += V·dt`. Then `T.locate` → `s, u, h`.\n534\t7. **Barrel roll.** Triggers only when airborne with `airT > 0.08 s`:\n535\t   - a side-shift press, or\n536\t   - a steer flick (steer crosses ≤ −0.7 then ≥ +0.7, or the reverse, and back, within 0.4 s; detected in\n537\t     `01-input.js`).\n538\t\n539\t   The roll starts with `rollT = 0.45 s` toward rollDir and costs `rollCost` (10) energy. On landing:\n540\t   - a finished roll → boost (`boostMul 1.2`, 1.2 s) + \"BARREL ROLL\" event;\n541\t   - a roll still turning → \"BOTCHED\": speed ×0.75, energy −5, stagger 0.5 s.\n542\t\n543\t   The visual is a full 360° about F. Long jumps allow several rolls, each costing energy.\n544\t8. **Walls** (deck/drop, wall present on that side). `lim = hw − 24 u`. If `|u| > lim`:\n545\t   - push P back by `(|u| − lim)` along ∓R';\n546\t   - normal speed `vn = dot(V, ±R')`; if `vn > 0`, then `V −= ±R'·vn·(1 + wallBounce)` with `wallBounce` 0.35;\n547\t   - tangential scrub: `V −= F·min(v, wallFriction·vn)` with `wallFriction` 0.25;\n548\t   - **yaw nudge:** rotate F toward the track tangent by `min(0.5, 0.6·vn/v)` rad (the craft never grinds nose-first);\n549\t   - damage `wallDamage·clamp((vn − 150)/120, 0, 12)·dmgMul`;\n550\t   - scraping (in contact with `vn ≤ 150`) costs 4 energy/s while `v > 500`;\n551\t   - events `wall` / `scrape`.\n552\t\n553\t   **Open edges:** `|u| > hw + 2 m` with no wall means no surface. The craft falls, and a rescue follows (step 11).\n554\t9. **Pads and pit** (in track space, grounded only):\n555\t   - **Speed pad:** `boostT = min(2.0, max(boostT, padBoostTime))` (0.9 s), `boostMul = padBoost` (1.25). A pad\n556\t     re-arms per craft after 0.5 s.\n557\t   - **Weapon pad:** if no weapon is held, roll one (§3.4); event `pickup`.\n558\t   - **Pit strip:** `energy += pitRecharge·dt` (25/s), a green shimmer FX and a recharge sound loop.\n559\t10. **Energy.** Every damage source goes through `SN.Ship.damage(ship, amount, cause, by)`. It applies `dmgMul`.\n560\t    `shieldT > 0` (bulwark) or god mode blocks it. Below 25 % a warning plays. At 0 the craft is eliminated (§3.3\n561\t    decides between DNF and respawn).\n562\t11. **Rescue.** Triggered by:\n563\t    - a fall below the kill height (gap: `zLip − 40 m`; otherwise surface − 60 m);\n564\t    - leaving an open edge: rescue once the craft is 6 m below the deck, or after 1 s. There is no terrain\n565\t      collision, so the fall must end before it would visibly pass through the ground. The terrain carve keeps the\n566\t      ground ≥ 10 m below every open edge (§3.7) so the drop reads as a fall;\n567\t    - being stuck (`v < 50 u/s` for 3 s while thrusting, outside the countdown).\n568\t\n569\t    The rescue drone lifts the craft back on the centre line at `s_lastGood + 20 m` (the last grounded `s` with\n570\t    `|u| < hw`), in 2.5 s with the craft frozen. Energy −10, speed 0, event `rescue`. In OVERCLOCK the rescue costs 20\n571\t    energy.\n572\t12. **Ship–ship collisions** (`27-collide.js`, after all craft move, pairs in index order): sphere pairs. The craft are\n573\t    separated along the contact normal in inverse proportion to mass. Impulse\n574\t    `j = −(1 + 0.3)·vn / (1/m1 + 1/m2)`. Damage `0.004·|vn|` each. A `bump` event fires above 120 u/s. Ghost craft\n575\t    (hub, dev \"ghost AI\") skip this.\n576\t13. **Launch boost** (countdown): holding thrust raises the revs at 0.6/s; releasing drops them at 0.8/s.\n577\t    - At GO, revs in 0.72–0.88 → \"PERFECT START\" boost (1.0 s, ×1.25).\n578\t    - Revs above 0.95 → \"STALL\" (no thrust for 0.5 s).\n579\t    - The HUD shows a rev bar during the countdown.\n580\t\n581\t**Feel targets (checked by the physics tests; tune with the sliders until they hold):**\n582\t- 0 → 90 % of top in 2.2–3.0 s (it depends on the THRUST stat: 2.68 s at THRUST 5 by the formula).\n583\t- Thrust-only top speed within ±2 % of `top`.\n584\t- Lateral grip caps out at `gripMax`. These figures were checked with a 2D model of this exact step during planning\n585\t  (KESTREL stats, SPARK, top 328 km/h):\n586\t  - full lock with no airbrake, from top speed: path radius 120–150 m over the first second, the nose at the 35° slip\n587\t    cap, about 255 km/h after 1.4 s, a slide that settles near 180 km/h if held;\n588\t  - full lock with the inside airbrake fully on: radius 45–60 m, about 160 km/h after 1.4 s (the hairpin tool);\n589\t  - steady cornering on a 65 m line: about 188 km/h without airbrakes, about 238 km/h with exactly the inside\n590\t    airbrake the corner needs.\n591\t\n592\t  The Solenne lighthouse hairpin is taken without a wall touch by the AI at skill 1.\n593\t- Side-shift moves the craft about 4 m sideways (768 u/s decaying at 12/s gives 4.2 m).\n594\t- Every jump in §4.3 behaves as App. C says, at each class's top speed (gap: clears at ≥ 75 m/s, falls short below\n595\t  60 m/s).\n596\t- At 3,000 u/s nothing tunnels through a wall or the surface.\n597\t\n598\t**Visual-only motion** (computed in `62-shipkit.js` from the state, never fed back):\n599\t- roll = bank + `clamp(yawRate·0.28, ±0.5)` + barrel roll angle;\n600\t- pitch = slope + `pitch·7°` + bob;\n601\t- airbrake flaps open by `brake·60°`;\n602\t- engine glow follows thrust;\n603\t- the boost flame lengthens with `boostT`;\n604\t- the shield shell flashes on a hit;\n605\t- below 25 % energy, damage smoke and sparks.\n606\t\n607\t### 3.3 Race director and modes (`40-race.js`)\n608\t\n609\t**Lifecycle** (`race.state`):\n610\t\n611\t1. `intro`: a 6 s flyover by the TV director (§3.6). The track card shows name, place, length, laps, class. ✕, Enter\n612\t   or a click skips it.\n613\t2. `grid`: 1.5 s, a chase cam on the player.\n614\t3. `countdown`: 3 s with lights (3-2-1-GO) on the start gantry and the HUD, the launch revs and the announcer.\n615\t4. `racing`.\n616\t5. `finished`: the player crossed the line, or was eliminated.\n617\t   - The player becomes a ghost-cam spectator (TV director) while the others finish.\n618\t   - After 8 s, or when every craft is done, unfinished craft get an estimated time\n619\t     (`t + (remaining distance / their average speed)`) and the results are sealed.\n620\t6. `results`: go to the `results` scene.\n621\t\n622\t**Laps and sectors.** A lap counts when the craft crosses `s = 0` forward after passing sectors 1…7 in order. Lap\n623\ttime, best lap and the final lap's announcer/music layer come from it. **Wrong way:** `dot(F, trackF) < −0.2` and\n624\t`v > 300 u/s` for 1.2 s → a HUD warning plus an announcer line.\n625\t\n626\t**Positions:** sorted by `finished` time, then by progress `p`, descending. The order is recomputed every step, with\n627\ta \"position changed\" event for the HUD arrows.\n628\t\n629\t**Elimination:** at energy 0 the craft explodes. In RACE/SEASON it is **DNF** (results show \"ELIMINATED\"). In\n630\tSNIPEOUT, ACADEMY and hub sessions it **respawns** 3 s later at its own `s` on the centre line, with 100 % energy and\n631\t2 s of invulnerability (blinking).\n632\t\n633\t**Modes (`rules` objects, one file section each):**\n634\t\n635\t| Mode | Field | Weapons | Rules / win | Medals |\n636\t| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n637\t| QUICK RACE | 8 craft (player + 7 AI) | on | laps 1–5 (default 3); place = result | gold 1st, silver 2nd, bronze 3rd |\n638\t| TIME TRIAL | solo | off (pads dark) | 3 laps; ghost of your best run (§3.13) | per track/class times, measured (§4.2) |\n639\t| HOT LAP | solo, flying start (spawn 300 m before the line at 80 % top) | off | unlimited laps; the best lap counts; End run in the pause menu (or 10 laps) | per track/class lap times |\n640\t| SNIPEOUT | 8 craft | on, offensive-weighted table, no AUTOPILOT | +1 per hit landed, +3 per elimination, +1 bonus for a RAILSHOT elimination (\"SNIPED\"); respawns; first to target (10 or 12) or most after 5 min | 1st/2nd/3rd |\n641\t| OVERCLOCK | solo, neon skin | off; speed pads off | automatic thrust; zone n every 12 s: `top = SPARK·(0.75 + 0.06·n)`; walls ×1.5 damage; +5 energy per zone cleared; ends at 0 energy | bronze zone 10, silver 20, gold 30, \"OVERCLOCKED\" 40 |\n642\t| ACADEMY | solo (+ drones) | scripted | 11 drills (§4.5), each retried until passed | gold when every drill passed first time |\n643\t| VERSUS | 2 humans + 6 AI, split screen | on | race or snipeout, as above | per player |\n644\t| SEASON event | as its mode | as its mode | the event's target | the event's medal rule |\n645\t| GRAND PRIX | 8 craft × 4 races | on | points 10-8-6-5-4-3-2-1; DNF 0; ties by best finish | champion = gold, 2nd = silver, 3rd = bronze |\n646\t| HUB SESSION | each copy: own craft + 7 AI; other humans as ghosts | on | 3 laps FLARE on a seeded track; elimination respawns; `AIHub.result({ time })` | the hub's standings |\n647\t\n648\t**Results data** (`race.results()`): place, pilot, team, time or gap, best lap, points (GP/SNIPEOUT), DNF, medal for\n649\tthe player, new records, and unlocks triggered (season).\n650\t\n651\t### 3.4 Weapons and pickups (`30-weapons.js`, `06-data-weapons.js`)\n652\t\n653\tProjectiles live in **track space**: `s, u, h` and `vs, vu`. They follow the track through curves, the way the\n654\tsource's weapons hug it. Each step they advance and wrap with `s`. They hit a craft when `|Δs| < 40 u`, `|Δu| < 34 u`\n655\tand `|Δh| < 40 u`. They hit a wall at `|u| > hw` (they explode). In gaps they fly straight on and expire. Every hit\n656\tgoes through `SN.Ship.damage` and emits `hit`. The 3D FX are in `68-fx.js`.\n657\t\n658\t| Weapon (icon colour) | Fire | Behaviour | Damage / effect | Absorb |\n659\t| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n660\t| **SWARM** (red) | tap | 3 rockets, lateral spread −1.5/0/+1.5 m growing at 120 u/s, speed `v_ship + 2400`, life 1.4 s | 10 each, jolt (speed ×0.9, stagger 0.2 s) | +16 |\n661\t| **SEEKER** (orange) | lock: hold the target ahead in a 25° cone within 3000 u for 0.6 s (\"LOCKED\" tone), then press | homing missile, speed `v + 2000`, steers u toward the target at 900 u/s, `s` speed matched to catch up; unlocked it flies straight | 24, spin-out stagger 0.5 s | +22 |\n662\t| **MINEFIELD** (magenta) | tap | drops 5 mines behind at 0.12 s intervals (`u` at drop, `s − 60 u`); armed after 0.3 s; live 30 s; trigger radius 40 u | 12 each, jolt | +18 |\n663\t| **CANNON** (yellow) | hold | 24 bolts at 12/s, speed `v + 4200`, ±0.5 m jitter, aim assist toward a target within ±1.5 m | 2.5 per bolt | +14 |\n664\t| **RAILSHOT** (white/cyan): the *snipe* | hold to charge 0.8 s (ring on the HUD), release to fire | hitscan along the track ahead to 4000 u. It hits the first craft within ±32 u of the aim line `u_aim(Δs) = u + Δs·tan(heading vs track)` (aim assist: ±16 u extra if charged fully). A beam is drawn in 3D | 34, big jolt; an elimination by RAILSHOT is a \"SNIPED!\" | +28 |\n665\t| **TREMOR** (green) | tap | a wave rolls forward along the surface from the user, full width, at `v + 1800` for 1.3 s. It hits each **grounded** craft it passes (airborne craft dodge it) | 26, pops the craft up 3 m, stagger 0.4 s | +30 |\n666\t| **BULWARK** (blue) | tap | invulnerable for 4 s (walls too); no pickups meanwhile | blocks everything | +12 |\n667\t| **AUTOPILOT** (teal) | tap | the AI drives for 5 s (skill 1.0); the HUD counts it down; ends early after a rescue | — | +10 |\n668\t| **NITRO** (amber) | tap | boost 2.2 s, `boostMul 1.35`, thrust ×2 | — | +10 |\n669\t| **SIPHON** (lime) | tap: it latches onto the nearest craft ahead by itself | beam to the nearest craft ahead within 1500 u (along the track) for 3 s; breaks beyond 1900 u | drains 9/s from the target into you | +20 |\n670\t\n671\t- **Absorb** (○ / Shift / right click): consumes the weapon and adds its absorb value × the `absorbMul` slider.\n672\t- **One weapon at a time.** A pad gives nothing while a weapon is held, or while BULWARK or AUTOPILOT runs.\n673\t- **Pickup roll:** weighted by position. Pick the table by `pos ∈ {1,2}` front, `{3..5}` mid, `{6..8}` back, then\n674\t  apply `pickupLuck` (0 = uniform, 1 = table, 2 = table squared).\n675\t\n676\t  | | SWARM | SEEKER | MINE | CANNON | RAIL | TREMOR | BULWARK | AUTO | NITRO | SIPHON |\n677\t  | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n678\t  | front | 2 | 1 | 4 | 3 | 1 | 0 | 3 | 0 | 1 | 1 |\n679\t  | mid | 3 | 3 | 2 | 2 | 2 | 1 | 2 | 1 | 2 | 2 |\n680\t  | back | 2 | 3 | 1 | 1 | 2 | 3 | 1 | 3 | 3 | 2 |\n681\t  | snipeout | 3 | 3 | 2 | 3 | 3 | 2 | 2 | 0 | 1 | 2 |\n682\t\n683\t  The HUD plays a 0.5 s slot-machine spin, then the announcer says the name. Rolls use `race.rng('pickup')`.\n684\t- **Warnings for the target:** a seeker lock beeps at the target and shows \"LOCK\" with an arrow at the bottom centre.\n685\t  A railshot charging aimed at you shows a thin red line.\n686\t\n687\t### 3.5 AI pilots (`35-ai.js`)\n688\t\n689\tEach AI craft produces `ShipControls` every step from the track's line and speed arrays and the race state. The same\n690\tfunction drives AUTOPILOT, the attract mode, the player bot in tests, and the medal calibration.\n691\t\n692\t1. **Look-ahead target.** `sL = s + 0.55 s·v + 300 u`. Target point `Q = C(sL) + R'(sL)·uTarget(sL)`.\n693\t   - `uTarget` = racing line `T.line` + avoidance offset + pad bias + pit bias.\n694\t   - Heading error `e` = the signed angle from F to `(Q − P)` projected on the surface plane.\n695\t   - `steer = clamp(2.2·e + 0.25·ė, −1, 1)`, plus seeded noise ±(0.05·(1 − skill)).\n696\t2. **Speed.** `vT = T.vline(s + 0.4·v)·skillK` (skillK = 0.86 + 0.14·skill, also scaling `alat`).\n697\t   - thrust if `v < vT·1.01`;\n698\t   - both airbrakes if `v > vT·1.05`;\n699\t   - the inside airbrake (the side of the turn) at `clamp((v²·|κL| − gripMax) / (0.6·gripMax), 0, 1)`, which is\n700\t     exactly the extra grip the corner needs, plus `clamp((|e| − 0.12)/0.28, 0, 1)` when the heading error is large;\n701\t   - pitch: nose-down on descents steeper than 4 %, nose-up on crests (vertical curvature) and over gaps when short of\n702\t     the landing.\n703\t3. **Avoidance and overtaking.** A craft ahead within 900 u with `|Δu| < 70 u` and closing → shift `uTarget` by\n704\t   ±110 u toward the wider side (blend 0.6 s). It returns to the line after passing. Mines seen ahead (within 1200 u)\n705\t   push `uTarget` away by 80 u. A side-shift dodges incoming weapons when skill > 0.7 (reaction 0.25 s).\n706\t4. **Pads.** A speed pad within 1500 u ahead and within 120 u of the line → bias `uTarget` onto it (skill-weighted).\n707\t   Weapon pads likewise when unarmed. Pit: if energy < 30 % and the pit is ahead within 2500 u → the pit line.\n708\t5. **Weapons (per weapon):**\n709\t   - SWARM, CANNON: a target ahead within 1800 u and `|Δu| < 60 u`.\n710\t   - SEEKER: fire when locked.\n711\t   - RAILSHOT: charge when a target is within 3500 u and `|Δu_aim| < 40 u`; release at full charge.\n712\t   - MINEFIELD: a craft behind within 1200 u, or simply in the last 30 % of a lap when leading.\n713\t   - TREMOR: ≥ 2 craft within 2500 u ahead.\n714\t   - BULWARK: a lock warning, or energy < 35 % in traffic.\n715\t   - AUTOPILOT: in a technical section (`|κ|` high) or with energy < 40 %.\n716\t   - NITRO: on a straight (`|κL| < 1/600 m` for the next 400 m).\n717\t   - SIPHON: a target ahead within 1400 u and own energy < 85.\n718\t   - Absorb instead when energy < 30 % and the weapon is defensive or useless at that moment.\n719\t   - Each pilot's `aggression` (0.4–1.3) scales reaction thresholds and hold times.\n720\t6. **Jumps.** Hold `v ≥ vJump` on gap approaches. Barrel roll when the predicted airtime is > 0.6 s, energy > 50 %\n721\t   and skill > 0.6, at chance `0.5·aggression` (attract: always).\n722\t7. **Mistakes.** For each corner (κ peak), a chance `(1 − skill)·0.15` to brake late by 0.25 s (it may scrape a wall).\n723\t8. **Rubber band** (Quick Race, Season, Versus; never Time Trial/Hot Lap/Overclock):\n724\t   `top ×= 1 + rb·clamp((p_player − p_ai)/32000, −1, 1)·0.04`, with rb from the difficulty (Easy 1.5, Normal 1.0,\n725\t   Hard 0.3) times the `aiRubberBand` slider.\n726\t9. **Difficulty** (Settings → Difficulty):\n727\t\n728\t   | | AI skill | aggression | rubber band |\n729\t   | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n730\t   | Easy | 0.86 | ×0.6 | 1.5 |\n731\t   | Normal | 0.93 | ×1.0 | 1.0 |\n732\t   | Hard | 0.99 | ×1.3 | 0.3 |\n733\t\n734\t   Each pilot has an offset (§4.1). NULL//SET pilots get +0.02.\n735\t10. **Attract cheats.** The AI may cheat freely in attract (TASK.md): infinite energy, pickups forced in rotation so\n736\t    all 10 weapons appear, a barrel roll on every jump, aggression 1.5.\n737\t\n738\t### 3.6 Cameras and the TV director (`60-render.js`)\n739\t\n740\tThe World3D camera runs in **`'fixed'`** mode. We compute a pose `{ x, y, z, yaw, pitch, roll, fov }` (engine units,\n741\tradians; `pitch < 0` looks down) every step into `camera.fixed`. In `onDraw` we **interpolate** between the last two\n742\tstep poses with `game.alpha` and write `world.camera.pose` (the header allows \"a last touch to camera.pose\"). Craft\n743\tmeshes are interpolated the same way (`prev` → current). Set `camera.target = { x, y, z }` to the player craft so the\n744\tsun's shadow box follows it.\n745\t\n746\t| Camera | Pose |\n747\t| --- | --- |\n748\t| **Chase** (default) | eye = `P − Fs·d + Us·hgt`, where `d = camDistance·(1 + 0.15·v/top)` (150 u) and `hgt = camHeight` (46 u). Look at `P + F·120 + U·12`. `Fs`, `Us` are F and U smoothed by slerp at `camLag` (8/s), so the camera swings, never cuts corners. `Us` blends from Zup toward the craft's U at 0.6, so the horizon tilts with the banks. `fov = camFov + camFovBoost·(v/top)²` (72° + 16°) + 6° while boosting. Shake from `game.shake` (impacts, rail hits, landings) |\n749\t| **Far chase** | d ×1.5, hgt ×1.6, fov −6° |\n750\t| **Cockpit** | eye = `P + F·20 + U·14`, look along F, full craft roll, fov 84° + boost. The craft mesh is hidden except a nose/canopy-rim \"dash\" mesh |\n751\t| **Look back** (held) | the chase eye mirrored in front of the craft looking back (`P + F·d + Us·hgt` → P) |\n752\t| **Free fly** (dev) | WASD/stick fly, Q/E or triggers up/down, mouse/right stick turn |\n753\t| **Podium / hangar orbit** | an orbit around a point (menus, results podium) |\n754\t\n755\tRoll sign: verify with a screenshot on Karakum's spiral, a right-hand banked turn. The horizon must tilt the way the\n756\ttrack does. If it is inverted, negate the roll in one place (`SN.cam.rollSign`).\n757\t\n758\t**TV director** (intro flyover, attract, replay, spectating, podium intro):\n759\t- **Camera spots** are built at load every ~200 m. Each is `C(s) + R'·side·(hw + 15…30 m) + Zup·(6…20 m)`, on the\n760\t  outside of curves, alternating sides on straights. Skip a spot if the terrain (`world.ground`) is above it, or if it\n761\t  is inside another track section (`T.query`). Tunnel spots go 2 m under the ceiling, 4 m from the wall. Overpass\n762\t  spots look up from the lower deck. Each spot stores `s`.\n763\t- **Shots:**\n764\t  - `trackside`: fixed eye, looking at the target, with the FOV narrowing (40→20°) as the target nears;\n765\t  - `heli`: 40 m up, 60 m back, following;\n766\t  - `chase`;\n767\t  - `nose`;\n768\t  - `low`: 1 m above the surface ahead, looking back at the target;\n769\t  - `flyby`: along the line 30 m ahead of the target, looking back.\n770\t- **Logic:**\n771\t  - target = the player (spectate/replay) or the most interesting craft (attract: leader, a close fight within 300 u,\n772\t    a weapon fired in the last 2 s, a jump);\n773\t  - pick the spot 150–900 u ahead of the target with a clear line (raycast against the track only), hold 2.5–6 s, and\n774\t    cut when the target passes the spot by 400 u;\n775\t  - every third cut is heli, chase, nose or low;\n776\t  - events cut early: an elimination, a railshot or a jump launch;\n777\t  - never cut twice within 1.2 s.\n778\t- **Intro flyover:** 6 s along the line from `s = −900 m` to the grid at 2.5× the target speed, then a 1 s whip onto\n779\t  the grid."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4110026b-2798-4dbf-ae8a-e81d8e816e30","uuid":"f73bc8a8-efc2-405d-8e6a-fdf7c60d1068","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:46:51.914Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261103-184630__xa320fb/work/PLAN.md","content":"\n### 3.1 Track system (`20-track.js`)\n\n**TrackDef (data, metres; §4.3 has all four):**\n\n```js\nSN.TRACKS.solenne = {\n  id: 'solenne', name: 'PORT SOLENNE', place: 'RIVIERA SPRAWL · MEDITERRANEAN ZONE', tier: 1, theme: 'coast', song: 'solenne',\n  width: 28,                       // metres, full width between the walls (per control point override: { w })\n  origin: [2048, 2048, 0],         // metres, added to every point (keeps the world inside World3D's terrain square)\n  points: [[x, y, z], ...],        // a closed loop in driving order\n  widths: { 18: 30 },              // optional per control point width overrides (metres), interpolated between points\n  start: 230,                      // metres along the spline from points[0] to the start line (s = 0 after rebasing)\n  jumps:  [{ from: 12, to: 14, kind: 'drop', name: 'THE HARBOUR STEP' }],                 // control-point indices\n  tunnels:[{ a: { cp: 7, d: 30 }, b: { cp: 9, d: 40 }, style: 'stone' }],\n  speedPads:  [{ cp: 1, d: 120, u: 0 }, ...],   // cp + d metres along the track, u metres lateral (+ right)\n  weaponPads: [{ cp: 2, d: 80 }, ...],          // a row of three pads across (u = -8, 0, +8), or { u } for one\n  pit: { a: { cp: 0, d: 20 }, b: { cp: 1, d: 259 }, side: 'right', w: 8 },\n  openEdges: [{ a: {…}, b: {…}, side: 'left' }],  // no wall: a craft can leave the track and fall (rescue)\n  banks: [{ from: 15, to: 20, deg: 28 }],         // manual bank over a run of control points (else auto)\n  scenery: {...}                                  // theme parameters (§4.3, §3.7)\n};\n```\n\n**Build (`SN.Track.build(def)`, deterministic, about 10 ms each):**\n\n1. Convert points to u (`×16`, plus the origin). Build a closed **centripetal Catmull-Rom** (α = 0.5) through them:\n   App. A, the same code as `tools/trackcheck.mjs`. Sample each segment 64 times, accumulate arc length, then\n   **resample at ds = 32 u (2 m)**, giving 1,900–2,520 slices. Record each control point's knot `s` exactly (needed by\n   the `{cp, d}` features).\n2. Rebase so that `s = 0` is at `start`. Every stored `s` is then `(raw − start) mod L`.\n3. Per slice: `C` (centre), `F` (unit tangent from central differences), the plan-view curvature `κ` (signed, from the\n   heading change over ±10 m), the width `w` (interpolated per control point; half width `hw = w/2`), the **bank** and\n   the frame. Auto bank is `b = clamp(1600 / R_m, 0, 28)°`, signed by `κ` and smoothed over ±40 m (a 120 m radius\n   gives 13°, 56 m gives 28°). A manual `banks` entry overrides it with a 60 m blend at each end. Frame:\n   `R0 = normalize(cross(Zup, F))`, `U0 = cross(F, R0)`, then rotate both by the bank (§2.4).\n4. Features → slice flags and lists:\n   - `gap` and `drop` ranges from the jumps;\n   - `tunnel` with its ceiling at 12 m;\n   - `open` per side; `pit` range and side;\n   - pads as rectangles in (s, u): speed pad 8 m long × 6 m wide, weapon pad 6 × 6 m;\n   - **8 sectors** at equal s;\n   - **grid slots**: 8 slots, 2 per row, rows 16 m apart, the first row 10 m behind the line, at `u = ∓4.5 m`,\n     staggered 6 m;\n   - **overpasses**: auto-detected exactly as the checker does (App. C), with the clearance stored.\n5. **2D bucket grid** (cell 32 m) of slice indices for `T.query(x, y, zHint)`. It feeds particles, the terrain carve,\n   scenery placement, trackside cameras and the minimap.\n6. Validation (throws with the track id and the reason):\n   - length within 1 % of §4.3;\n   - every overpass clearance ≥ 12 m;\n   - no unintended overlap;\n   - every drop has a heading change ≤ 25° and every gap ≤ 10°;\n   - no pad in a gap or drop;\n   - a weapon pad row fits inside `hw − 1 m`;\n   - the pit range has no jump.\n\n**Surface model (`T.surface(s, u)`):**\n\n| Slice kind | Surface point P, normal N | Walls |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `deck` (normal) | `P = C + R'·u`, `N = U'` | at `±hw`, unless the edge is `open` |\n| `gap` (a void) | none. The craft is airborne. Below `zLip − 40 m` it is a **fall**, and a rescue follows | none |\n| `drop` (step down) | the **lower deck**: flat, at the far edge's height `z1`, following the spline in plan view: `P = (C.x + R'h.x·u, C.y + R'h.y·u, z1 + bank1 tilt)`, where `R'h` is the horizontal part of `R'`, `N = up` tilted by the far edge's bank | at `±hw(s1)` along the plan path |\n| `tunnel` | as deck, plus a ceiling at `h = 12 m`: clamp the craft below `12 m − 1.5 m` and cancel its upward velocity | yes |\n\n**`T.locate(P, sHint)`** runs 3 Newton steps: `s += dot(P − C(s), F(s))` (clamped to ±64 u a step, wrapping at L),\nthen `u = dot(P − C, R')` and `h = dot(P − Psurf, N)`. It is always local to the craft's previous `s`, which makes\noverpasses safe: the lower track is never \"found\" from the upper one. Each craft keeps `s` continuous. Its progress\n`p` adds L on each forward wrap and subtracts on a backward one.\n\n**Racing line and speed profile (per track, per class, built at load):**\n- *Line:* an elastic band. Start with u = 0 everywhere. Repeat 400 times over all slices:\n  `mid = (P[i−1] + P[i+1]) / 2`, `u_i += 0.5·(dot(mid − C_i, R'_i) − u_i)`, clamp `|u_i| ≤ hw_i − 3.5 m`. On a gap\n  approach (150 m before the lip to the far edge) pull u toward 0, weight 0.8. That gives the minimum-curvature line.\n  Then compute its own plan curvature `κL`.\n- *Speed:* `vmax_i = min(top_c, sqrt(alat_c / |κL_i|))`, with\n  `alat_c = gripMax_c × 1.15 × skillK` (gripMax is 40 m/s² at SPARK, §3.2; ×1.15 for the airbrakes the AI uses).\n  Then a forward pass with\n  `a = athr_c·(1 − (v/top_c)²)`, a backward pass with airbrake deceleration `450 u/s² × (top_c/1440)` (28 m/s² at\n  SPARK), repeated 3 times around the loop. On a **gap** approach enforce `v ≥ vJump` (1360 u/s = 85 m/s for the\n  Karakum gorge, whose checked minimum is 75 m/s). Gap and drop slices ignore curvature.\n- These two arrays drive the AI (§3.5), autopilot, the attract mode, the bots in the tests, the medal calibration and\n  the TV director's anticipation.\n\n**Minimap:** the plan-view polyline of `C` every 20 m, fitted to a 72 × 72 px box (aspect kept). Overpass upper\nsections are drawn last and brighter.\n\n### 3.2 Craft physics and handling (`25-ship.js`, `27-collide.js`)\n\n**State per craft:** `P, V` (world, u and u/s), `F` (heading, unit), the frame `U, R`, `s, u, h, p` (track), `lap`,\n`sector`, `grounded`, `airT`, `energy` (0..100), `boostT`, `boostMul`, `weapon`, `charge`, `lockT`, `shieldT`\n(bulwark), `autoT`, `rollT` and `rollDir`, `rollDone`, `shiftCD`, `stagger`, `rescueT`, `elim`, `respawnT`,\n`finished`, `stats` (hits, kills, wall touches, pads, rolls, best lap…), `prev` (last step's `P`, quaternion; for\ndrawing).\n\n**Craft constants.** Length 6 m (96 u). Collision is 2 spheres of r = 22 u at ±26 u along F. Hover height\n`H0 = 14 u`. Ship half width for the walls: 24 u.\n\n**Class (§4.2) × team stats (§4.1) give the effective numbers.** Stats run 1–10:\n- `top = classTop × (0.94 + 0.012·speed)`;\n- `athr = 0.55·top × (0.80 + 0.04·thrust)`;\n- `steer = 1.9 rad/s × (top/1440)^0.5 × (0.82 + 0.035·handling)`;\n- `grip = 5.5/s × (top/1440)^0.5 × (0.82 + 0.035·handling)` (how fast the slide is caught);\n- `gripMax = 640 u/s² × (top/1440)^1.5 × (0.82 + 0.035·handling)`: the most lateral acceleration the hover field gives\n  (40 m/s² at SPARK). This cap is what makes speed, lines and airbrakes matter;\n- `dmgMul = 1.35 − 0.06·shield`;\n- `mass = 0.8 + 0.05·shield`.\n\nAll of them are also multiplied by the Tune sliders.\n\n**The step** (1/120 s, in this order, for each craft in grid order):\n\n1. **Controls in.** From the human mapping (§3.9), the AI, the replay, the autopilot or the bot. Keyboard steering\n   ramps at 6/s toward ±1 so the keys feel analog. The stick passes straight through.\n2. **Yaw.** `yawTarget = steer·steerRate·(1 − 0.35·v/top) + (brakeR − brakeL)·airbrakeYaw` (with\n   `airbrakeYaw = 1.4 rad/s × (top/1440)^0.5`). `yawRate → yawTarget` at `steerResponse` (9/s). Rotate F about U by\n   `yawRate·dt`. While `stagger > 0` (a hit), steering is ignored and the craft wobbles ±0.4 rad/s.\n3. **Thrust and drag**, along F:\n   - `a = thrust·athr·boostK − cd·v² − coast − brakeDrag`;\n   - `cd = athr / top²` (so held thrust settles at `top`);\n   - while boosting, `top·boostMul` replaces `top` in `cd` and the thrust is ×1.8;\n   - `coast = 40 u/s²` when not thrusting;\n   - `brakeDrag = (brakeL + brakeR)/2 × airbrakeDrag × 0.35·top`;\n   - slope: add `−300 u/s² × F.z` (downhill speeds you up);\n   - pitch: nose-down cuts drag by 3 %·pitch.\n4. **Grip and slide.**\n   - Split V into the along-F part and the lateral part `vl = dot(V, R)`.\n   - The lateral grip available is `gmax = gripMax·(1 + 0.6·max(brakeL, brakeR))`: the airbrake flap works as a\n     rudder, which is why airbrakes are the cornering tool.\n   - Reduce `vl` toward 0 by `min(|vl|·(1 − e^(−grip·dt)), gmax·dt)`. A turn that needs more than `gmax` (`v²/R`)\n     slides outward.\n   - **Slip cap:** if the angle between F and V exceeds `slipMax` (35°), rotate F back to 35° from V. The craft\n     slides, never spins.\n   - **Scrub:** speed `−= scrubK·|vl|·dt` (scrubK 0.35/s). Sliding costs speed.\n   - **Side-shift** (a press; grounded; cooldown 0.6 s): a separate lateral velocity `vShift = ±sideShiftSpeed`\n     (768 u/s) that decays at `shiftDecay` (12/s), outside the grip cap. That gives about 4 m of sideways jump in\n     0.3 s. Thruster puffs.\n5. **Hover / air.** Get the surface at the craft's `(s, u)`.\n   - **Grounded:** surface present and `h < captureH` (64 u).\n     - Spring along N: `aN = k·(Ht − h) − c·vN`, clamped to `[−magnetPull, +900]`, with `k = 220/s²`, `c = 28/s`,\n       `magnetPull = 1800 u/s²` and `Ht = H0 − 4·pitch + bob` (bob is `1.2·sin(2.2 t)`).\n     - Gravity is cancelled while grounded: the anti-gravity field is the source's fiction.\n     - The craft's up vector U slerps to N at 12/s.\n     - At crests the spring cannot pull hard enough, so `h` grows past `captureH` and the craft lifts off by itself.\n       Ramps launch the same way.\n   - **Airborne:** `a = −airGravity·(1 + 0.45·pitch)·Zup` (airGravity 640 u/s² = 40 m/s²). U slerps to the surface\n     normal below (if one is within 200 u) or else to Zup at 2/s. `airT += dt`.\n   - **Landing** (surface present, `h < H0 + 4`, `vN < 0`): impact angle `θ = atan(−vN / v)`.\n     - If `θ > 25°`: energy `−(θ − 25)·0.4·dmgMul`, speed `×(1 − min(0.35, (θ − 15°)/60°))`, and a hard-landing event\n       (shake, sparks, a \"THUD\").\n     - Otherwise a soft landing.\n     - Either way, resolve the barrel roll (step 7).\n   - **Bottoming out:** `h < 5 u` → `h = 5`, `vN = max(vN, 0)`, speed `×0.996` per step, a scrape event.\n6. **Integrate** `V += a·dt`, `P += V·dt`. Then `T.locate` → `s, u, h`.\n7. **Barrel roll.** Triggers only when airborne with `airT > 0.08 s`:\n   - a side-shift press, or\n   - a steer flick (steer crosses ≤ −0.7 then ≥ +0.7, or the reverse, and back, within 0.4 s; detected in\n     `01-input.js`).\n\n   The roll starts with `rollT = 0.45 s` toward rollDir and costs `rollCost` (10) energy. On landing:\n   - a finished roll → boost (`boostMul 1.2`, 1.2 s) + \"BARREL ROLL\" event;\n   - a roll still turning → \"BOTCHED\": speed ×0.75, energy −5, stagger 0.5 s.\n\n   The visual is a full 360° about F. Long jumps allow several rolls, each costing energy.\n8. **Walls** (deck/drop, wall present on that side). `lim = hw − 24 u`. If `|u| > lim`:\n   - push P back by `(|u| − lim)` along ∓R';\n   - normal speed `vn = dot(V, ±R')`; if `vn > 0`, then `V −= ±R'·vn·(1 + wallBounce)` with `wallBounce` 0.35;\n   - tangential scrub: `V −= F·min(v, wallFriction·vn)` with `wallFriction` 0.25;\n   - **yaw nudge:** rotate F toward the track tangent by `min(0.5, 0.6·vn/v)` rad (the craft never grinds nose-first);\n   - damage `wallDamage·clamp((vn − 150)/120, 0, 12)·dmgMul`;\n   - scraping (in contact with `vn ≤ 150`) costs 4 energy/s while `v > 500`;\n   - events `wall` / `scrape`.\n\n   **Open edges:** `|u| > hw + 2 m` with no wall means no surface. The craft falls, and a rescue follows (step 11).\n9. **Pads and pit** (in track space, grounded only):\n   - **Speed pad:** `boostT = min(2.0, max(boostT, padBoostTime))` (0.9 s), `boostMul = padBoost` (1.25). A pad\n     re-arms per craft after 0.5 s.\n   - **Weapon pad:** if no weapon is held, roll one (§3.4); event `pickup`.\n   - **Pit strip:** `energy += pitRecharge·dt` (25/s), a green shimmer FX and a recharge sound loop.\n10. **Energy.** Every damage source goes through `SN.Ship.damage(ship, amount, cause, by)`. It applies `dmgMul`.\n    `shieldT > 0` (bulwark) or god mode blocks it. Below 25 % a warning plays. At 0 the craft is eliminated (§3.3\n    decides between DNF and respawn).\n11. **Rescue.** Triggered by:\n    - a fall below the kill height (gap: `zLip − 40 m`; otherwise surface − 60 m);\n    - leaving an open edge: rescue once the craft is 6 m below the deck, or after 1 s. There is no terrain\n      collision, so the fall must end before it would visibly pass through the ground. The terrain carve keeps the\n      ground ≥ 10 m below every open edge (§3.7) so the drop reads as a fall;\n    - being stuck (`v < 50 u/s` for 3 s while thrusting, outside the countdown).\n\n    The rescue drone lifts the craft back on the centre line at `s_lastGood + 20 m` (the last grounded `s` with\n    `|u| < hw`), in 2.5 s with the craft frozen. Energy −10, speed 0, event `rescue`. In OVERCLOCK the rescue costs 20\n    energy.\n12. **Ship–ship collisions** (`27-collide.js`, after all craft move, pairs in index order): sphere pairs. The craft are\n    separated along the contact normal in inverse proportion to mass. Impulse\n    `j = −(1 + 0.3)·vn / (1/m1 + 1/m2)`. Damage `0.004·|vn|` each. A `bump` event fires above 120 u/s. Ghost craft\n    (hub, dev \"ghost AI\") skip this.\n13. **Launch boost** (countdown): holding thrust raises the revs at 0.6/s; releasing drops them at 0.8/s.\n    - At GO, revs in 0.72–0.88 → \"PERFECT START\" boost (1.0 s, ×1.25).\n    - Revs above 0.95 → \"STALL\" (no thrust for 0.5 s).\n    - The HUD shows a rev bar during the countdown.\n\n**Feel targets (checked by the physics tests; tune with the sliders until they hold):**\n- 0 → 90 % of top in 2.2–3.0 s (it depends on the THRUST stat: 2.68 s at THRUST 5 by the formula).\n- Thrust-only top speed within ±2 % of `top`.\n- Lateral grip caps out at `gripMax`. These figures were checked with a 2D model of this exact step during planning\n  (KESTREL stats, SPARK, top 328 km/h):\n  - full lock with no airbrake, from top speed: path radius 120–150 m over the first second, the nose at the 35° slip\n    cap, about 255 km/h after 1.4 s, a slide that settles near 180 km/h if held;\n  - full lock with the inside airbrake fully on: radius 45–60 m, about 160 km/h after 1.4 s (the hairpin tool);\n  - steady cornering on a 65 m line: about 188 km/h without airbrakes, about 238 km/h with exactly the inside\n    airbrake the corner needs.\n\n  The Solenne lighthouse hairpin is taken without a wall touch by the AI at skill 1.\n- Side-shift moves the craft about 4 m sideways (768 u/s decaying at 12/s gives 4.2 m).\n- Every jump in §4.3 behaves as App. C says, at each class's top speed (gap: clears at ≥ 75 m/s, falls short below\n  60 m/s).\n- At 3,000 u/s nothing tunnels through a wall or the surface.\n\n**Visual-only motion** (computed in `62-shipkit.js` from the state, never fed back):\n- roll = bank + `clamp(yawRate·0.28, ±0.5)` + barrel roll angle;\n- pitch = slope + `pitch·7°` + bob;\n- airbrake flaps open by `brake·60°`;\n- engine glow follows thrust;\n- the boost flame lengthens with `boostT`;\n- the shield shell flashes on a hit;\n- below 25 % energy, damage smoke and sparks.\n\n### 3.3 Race director and modes (`40-race.js`)\n\n**Lifecycle** (`race.state`):\n\n1. `intro`: a 6 s flyover by the TV director (§3.6). The track card shows name, place, length, laps, class. ✕, Enter\n   or a click skips it.\n2. `grid`: 1.5 s, a chase cam on the player.\n3. `countdown`: 3 s with lights (3-2-1-GO) on the start gantry and the HUD, the launch revs and the announcer.\n4. `racing`.\n5. `finished`: the player crossed the line, or was eliminated.\n   - The player becomes a ghost-cam spectator (TV director) while the others finish.\n   - After 8 s, or when every craft is done, unfinished craft get an estimated time\n     (`t + (remaining distance / their average speed)`) and the results are sealed.\n6. `results`: go to the `results` scene.\n\n**Laps and sectors.** A lap counts when the craft crosses `s = 0` forward after passing sectors 1…7 in order. Lap\ntime, best lap and the final lap's announcer/music layer come from it. **Wrong way:** `dot(F, trackF) < −0.2` and\n`v > 300 u/s` for 1.2 s → a HUD warning plus an announcer line.\n\n**Positions:** sorted by `finished` time, then by progress `p`, descending. The order is recomputed every step, with\na \"position changed\" event for the HUD arrows.\n\n**Elimination:** at energy 0 the craft explodes. In RACE/SEASON it is **DNF** (results show \"ELIMINATED\"). In\nSNIPEOUT, ACADEMY and hub sessions it **respawns** 3 s later at its own `s` on the centre line, with 100 % energy and\n2 s of invulnerability (blinking).\n\n**Modes (`rules` objects, one file section each):**\n\n| Mode | Field | Weapons | Rules / win | Medals |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| QUICK RACE | 8 craft (player + 7 AI) | on | laps 1–5 (default 3); place = result | gold 1st, silver 2nd, bronze 3rd |\n| TIME TRIAL | solo | off (pads dark) | 3 laps; ghost of your best run (§3.13) | per track/class times, measured (§4.2) |\n| HOT LAP | solo, flying start (spawn 300 m before the line at 80 % top) | off | unlimited laps; the best lap counts; End run in the pause menu (or 10 laps) | per track/class lap times |\n| SNIPEOUT | 8 craft | on, offensive-weighted table, no AUTOPILOT | +1 per hit landed, +3 per elimination, +1 bonus for a RAILSHOT elimination (\"SNIPED\"); respawns; first to target (10 or 12) or most after 5 min | 1st/2nd/3rd |\n| OVERCLOCK | solo, neon skin | off; speed pads off | automatic thrust; zone n every 12 s: `top = SPARK·(0.75 + 0.06·n)`; walls ×1.5 damage; +5 energy per zone cleared; ends at 0 energy | bronze zone 10, silver 20, gold 30, \"OVERCLOCKED\" 40 |\n| ACADEMY | solo (+ drones) | scripted | 11 drills (§4.5), each retried until passed | gold when every drill passed first time |\n| VERSUS | 2 humans + 6 AI, split screen | on | race or snipeout, as above | per player |\n| SEASON event | as its mode | as its mode | the event's target | the event's medal rule |\n| GRAND PRIX | 8 craft × 4 races | on | points 10-8-6-5-4-3-2-1; DNF 0; ties by best finish | champion = gold, 2nd = silver, 3rd = bronze |\n| HUB SESSION | each copy: own craft + 7 AI; other humans as ghosts | on | 3 laps FLARE on a seeded track; elimination respawns; `AIHub.result({ time })` | the hub's standings |\n\n**Results data** (`race.results()`): place, pilot, team, time or gap, best lap, points (GP/SNIPEOUT), DNF, medal for\nthe player, new records, and unlocks triggered (season).\n\n### 3.4 Weapons and pickups (`30-weapons.js`, `06-data-weapons.js`)\n\nProjectiles live in **track space**: `s, u, h` and `vs, vu`. They follow the track through curves, the way the\nsource's weapons hug it. Each step they advance and wrap with `s`. They hit a craft when `|Δs| < 40 u`, `|Δu| < 34 u`\nand `|Δh| < 40 u`. They hit a wall at `|u| > hw` (they explode). In gaps they fly straight on and expire. Every hit\ngoes through `SN.Ship.damage` and emits `hit`. The 3D FX are in `68-fx.js`.\n\n| Weapon (icon colour) | Fire | Behaviour | Damage / effect | Absorb |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **SWARM** (red) | tap | 3 rockets, lateral spread −1.5/0/+1.5 m growing at 120 u/s, speed `v_ship + 2400`, life 1.4 s | 10 each, jolt (speed ×0.9, stagger 0.2 s) | +16 |\n| **SEEKER** (orange) | lock: hold the target ahead in a 25° cone within 3000 u for 0.6 s (\"LOCKED\" tone), then press | homing missile, speed `v + 2000`, steers u toward the target at 900 u/s, `s` speed matched to catch up; unlocked it flies straight | 24, spin-out stagger 0.5 s | +22 |\n| **MINEFIELD** (magenta) | tap | drops 5 mines behind at 0.12 s intervals (`u` at drop, `s − 60 u`); armed after 0.3 s; live 30 s; trigger radius 40 u | 12 each, jolt | +18 |\n| **CANNON** (yellow) | hold | 24 bolts at 12/s, speed `v + 4200`, ±0.5 m jitter, aim assist toward a target within ±1.5 m | 2.5 per bolt | +14 |\n| **RAILSHOT** (white/cyan): the *snipe* | hold to charge 0.8 s (ring on the HUD), release to fire | hitscan along the track ahead to 4000 u. It hits the first craft within ±32 u of the aim line `u_aim(Δs) = u + Δs·tan(heading vs track)` (aim assist: ±16 u extra if charged fully). A beam is drawn in 3D | 34, big jolt; an elimination by RAILSHOT is a \"SNIPED!\" | +28 |\n| **TREMOR** (green) | tap | a wave rolls forward along the surface from the user, full width, at `v + 1800` for 1.3 s. It hits each **grounded** craft it passes (airborne craft dodge it) | 26, pops the craft up 3 m, stagger 0.4 s | +30 |\n| **BULWARK** (blue) | tap | invulnerable for 4 s (walls too); no pickups meanwhile | blocks everything | +12 |\n| **AUTOPILOT** (teal) | tap | the AI drives for 5 s (skill 1.0); the HUD counts it down; ends early after a rescue | — | +10 |\n| **NITRO** (amber) | tap | boost 2.2 s, `boostMul 1.35`, thrust ×2 | — | +10 |\n| **SIPHON** (lime) | tap: it latches onto the nearest craft ahead by itself | beam to the nearest craft ahead within 1500 u (along the track) for 3 s; breaks beyond 1900 u | drains 9/s from the target into you | +20 |\n\n- **Absorb** (○ / Shift / right click): consumes the weapon and adds its absorb value × the `absorbMul` slider.\n- **One weapon at a time.** A pad gives nothing while a weapon is held, or while BULWARK or AUTOPILOT runs.\n- **Pickup roll:** weighted by position. Pick the table by `pos ∈ {1,2}` front, `{3..5}` mid, `{6..8}` back, then\n  apply `pickupLuck` (0 = uniform, 1 = table, 2 = table squared).\n\n  | | SWARM | SEEKER | MINE | CANNON | RAIL | TREMOR | BULWARK | AUTO | NITRO | SIPHON |\n  | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n  | front | 2 | 1 | 4 | 3 | 1 | 0 | 3 | 0 | 1 | 1 |\n  | mid | 3 | 3 | 2 | 2 | 2 | 1 | 2 | 1 | 2 | 2 |\n  | back | 2 | 3 | 1 | 1 | 2 | 3 | 1 | 3 | 3 | 2 |\n  | snipeout | 3 | 3 | 2 | 3 | 3 | 2 | 2 | 0 | 1 | 2 |\n\n  The HUD plays a 0.5 s slot-machine spin, then the announcer says the name. Rolls use `race.rng('pickup')`.\n- **Warnings for the target:** a seeker lock beeps at the target and shows \"LOCK\" with an arrow at the bottom centre.\n  A railshot charging aimed at you shows a thin red line.\n\n### 3.5 AI pilots (`35-ai.js`)\n\nEach AI craft produces `ShipControls` every step from the track's line and speed arrays and the race state. The same\nfunction drives AUTOPILOT, the attract mode, the player bot in tests, and the medal calibration.\n\n1. **Look-ahead target.** `sL = s + 0.55 s·v + 300 u`. Target point `Q = C(sL) + R'(sL)·uTarget(sL)`.\n   - `uTarget` = racing line `T.line` + avoidance offset + pad bias + pit bias.\n   - Heading error `e` = the signed angle from F to `(Q − P)` projected on the surface plane.\n   - `steer = clamp(2.2·e + 0.25·ė, −1, 1)`, plus seeded noise ±(0.05·(1 − skill)).\n2. **Speed.** `vT = T.vline(s + 0.4·v)·skillK` (skillK = 0.86 + 0.14·skill, also scaling `alat`).\n   - thrust if `v < vT·1.01`;\n   - both airbrakes if `v > vT·1.05`;\n   - the inside airbrake (the side of the turn) at `clamp((v²·|κL| − gripMax) / (0.6·gripMax), 0, 1)`, which is\n     exactly the extra grip the corner needs, plus `clamp((|e| − 0.12)/0.28, 0, 1)` when the heading error is large;\n   - pitch: nose-down on descents steeper than 4 %, nose-up on crests (vertical curvature) and over gaps when short of\n     the landing.\n3. **Avoidance and overtaking.** A craft ahead within 900 u with `|Δu| < 70 u` and closing → shift `uTarget` by\n   ±110 u toward the wider side (blend 0.6 s). It returns to the line after passing. Mines seen ahead (within 1200 u)\n   push `uTarget` away by 80 u. A side-shift dodges incoming weapons when skill > 0.7 (reaction 0.25 s).\n4. **Pads.** A speed pad within 1500 u ahead and within 120 u of the line → bias `uTarget` onto it (skill-weighted).\n   Weapon pads likewise when unarmed. Pit: if energy < 30 % and the pit is ahead within 2500 u → the pit line.\n5. **Weapons (per weapon):**\n   - SWARM, CANNON: a target ahead within 1800 u and `|Δu| < 60 u`.\n   - SEEKER: fire when locked.\n   - RAILSHOT: charge when a target is within 3500 u and `|Δu_aim| < 40 u`; release at full charge.\n   - MINEFIELD: a craft behind within 1200 u, or simply in the last 30 % of a lap when leading.\n   - TREMOR: ≥ 2 craft within 2500 u ahead.\n   - BULWARK: a lock warning, or energy < 35 % in traffic.\n   - AUTOPILOT: in a technical section (`|κ|` high) or with energy < 40 %.\n   - NITRO: on a straight (`|κL| < 1/600 m` for the next 400 m).\n   - SIPHON: a target ahead within 1400 u and own energy < 85.\n   - Absorb instead when energy < 30 % and the weapon is defensive or useless at that moment.\n   - Each pilot's `aggression` (0.4–1.3) scales reaction thresholds and hold times.\n6. **Jumps.** Hold `v ≥ vJump` on gap approaches. Barrel roll when the predicted airtime is > 0.6 s, energy > 50 %\n   and skill > 0.6, at chance `0.5·aggression` (attract: always).\n7. **Mistakes.** For each corner (κ peak), a chance `(1 − skill)·0.15` to brake late by 0.25 s (it may scrape a wall).\n8. **Rubber band** (Quick Race, Season, Versus; never Time Trial/Hot Lap/Overclock):\n   `top ×= 1 + rb·clamp((p_player − p_ai)/32000, −1, 1)·0.04`, with rb from the difficulty (Easy 1.5, Normal 1.0,\n   Hard 0.3) times the `aiRubberBand` slider.\n9. **Difficulty** (Settings → Difficulty):\n\n   | | AI skill | aggression | rubber band |\n   | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n   | Easy | 0.86 | ×0.6 | 1.5 |\n   | Normal | 0.93 | ×1.0 | 1.0 |\n   | Hard | 0.99 | ×1.3 | 0.3 |\n\n   Each pilot has an offset (§4.1). NULL//SET pilots get +0.02.\n10. **Attract cheats.** The AI may cheat freely in attract (TASK.md): infinite energy, pickups forced in rotation so\n    all 10 weapons appear, a barrel roll on every jump, aggression 1.5.\n\n### 3.6 Cameras and the TV director (`60-render.js`)\n\nThe World3D camera runs in **`'fixed'`** mode. We compute a pose `{ x, y, z, yaw, pitch, roll, fov }` (engine units,\nradians; `pitch < 0` looks down) every step into `camera.fixed`. In `onDraw` we **interpolate** between the last two\nstep poses with `game.alpha` and write `world.camera.pose` (the header allows \"a last touch to camera.pose\"). Craft\nmeshes are interpolated the same way (`prev` → current). Set `camera.target = { x, y, z }` to the player craft so the\nsun's shadow box follows it.\n\n| Camera | Pose |\n| --- | --- |\n| **Chase** (default) | eye = `P − Fs·d + Us·hgt`, where `d = camDistance·(1 + 0.15·v/top)` (150 u) and `hgt = camHeight` (46 u). Look at `P + F·120 + U·12`. `Fs`, `Us` are F and U smoothed by slerp at `camLag` (8/s), so the camera swings, never cuts corners. `Us` blends from Zup toward the craft's U at 0.6, so the horizon tilts with the banks. `fov = camFov + camFovBoost·(v/top)²` (72° + 16°) + 6° while boosting. Shake from `game.shake` (impacts, rail hits, landings) |\n| **Far chase** | d ×1.5, hgt ×1.6, fov −6° |\n| **Cockpit** | eye = `P + F·20 + U·14`, look along F, full craft roll, fov 84° + boost. The craft mesh is hidden except a nose/canopy-rim \"dash\" mesh |\n| **Look back** (held) | the chase eye mirrored in front of the craft looking back (`P + F·d + Us·hgt` → P) |\n| **Free fly** (dev) | WASD/stick fly, Q/E or triggers up/down, mouse/right stick turn |\n| **Podium / hangar orbit** | an orbit around a point (menus, results podium) |\n\nRoll sign: verify with a screenshot on Karakum's spiral, a right-hand banked turn. The horizon must tilt the way the\ntrack does. If it is inverted, negate the roll in one place (`SN.cam.rollSign`).\n\n**TV director** (intro flyover, attract, replay, spectating, podium intro):\n- **Camera spots** are built at load every ~200 m. Each is `C(s) + R'·side·(hw + 15…30 m) + Zup·(6…20 m)`, on the\n  outside of curves, alternating sides on straights. Skip a spot if the terrain (`world.ground`) is above it, or if it\n  is inside another track section (`T.query`). Tunnel spots go 2 m under the ceiling, 4 m from the wall. Overpass\n  spots look up from the lower deck. Each spot stores `s`.\n- **Shots:**\n  - `trackside`: fixed eye, looking at the target, with the FOV narrowing (40→20°) as the target nears;\n  - `heli`: 40 m up, 60 m back, following;\n  - `chase`;\n  - `nose`;\n  - `low`: 1 m above the surface ahead, looking back at the target;\n  - `flyby`: along the line 30 m ahead of the target, looking back.\n- **Logic:**\n  - target = the player (spectate/replay) or the most interesting craft (attract: leader, a close fight within 300 u,\n    a weapon fired in the last 2 s, a jump);\n  - pick the spot 150–900 u ahead of the target with a clear line (raycast against the track only), hold 2.5–6 s, and\n    cut when the target passes the spot by 400 u;\n  - every third cut is heli, chase, nose or low;\n  - events cut early: an elimination, a railshot or a jump launch;\n  - never cut twice within 1.2 s.\n- **Intro flyover:** 6 s along the line from `s = −900 m` to the grid at 2.5× the target speed, then a 1 s whip onto\n  the grid.","numLines":400,"startLine":380,"totalLines":2083}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Mm7CPEKDon1QHwALt8C8da","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
