{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015zZ1M9noWu7MayY3QCkbfk","type":"tool_result","content":"780\t\n781\t### 3.7 Rendering (`60-render.js`, `62-shipkit.js`, `64-trackmesh.js`, `66-scenery.js`, `68-fx.js`)\n782\t\n783\t**Worlds.** `World3D.init(game)` runs once (boot). Then:\n784\t- **Hangar world**, made at boot. A small `level` (text rows):\n785\t  - a 24 × 16 tile hall: floor `{ floor: 0 }`, a turntable `{ mark: 'turntable' }` and a podium of three raised floors\n786\t    (`{ floor: 24 }` 1st, `{ floor: 16 }` 2nd, `{ floor: 8 }` 3rd, marks `p1 p2 p3`);\n787\t  - no torch tiles (`torchLights: 0`); our own lights: 3 coloured `world.light`s plus team-coloured neon strips\n788\t    (our meshes);\n789\t  - camera `'fixed'`, `fog: false`.\n790\t\n791\t  It is used by the menus, team select (the craft on the turntable), results/podium (pilots as rig **cards** via\n792\t  `world.hero({ rig })` posed `cheer` / `wave` / `hips`) and the ending.\n793\t- **Track world**, one per track, made by the `loading` scene. At most one is alive besides the hangar: dispose the\n794\t  previous with `world.dispose()`. Boot makes PORT SOLENNE's, so the title and attract start at once.\n795\t\n796\t```js\n797\tnew E.World3D(game, {\n798\t  terrain: { size: 65536 /* 4 km */, height: theme.height, color: theme.color, far: 26000, cell: 64, rock: theme.rock, bottom: -3000 },\n799\t  sky: theme.sky, fog: theme.fog, ambient: theme.ambient, sun: Object.assign({ shadow: true, area: 900 }, theme.sun),\n800\t  torchLights: 0, lights: 4, glowLights: 8, shadows: game.settings.shadows3d !== false,\n801\t  filter: { look: game.settings.filter3d || 'clean', bloom: game.settings.bloom !== false },\n802\t  camera: { mode: 'fixed', far: 26000, near: 4 }, particleGround: (x, y, z) => track.groundBelow(x, y, z),\n803\t  onDraw: (w, r) => SN.render.onDraw(w, r)\n804\t});\n805\t```\n806\t\n807\t**Terrain carving.** `theme.height(x, y)` = the theme's natural height, combined with a **corridor grid** (cell 16 m,\n808\tbuilt from the slices at load):\n809\t- near the track: `min(natural, deckZ − clearance(d))`, where `clearance` grows from 3 m at the edge to 0 at 60 m, so\n810\t  the ground falls away under elevated decks and meets the track at grade;\n811\t- under tunnel slices: `max(natural, ceilZ + 4 m)`, so the rock covers the tunnel;\n812\t- portal frames hide the seams.\n813\t\n814\tKeep `height()` fast: it is a few grid lookups and noise (`E.noise2`).\n815\t\n816\t**Materials** (make them all when the world is made, never mid-race):\n817\t- `MeshLambertNodeMaterial({ vertexColors: true })` for the track surface, walls and scenery;\n818\t- `MeshBasicNodeMaterial` for emissive neon, pads, engine glow and beams. They are bright, so the bloom catches them.\n819\t  Set `fog: false` on the overclock skin;\n820\t- `MeshToonNodeMaterial` for the craft hulls;\n821\t- transparent additive materials for the shield shells, ghosts and beams.\n822\t\n823\tTextures are canvases drawn pixel by pixel at 64–256 px (`NearestFilter`, the engine's native crisp look): track\n824\tpanels, lane dashes, chevrons, sponsor boards, team logos, window grids. **Pads and painted markings** use\n825\t`polygonOffset` (factor −2, units −2) and sit 1 u above the surface. That avoids z-fighting at distance.\n826\t\n827\t**Track meshes** (`64-trackmesh.js`), built in chunks of 40 slices (80 m) for frustum culling:\n828\t- **Surface:** 6 lateral strips. Vertex colours: dark graphite panels `#22252c`/`#2a2e36` alternating every 8 m,\n829\t  bright edge lines, centre dashes, a tint per theme. The grid boxes and the start/finish chequer are painted near\n830\t  `s = 0`.\n831\t- **Walls:** 1.6 m barrier panels with a glowing top strip in the theme's neon (`#29c8e8` coast, `#ffb347` desert,\n832\t  `#ff3ab4` city, `#7af0ff` arctic). On the outside of curves, **directional chevrons** (emissive arrows pointing the\n833\t  way of the turn) every 6 m. Open edges have no wall but a dashed hazard line on the edge.\n834\t- **Underside and supports:**\n835\t  - the deck's underside and thickness (1.2 m), so the deck reads as a bridge;\n836\t  - pylons every 40 m where the deck is more than 4 m above the terrain, at the deck edges; skipped where they would\n837\t    stand in another section's driving envelope;\n838\t  - overpass decks get piers outside the lower deck's walls.\n839\t- **Tunnels:** a 10-segment arch to 12 m, ribs every 12 m, emissive light strips along both upper sides, portal\n840\t  facades by style (stone arches, neon frames, ice). Three world lights follow the player through tunnels (warm,\n841\t  cool, theme).\n842\t- **Pads:**\n843\t  - speed pad: an 8 × 6 m quad with 3 chevrons whose colours cycle front to back at 6 Hz (the pad meshes' colour\n844\t    attribute rewritten each frame, `needsUpdate`), cyan `#3ad8ff`;\n845\t  - weapon pad: a 6 × 6 m amber `#ffb000` quad with a pulsing triangle sigil and a light post at the edge;\n846\t  - pit strip: green `#3aff8a` with \"+\" marks and a gantry sign PIT.\n847\t- **Gantries:** the start/finish gantry has the 3-light start lights (red → green), a timing board (canvas texture\n848\t  showing the race time) and team flags. Sponsor gantries go every ~350 m over the track. Each track also has a\n849\t  landmark arch.\n850\t- **Drop and gap edges:** the lip face (a vertical face), the far-edge face, and a hazard stripe painted on the lip.\n851\t- **Overclock skin:** a **separate world** that the `loading` scene builds for OVERCLOCK runs (and the attract's\n852\t  overclock segment), so no fog or sky changes are needed at runtime:\n853\t  - theme `overclock`: black sky, black fog close in (near 2400 u, far 9600 u), flat black terrain at −400 m, no\n854\t    scenery;\n855\t  - the same track chunks built with the overclock materials: a black surface with an emissive grid (lines every 4 m)\n856\t    and neon wall lines;\n857\t  - each zone changes only the materials' colour, `hsl(zone·37°, 100%, 60%)` (no new materials, so no shader builds);\n858\t  - sky colour pulses on the beat; bloom up.\n859\t\n860\t**Craft (`62-shipkit.js`)**, built from code as BufferGeometry, flat-shaded, 200–600 triangles each:\n861\t- **Hull:** lofted through 6 cross-sections (an octagon scaled per section, from the needle nose to the tail), with\n862\t  per-design profiles;\n863\t- **canopy:** dark glossy, with an emissive rim;\n864\t- **wings:** flat wedges, swept, with team-coloured tips;\n865\t- **fins:** 0–2;\n866\t- **engine pods:** 1–3, cylinders with emissive inner discs (team engine colour);\n867\t- **airbrake flaps:** 2 hinged boxes at the rear sides (rotate);\n868\t- **livery** by vertex colour per part (primary, secondary, accent stripe), the race number, and the team logo\n869\t  (a 32 px canvas decal on the top);\n870\t- **exhaust trail:** a ribbon of the last 0.35 s of tail positions, alpha fading, team colour;\n871\t- **boost flame:** a cone that grows;\n872\t- **shield shell:** an ellipsoid at opacity 0 that flashes to 0.6 on a hit, bulwark-blue for BULWARK;\n873\t- **explosion:** 8 hull shards flying ballistically for 1.5 s, plus `particles.explosion` and a light flash;\n874\t- **rescue drone:** a 4-rotor drone mesh with a tractor beam cone.\n875\t\n876\tThe six designs are in §4.1. **Ghosts** (hub players, time-trial ghost) use the same mesh in a transparent additive\n877\tmaterial (opacity 0.35) tinted with the seat or ghost colour, plus a name tag.\n878\t\n879\t**Effects (`68-fx.js`)**:\n880\t- wall sparks via `game.particles.sparks` at the contact point;\n881\t- dust and spray on landings (`dust`; water spray at Solenne and Borealis);\n882\t- weapon visuals: rocket meshes with smoke trails, the seeker's spiral trail, mines (spinning spheres, blinking red),\n883\t  cannon tracers, the rail beam (a 0.6 m white-cyan cylinder fading over 0.4 s, plus a screen flash), the tremor wave\n884\t  (a glowing band of quads riding the surface), the bulwark hex bubble, the autopilot ring, nitro flames, the siphon\n885\t  zigzag beam;\n886\t- **speed lines** in the HUD (screen-space streaks from the centre, density ∝ `(v/top)²`, more while boosting);\n887\t- weather: Borealis snow (instanced flakes near the camera), Karakum heat-haze dust, Meridian light rain (streak\n888\t  particles), Solenne sea spray.\n889\t\n890\t**Split screen.** `game.splitScreen(2, { layout: 'rows' })` with `world.addCamera({ mode: 'fixed', far: 26000 })`.\n891\tEach viewport's `camera.fixed` is set from its own player's chase or cockpit cam. World3D turns filters off while\n892\tsplit, which is expected.\n893\t\n894\t**Warm-up.** In `loading`, after everything is built, do one hidden frame with every pooled mesh visible in front of\n895\tthe camera (each weapon FX, both skins, ghosts), call `world.prepare()`, then hide them. No shader stalls mid-race.\n896\t\n897\t### 3.8 HUD (`70-hud.js`): pixel art at game resolution, anchored to `r.W × r.H`\n898\t\n899\tLayout at 427 × 240 (16:9; everything is anchored and scales with `HUD size`):\n900\t- **Top left:** POSITION as a big number (`E.font.title`, scale 4) plus `/8` small. LAP `2/3` below it. In SNIPEOUT\n901\t  this is the points table (top 4) instead.\n902\t- **Top centre:** the race time `1:23.45`. On a lap: the lap time with ±delta vs best (green/red), held 3 s.\n903\t  \"FINAL LAP\" banner.\n904\t- **Top right:** the minimap (72 px), craft as team-coloured dots, the player blinking, ghosts hollow.\n905\t- **Bottom left:** the weapon slot. A 24 × 24 pixel icon per weapon (§4.4), its name, and prompts `□ FIRE  ○ ABSORB`\n906\t  drawn with the glyph icons (§3.9). The pickup roll spin. The railshot charge ring. The autopilot/bulwark countdown.\n907\t- **Bottom right:**\n908\t  - speed: a segmented bar of 24 segments, cyan → white → magenta in boost, with km/h at scale 2;\n909\t  - energy: 20 segments, green > 50 %, yellow > 25 %, red and blinking below; it shakes on damage; \"PIT\" hint when\n910\t    low;\n911\t  - the boost indicator.\n912\t- **Centre:**\n913\t  - the countdown digits (scale 6, pop tween);\n914\t  - the rev bar during the countdown;\n915\t  - **callouts:** weapon names, PERFECT START, BARREL ROLL, SNIPED!, ELIMINATED, WRONG WAY, PERFECT LAP, NEW RECORD,\n916\t    ZONE n. They pop with scale and alpha, last 1.2 s, and stack at most 2;\n917\t  - the lock reticle on the projected target (`world.project`), a rotating bracket that turns red when locked;\n918\t  - the incoming-lock arrow at the bottom centre.\n919\t- **Name tags:** pilot name and position above craft within 2500 u (projected), fading with distance.\n920\t- **Radio box:** a small portrait (`rig.drawPortrait`, 28 px) and a subtitle line at the top left under the position\n921\t  for pilot banter and the announcer (§3.10).\n922\t- **Split screen:** per viewport a compact HUD (position, lap, speed, energy, weapon) via `r.viewport`. Countdown and\n923\t  results go over the whole screen in `scene.hud(r)`.\n924\t- **Overclock:** ZONE number (scale 4), the zone progress bar (12 s), speed, energy. No position or lap.\n925\t- **Hub session:** the ghost players' names and live positions.\n926\t- The HUD stays clear of `game.cornerArea()` when the corner shows (it is hidden in play).\n927\t\n928\t### 3.9 Front-end, UI and UX: 10-foot and controller-first (`75-ui.js`, `55-glyphs.js`, `01-input.js`)\n929\t\n930\t**Rules for every screen** (TASK.md: a TV at 10 feet, no dense web-style data screens):\n931\t- At most 6 focusable items per screen.\n932\t- Labels at font scale ≥ 2 (14 px of 240). Titles at scale 3–4. Body text at scale 2, at most 3 lines.\n933\t- One focus at a time. It is drawn as a thick animated chevron frame plus a colour shift plus a 1 px \"scanline\"\n934\t  shimmer. It is never shown by colour alone (TASK and engine rule).\n935\t- Navigation:\n936\t  - d-pad, stick or arrows (WASD too in menus) move the focus, with `input.repeat` when held;\n937\t  - ✕, Enter or Space confirms; ○, Esc or Backspace goes back;\n938\t  - L1/R1, Q/E or the mouse wheel switch tabs or pages;\n939\t  - **mouse hover moves the focus**, a left click activates, and every screen has a clickable BACK chip at the bottom\n940\t    left.\n941\t- **A prompt bar** at the bottom of every screen shows the actions for the **last device used**\n942\t  (`input.lastDevice`):\n943\t  - gamepad: glyph icons;\n944\t  - keyboard: keycaps;\n945\t  - mouse: mouse icons (left click SELECT, BACK chip).\n946\t\n947\t  It switches the moment another device is touched.\n948\t- **Glyph icons (`55-glyphs.js`):**\n949\t  - **PlayStation** (the default): ✕ blue `#7cb2e8`, ○ red `#ff6b6b`, □ pink `#ff79c6`, △ green `#3fd8a6`, drawn in\n950\t    dark discs of 11 px; L1/R1/L2/R2 as rounded tabs with text; Options and Create as pill icons; the d-pad and stick\n951\t    as small icons.\n952\t  - **Xbox** (Settings → Button symbols): A green, B red, X blue, Y yellow; LB/RB/LT/RT; Menu and View.\n953\t  - **Keyboard:** keycaps sized to the label from `input.label(action, 'keyboard')`.\n954\t  - **Mouse:** a mouse with the left or right button lit.\n955\t\n956\t  `SN.glyph.draw(g, action, x, y, { device })` returns the width drawn. **Never hard-code key names.** Always go\n957\t  through `input.label` and the actual bindings (rebinding works).\n958\t- Animations: menu tiles slide in with `game.tween` (0.18 s, `outBack`), focus chevrons pulse, background light\n959\t  streaks drift, and screen changes use the engine's `'wipe'` fade (0.25 s).\n960\t\n961\t**Input mapping (`01-input.js`).** The game's preset, in this order (the order matters for the engine's half-keyboard\n962\tsplit, §3.16):\n963\t\n964\t```js\n965\tSN.INPUT = {\n966\t  up: ['KeyW', 'ArrowUp', 'Pad12'], down: ['KeyS', 'ArrowDown', 'Pad13'], left: ['KeyA', 'ArrowLeft', 'Pad14'], right: ['KeyD', 'ArrowRight', 'Pad15'],\n967\t  start: ['Enter', 'Pad9'], pause: ['Escape', 'KeyP', 'Pad9'], confirm: ['Enter', 'Space', 'Pad0'], cancel: ['Escape', 'Backspace', 'Pad1'],\n968\t  thrust: ['KeyW', 'Pad0'], fire: ['Space', 'Mouse0', 'Pad2'], absorb: ['ShiftLeft', 'Mouse2', 'Pad1'],\n969\t  brakeL: ['KeyQ', 'Pad6'], brakeR: ['KeyE', 'Pad7'], camera: ['KeyC', 'Pad3'], shiftL: ['KeyZ', 'Pad4'], shiftR: ['KeyX', 'Pad5'],\n970\t  brake: ['KeyS'], lookBack: ['KeyB', 'Pad11']\n971\t};\n972\t```\n973\t\n974\t- In a race, **steer and pitch are not read from up/down/left/right as actions**:\n975\t  - steer = `input.padMove[0]` (analog) + digital A/D/←/→/d-pad (ramped);\n976\t  - pitch = `−input.padMove[1]` + ↑/↓/d-pad (stick up = nose down).\n977\t\n978\t  W and S are therefore only thrust and brake in a race, while still moving the menu focus elsewhere.\n979\t- Airbrakes: `max(input.value('brakeL'), down('brake'))` (analog L2/R2 via engine edit 3).\n980\t- Double-tapping Q or E (within 0.25 s) = side-shift.\n981\t- Mouse buttons fire and absorb in a race.\n982\t- The **virtual pad** `SN.vpad[playerIndex]` (analog values) is merged into the controls. The tests' bots, the\n983\t  autopilot and the attract mode drive craft through it, the same path as a human.\n984\t- The menu's Controls screen names the actions:\n985\t  `menu: { controls: { thrust: 'Thrust', fire: 'Fire weapon', absorb: 'Absorb weapon', brakeL: 'Airbrake left',\n986\t  brakeR: 'Airbrake right', brake: 'Both airbrakes', shiftL: 'Side-shift / roll left', shiftR: 'Side-shift / roll right',\n987\t  camera: 'Camera', lookBack: 'Look back' } }`.\n988\t\n989\t**Screens:**\n990\t\n991\t| Screen | Contents (10-foot: big, few, focused) |\n992\t| --- | --- |\n993\t| **Title** | The Solenne track world in a slow TV-director flyby. The SNIPEOUT HD logo: `E.font.title` scale 5, chrome gradient `['#ffffff', '#9ff4ff', '#29c8e8', '#1a2a4a']`, with a pixel \"HD\" badge and an animated light sweep. The tagline. \"PRESS ✕ / ENTER\" pulsing (glyph of the last device). The version (`E.versionLabel()`) small at the bottom right. Idle for 10 s → attract |\n994\t| **Touch-only notice** | **Detection:** `!matchMedia('(any-pointer: fine)').matches && navigator.maxTouchPoints > 0`, no gamepad connected, and no key pressed yet. Re-check on every key press and on `gamepadconnected`; the notice goes away as soon as one appears. **Shows:** over the title, \"CONTROLLER OR KEYBOARD REQUIRED\" (scale 2, centred, in a panel) and one big **SETTINGS** button (tap → `game.menu('settings')`). `game.input.touchEnabled = false` and no scene declares `touch`, so there are no touch controls anywhere. The attract still starts after 10 s, and a tap returns to this notice |\n995\t| **Main menu** | Hangar world (the player's last craft on the turntable). A vertical list of 6 big tiles: **SEASON · QUICK RACE · CHALLENGES ▸ · VERSUS · ACADEMY · OPTIONS ▸**. CHALLENGES opens TIME TRIAL / HOT LAP / SNIPEOUT / OVERCLOCK; OPTIONS opens SETTINGS / CONTROLS / HOW TO PLAY / RECORDS / ABOUT / DEV MODE. When an autosave exists, the first tile reads **CONTINUE SEASON** (it loads `saves.latest()` and opens the season hub) |\n996\t| **Class select** | 4 tiles in a row: SPARK / FLARE / STORM / SINGULARITY, with a top-speed figure and a lock icon plus the unlock hint (\"WIN THE ROOKIE LICENCE\") |\n997\t| **Track select** | One big card at a time (←/→ or L1/R1 or the wheel or a click on the arrows): the track outline at 150 px drawn with px.line, the name (scale 3), place, length, a difficulty pip row, your best time, and a one-line blurb. The hangar background tints to the theme |\n998\t| **Team and pilot select** | The craft on the turntable (mouse drag rotates it, the right stick rotates). Team name (scale 3) and logo. **4 stat bars** (SPEED, THRUST, HANDLING, SHIELD) as 10-segment bars. One-line bio. The pilot toggle (2 pilots, portraits via `rig.drawPortrait` at 48 px). ←/→ change team |\n999\t| **Laps / confirm** | A summary card (mode, class, track, team, laps), START RACE |\n1000\t| **Loading** | The track name card, a progress bar, and one tip line (\"Absorb a weapon you can't use: shield is worth more than a miss.\") |\n1001\t| **Race** | the HUD (§3.8) |\n1002\t| **Results** | The top 8 as **one row per craft**: position, team colour chip, pilot, time or gap, best-lap star. The player's row is highlighted. Medal and record banners. Actions: CONTINUE · RETRY · REPLAY · MENU. A podium cutaway (hangar world, top 3 pilot cards cheering, confetti) plays first for 4 s when the player is top 3 |\n1003\t| **Season hub** | 4 columns (ROOKIE LICENCE, AUTHORITY NOTICE, STORM WARNING, GRAND PRIX), each with 2–4 event tiles: mode icon, track, medal earned. Locked columns are dimmed with the rule shown. Before an event's first run, a briefing (§3.11) |\n1004\t| **GP standings** | Between races: 8 rows, points, the gap to the leader, NEXT RACE |\n1005\t| **How to play** | 5 pages (L1/R1): CONTROLS (the controller diagram drawn in pixels, or the keyboard map, by device), RACING (pads, pitch, airbrakes, side-shift, rolls), WEAPONS (10 icons with a one-line effect each, two pages), ENERGY (walls, damage, pit lane, absorb, elimination), MODES |\n1006\t| **Records** | per track: best race and best lap per class, pilot name. One track per page |\n1007\t| **About / Credits** | §3.18 |\n1008\t\n1009\t### 3.10 Audio (`50-audio.js`, `10-data-music.js`): all synthesized, no files\n1010\t\n1011\t**Music:** the engine's tracker (`game.audio.music(song, { sync: true })`) with the §2.7 extensions. Songs are data:\n1012\t`{ bpm, steps: 4, tracks: [{ name, wave, vol, lp, uni, det, pan, notes, on }] }`. **Layers** (`audio.layer(name, vol,\n1013\tfade)`) make the music react:\n1014\t- the countdown has pads and bass only;\n1015\t- the drums come in at GO;\n1016\t- the lead comes in on the final lap;\n1017\t- after the race, everything but the pads fades out;\n1018\t- Overclock adds a layer every 2 zones and runs `audio.tempo(min(176, bpm + 3·zone))`.\n1019\t\n1020\tWhen a race starts, a \"now playing\" toast shows (`♪ STACKLINE — NULLPOINT`). Fictional artists, all original.\n1021\t\n1022\t| Song (id) | Where | BPM / key | Character |\n1023\t| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n1024\t| `zero` \"Zero Crossing\" by HALCYON DRIFT | title, menus | 112, D minor | airy pads, a soft arpeggio, a broken beat |\n1025\t| `solenne` \"Riviera Burn\" by SOLSTICE 9 | Port Solenne | 128, A minor | sunny electro-house, four-on-the-floor, offbeat open hats, a pumping saw bass, a pluck lead |\n1026\t| `karakum` \"Sandglass\" by DUNE//CODE | Karakum Spire | 140, E Phrygian | big beat, breakbeat drums (k/s pattern), a distorted acid bass (`lp` env), a call-and-response lead |\n1027\t| `meridian` \"Stackline\" by NULLPOINT | Meridian Stack | 172 (half-time feel), F minor | drum'n'bass breaks, a reese bass (`uni: 3, det: 18` saw, lowpass), stabs |\n1028\t| `borealis` \"Polar Vector\" by AURORA SYSTEMS | Borealis Vault | 136, B minor | trance: rolling 16th bass, a supersaw lead, a long riser every 8 bars |\n1029\t| `overclock` \"Clock Skew\" by THE AUTHORITY | Overclock | 120 → 176 | minimal techno that adds a layer per 2 zones |\n1030\t| stings | lap, final lap, win, podium, eliminated, unlock, medal | — | 1–3 s motifs (`audio.sting`) |\n1031\t\n1032\tExample, the start of `solenne`, to set the format and the bar:\n1033\t\n1034\t```js\n1035\tSN.SONGS.solenne = { bpm: 128, steps: 4, tracks: [\n1036\t  { name: 'kick',  wave: 'drums', vol: .22, notes: 'k . . . k . . . k . . . k . . . | k . . . k . . . k . . . k . k .' },\n1037\t  { name: 'hats',  wave: 'drums', vol: .10, notes: '. . o . . . o . . . o . . . o h | . . o . . . o . . . o . . h o h' },\n1038\t  { name: 'clap',  wave: 'drums', vol: .14, notes: '. . . . p . . . . . . . p . . . | . . . . p . . . . . . . p . p .' },\n1039\t  { name: 'bass',  wave: 'saw', vol: .16, lp: { f: 300, q: 9, env: 1800, dec: .12 },\n1040\t    notes: 'A1 . A2 . A1 A2 . A1 . A2 . A1 G2 . A2! . | F1 . F2 . F1 F2 . F1 . F2 . F1 E2 . F2! .' },\n1041\t  { name: 'pad',   wave: 'saw', vol: .05, uni: 3, det: 14, lp: { f: 1400, q: 1 }, notes: 'A3 - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - | F3 - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -' },\n1042\t  { name: 'lead',  wave: 'pulse', vol: .07, on: false, notes: 'E5 . C5 . A4 . C5 E5 . G5 . E5 . C5 . . | F5 . C5 . A4 . C5 F5 . A5 . F5 . E5 . .' }\n1043\t] };\n1044\t```\n1045\t\n1046\tEach song needs at least 16 bars of material (A/B sections, a breakdown) so that a 3-minute race doesn't drone.\n1047\t\n1048\t**SFX** (`audio.define` voices, plus our own WebAudio graphs on the effects bus where a voice can't do it). These\n1049\tnames are referenced by events (§2.5):\n1050\t\n1051\t| Group | Sounds |\n1052\t| --- | --- |\n1053\t| UI | `ui_move` (short pulse blip), `ui_ok` (two-tone up), `ui_back` (down), `ui_locked` (buzz), `ui_tab` (click) |\n1054\t| Race | `count_beep`, `count_go` (chord), `lap` (chime), `final_lap` (a rising sting), `finish` (fanfare), `wrongway` (siren blip), `pos_up` / `pos_down` (tiny arps) |\n1055\t| Craft | engine hum (continuous, below), `boost_pad` (whoosh plus a pitch sweep), `pickup_roll` (a ticking arp), `weapon_pad` (sparkle), `airbrake` (filtered noise hiss, looped while braking), `sideshift` (puff), `roll` (a whirr), `roll_boost`, `botch`, `land_soft`, `land_hard` (thud plus clank), `wall_hit` (metal bang, pitch by impact), `scrape` (looped band-passed noise, volume by speed), `bump`, `pit_charge` (looped rising tone), `low_shield` (beep every 0.8 s), `explode` (noise boom plus a sub drop), `eliminated`, `respawn`, `rescue` (drone whine) |\n1056\t| Weapons | `swarm_fire`, `seeker_lock` (beeps faster to a solid tone), `seeker_fire`, `mine_drop`, `cannon_fire`, `rail_charge` (a rising whine), `rail_fire` (crack plus a long zap), `tremor` (sub rumble), `bulwark_on/off`, `autopilot_on/off`, `nitro`, `siphon` (a crackling loop), `absorb` (a reverse whoosh with a chime), `hit_light`, `hit_heavy` |\n1057\t\n1058\t**Engine hum.** The four nearest craft each get a persistent graph: saw + detuned square → lowpass → gain →\n1059\tStereoPanner → the effects bus.\n1060\t- `f = 48 + 120·(v/top)` Hz with a thrust wobble.\n1061\t- Cutoff `500 + 2500·(v/top)` (+1500 in boost).\n1062\t- Others: volume by distance (1/(1 + d/800 u)), Doppler pitch `×clamp(1 + vRel/6000, .85, 1.15)`, pan by the screen\n1063\t  x of `world.project`.\n1064\t- The player's hum is louder and centred.\n1065\t- In a split screen: player 1 pans left, player 2 right.\n1066\t- All of it is muted on pause, on `game.audio.muted`, and on the hub's `end`.\n1067\t\n1068\t**Gibberish voice (Animalese/Simlish style), `SN.Voice.say(text, voice)`:**\n1069\t- Every word is turned into syllables seeded by the word's hash, so the same word always sounds the same (\"SEEKER\"\n1070\t  is always \"see-kra\").\n1071\t- Syllable count = `max(1, round(letters / 2.6))`.\n1072\t- Each syllable is a consonant burst (noise, band-passed at 2–5 kHz, 18 ms; picked by the word's letters) followed by\n1073\t  a vowel: a saw at `f0` through two band-pass \"formants\" `[F1, F2]` from a 5-vowel table (a: 800/1200, e: 400/2000,\n1074\t  i: 300/2300, o: 450/800, u: 325/700), lasting `70–110 ms / speed`.\n1075\t- Pitch: per-syllable jitter ±8 %; down 12 % at a full stop, up 18 % at \"?\", +10 % and louder at \"!\".\n1076\t- Breathiness: 15 % noise.\n1077\t- `say()` returns its duration. Subtitles and dialog pages wait on it. Headless, it is computed without sound.\n1078\t\n1079\t| Voice | f0 | Speed | Use |\n1080\t| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n1081\t| ANNOUNCER (race control's \"ORACLE\") | 205 Hz | 0.85 | calm, slightly ring-modulated (×0.4 at 60 Hz) |\n1082\t| pilots | 95–240 Hz | 1.0–1.3 | per pilot: radio banter, podium |\n1083\t| principals | 110–190 Hz | 0.9 | briefings |\n1084\t| KAI-ZERO | 140 Hz | 1.1 | bitcrushed (a WaveShaper step curve) |\n1085\t\n1086\t`E.Dialog` boxes use `voice: null` (no letter blips) and call `SN.Voice.say` per page.\n1087\t\n1088\t**Announcer lines** (each spoken as gibberish **and** shown as a subtitle, Settings → Subtitles):\n1089\t- every weapon name on pickup;\n1090\t- \"THREE\", \"TWO\", \"ONE\", \"GO\";\n1091\t- \"FINAL LAP\", \"PERFECT START\", \"BARREL ROLL\", \"SNIPED\", \"ELIMINATED\", \"WRONG WAY\", \"NEW LAP RECORD\";\n1092\t- \"ZONE {n}\", \"OVERCLOCKED\", \"RACE OVER\", \"WINNER\".\n1093\t\n1094\t### 3.11 Narrative and writing style (`09-data-story.js`)\n1095\t\n1096\tThe source's register: clipped, corporate, cool, a little ironic. It sounds like a league that sells speed like\n1097\tmineral water. Race control speaks in capitals and in rules. Teams speak like brochures. Pilots are terse and\n1098\tcompetitive. Sponsors are absurd and deadpan. No melodrama, no jokes that wink at the player. Everything is\n1099\toriginal: invented league, teams, people and brands.\n1100\t\n1101\t- **The league:** the **Hoverline Championship**, Season 2161, run by the **Hoverline Authority** (\"THE AUTHORITY\").\n1102\t  Its race-control intelligence is called **ORACLE**.\n1103\t  - Announcement style: `AUTHORITY NOTICE 0417 — ROOKIE LICENCE GRANTED. CLASS: SPARK. GRAVITY: OPTIONAL.`\n1104\t- **Team copy** (one line each, §4.1). Example:\n1105\t  `HAMMERHEAD HEAVY INDUSTRIES builds cranes, bridges and the occasional champion. All three survive impact.`\n1106\t- **Track copy.** Example: `PORT SOLENNE. Old stone, new money. The harbour lights are on a sponsorship contract.`\n1107\t- **Sponsor boards** (canvas textures, §4.6):\n1108\t  - `QWIK-FUEL — FILL UP. FALL UP.`\n1109\t  - `OKTA NOODLE — EAT AT 600 KM/H`\n1110\t  - `HALCYON BANK — YOUR MONEY, FASTER`\n1111\t  - `DO NOT LOOK DIRECTLY AT THE FUTURE`\n1112\t  - `AXON AIR — BREATHE PREMIUM`\n1113\t  - `VANTA PAINTS — DARKER THAN NOTHING`\n1114\t- **Story beats (the Season).** You are a test pilot signed to a race seat with your chosen team. Your team principal\n1115\t  briefs you. The rival collective NULL//SET (pilot KAI-ZERO) needles you. The Authority watches. The beats are listed\n1116\t  per event in §4.5.\n1117\t\n1118\t  The arc:\n1119\t  1. you are a rookie;\n1120\t  2. you get noticed;\n1121\t  3. a sponsor ultimatum, and NULL//SET's overclocking scandal (which is why OVERCLOCK trials exist);\n1122\t  4. the STORM class promotion;\n1123\t  5. the Grand Prix showdown;\n1124\t  6. champion, and SINGULARITY unlocked, with a deadpan Authority sign-off.\n1125\t\n1126\t### 3.12 Season, progression, saves (`08-data-season.js`, `78-season-ui.js`)\n1127\t\n1128\t- **Tiers:**\n1129\t  - Tier 1 (SPARK) is open from the start.\n1130\t  - Tier 2 (FLARE) opens with 3 medals in tier 1, which also **unlocks the FLARE class** everywhere.\n1131\t  - Tier 3 (STORM) opens with 3 medals in tier 2 and unlocks STORM.\n1132\t  - The GRAND PRIX opens with both tier-3 events at bronze or better.\n1133\t  - Winning the GP (any medal) **unlocks SINGULARITY**, the CHAMPION livery (gold trim on every team's craft, a\n1134\t    toggle in team select) and the ending.\n1135\t- Events can be replayed to improve a medal. The best medal is kept.\n1136\t- **Saves:** `game.saves` autosaves after every event and GP race. `game.saves.write` returns\n1137\t  `{ data, place: 'SEASON 2161', level: 'TIER 2' }`:\n1138\t\n1139\t  ```js\n1140\t  data = { v: 1, medals: { [eventId]: 'gold'|'silver'|'bronze' }, gp: { round, points: {pilotId: n}, done }, unlocked: { classes: [...], champion: bool },\n1141\t           seen: { [briefingId]: true }, records: { 'track/cls/mode': { ms, pilot } }, ghosts: { 'track/cls/mode': base64 }, team, pilot }\n1142\t  ```\n1143\t\n1144\t  `menu: { saves: true }` is **not** used (no save points). CONTINUE on the main menu loads `saves.latest()`. In a hub\n1145\t  session, storage is the hub's in-memory one, so nothing persists. That is expected.\n1146\t\n1147\t### 3.13 Replays, ghosts, records (`45-replay.js`)\n1148\t\n1149\t- **Replay** = re-simulate from the race's `{ seed, …, tune, frames }` (§2.8). The `replay` scene runs the sim at\n1150\t  `timeScale` 1, 2 or 4 (R1/L1, or a click on the speed chip) with the TV director (△ cycles: TV, chase, cockpit,\n1151\t  heli). A **click on any craft in the picture** (a hit test via `world.project` within 18 px) follows that craft.\n1152\t  ✕ pauses, ○ exits. On the last frame, assert that `R.hash()` equals the recorded hash. In dev builds, show \"REPLAY\n1153\t  DESYNC\" if not (a test guarantees it doesn't happen).\n1154\t- **Ghosts** (TIME TRIAL, HOT LAP): record the player's `(s, u, h, yaw relative to the track, roll)` at 20 Hz,\n1155\t  quantised to Int16, base64 in the save. Play back interpolated, as a translucent craft. The ghost never collides.\n1156\t  Save it only on a new best.\n1157\t- **Records:** best race and best lap per track/class/mode, with the pilot name. The NEW RECORD callout plus the\n1158\t  announcer.\n1159\t\n1160\t### 3.14 Attract mode (`85-attract.js`)\n1161\t\n1162\t- **Trigger:** 10 s with no input on the title or any front-end screen (`input.anyPressed()`, any `move()` above the\n1163\t  dead zone, any mouse move or click, or any key). The clock resets on input. It runs on touch-only devices too.\n1164\t- **Playlist** (loops; each segment 25–40 s, loading the track world in between behind a \"DEMO\" card):\n1165\t  1. a SPARK race at Port Solenne with 8 AI, weapons forced in rotation (all 10 weapons appear across the loop), a\n1166\t     barrel roll on the jump;\n1167\t  2. a STORM SNIPEOUT at Meridian Stack, with eliminations and respawns, and the Stack Drop;\n1168\t  3. OVERCLOCK at Karakum Spire, an AI from zone 1 jumping to zone 14 at one zone per 2 s, skin and music climbing;\n1169\t  4. a FLARE race at Borealis Vault, the Vault jump and the ice tunnel;\n1170\t  5. a 6 s title card with the logo and \"PRESS START\".\n1171\t\n1172\t  Each segment uses the TV director plus occasional chase and cockpit cuts.\n1173\t- **Cheats allowed:** infinite energy, forced pickups, no rescues, AI aggression 1.5.\n1174\t- **Overlay:** a \"DEMO\" chip at the top centre, the logo small at the top left, and \"PRESS ANY BUTTON\" blinking at the\n1175\t  bottom (the glyph of the last device). The HUD stays minimal: position list and weapon callouts, so the features\n1176\t  read.\n1177\t- **Exit:** **any** input (key, pad button, stick, mouse button, a click, a touch) returns to the title within one\n1178\t  step. The input is consumed (`input.consumeAll()`), so it doesn't also select anything. The race world stays loaded\n1179\t  for the title.\n1180\t\n1181\t### 3.15 Dev mode and live tuning (`80-dev.js`, `SN.Tune` in `00-core.js`)\n1182\t\n1183\t- **Reach:** the pause menu item **Dev mode**. It is present in every race mode except hub sessions. Front-end\n1184\t  screens get it through OPTIONS ▸ DEV MODE, so it is reachable without a race too. The panel opens over the paused\n1185\t  game. ○ or Esc closes it back to the pause menu, and Options resumes. Controller, keyboard and mouse all work (the\n1186\t  §3.9 widget kit). Tabs switch with L1/R1, Q/E, or a click on a tab.\n1187\t- **Tune registry:** `SN.Tune.def(key, { def, min, max, step, label, group })`. Read values with `SN.Tune.T[key]`.\n1188\t  `SN.Tune.reset(key?)` restores one or all defaults. Values live in memory for the session (a \"RESET ALL TO\n1189\t  DEFAULTS\" button is always visible). Every replay snapshots them.\n1190\t\n1191\t| Tab | Contents |\n1192\t| --- | --- |\n1193\t| **CHEATS** | God mode (no damage) · Infinite weapon · Give weapon ◀ name ▶ (applies on ✕) · AI weapons off · Freeze AI · Ghost AI (no collisions) · Refill energy · Energy to 10 % · Skip to final lap · Win now (finish 1st / max points / zone +10) · Eliminate all AI · Unlock everything · Reset season progress (asks first, in-panel) |\n1194\t| **TUNING** (live sliders, ◀ ▶ adjust, hold to speed up, mouse drag on the bar, a reset ↺ per row, RESET ALL) | **Handling:** thrustMul 1 [0.5–2], topSpeedMul 1 [0.6–1.6], dragMul 1 [0.5–2], steerRate 1.9 [0.8–3.5], steerResponse 9 [2–20], gripMul 1 [0.3–2], airbrakeYaw 1.4 [0–3], airbrakeDrag 0.9 [0–2], gripMaxMul 1 [0.4–2], slipMax 35° [10–60], scrubK 0.35 [0–1], sideShiftSpeed 768 [0–1500], shiftDecay 12 [4–30]. **Hover:** hoverHeight 14 [6–30], hoverStiffness 220 [60–600], hoverDamping 28 [5–60], magnetPull 1800 [600–4000], airGravity 640 [200–1500], pitchEffect 1 [0–2]. **Walls & energy:** wallBounce 0.35 [0–1], wallFriction 0.25 [0–1], wallDamage 1 [0–3], pitRecharge 25 [0–100], rollCost 10 [0–30], rollBoost 1.2 [1–1.6]. **Pads & weapons:** padBoost 1.25 [1–1.8], padBoostTime 0.9 [0.2–2.5], weaponDamageMul 1 [0–3], absorbMul 1 [0–3], pickupLuck 1 [0–2]. **AI:** aiSkill 1 [0.5–1.2], aiRubberBand 1 [0–2], aiAggression 1 [0–2]. **Camera:** camDistance 150 [60–300], camHeight 46 [10–120], camFov 72 [50–100], camFovBoost 16 [0–40], camLag 8 [1–20] |\n1195\t| **WORLD** | Time scale (0.25 / 0.5 / 1 / 2) · Teleport: lap position % slider + GO · Free camera · Overclock zone +1 · Weather on/off · HUD on/off · Debug overlay (centre line, slice frames, racing line coloured by target speed, craft collision spheres, pad rectangles, AI targets, camera spots) |\n1196\t| **INFO** | live: s, u, h, p, speed (u/s and km/h), energy, lap, sector, position, airborne time, slice index, surface kind, seed, `R.hash()`, World3D backend and `world.stats` (calls, tris, ms), steps per second |\n1197\t\n1198\t### 3.16 Multiplayer: local split screen and AI Hub sessions\n1199\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4110026b-2798-4dbf-ae8a-e81d8e816e30","uuid":"1c3f87ea-1252-4449-975a-0847e0d41450","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:46:58.112Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261103-184630__xa320fb/work/PLAN.md","content":"\n### 3.7 Rendering (`60-render.js`, `62-shipkit.js`, `64-trackmesh.js`, `66-scenery.js`, `68-fx.js`)\n\n**Worlds.** `World3D.init(game)` runs once (boot). Then:\n- **Hangar world**, made at boot. A small `level` (text rows):\n  - a 24 × 16 tile hall: floor `{ floor: 0 }`, a turntable `{ mark: 'turntable' }` and a podium of three raised floors\n    (`{ floor: 24 }` 1st, `{ floor: 16 }` 2nd, `{ floor: 8 }` 3rd, marks `p1 p2 p3`);\n  - no torch tiles (`torchLights: 0`); our own lights: 3 coloured `world.light`s plus team-coloured neon strips\n    (our meshes);\n  - camera `'fixed'`, `fog: false`.\n\n  It is used by the menus, team select (the craft on the turntable), results/podium (pilots as rig **cards** via\n  `world.hero({ rig })` posed `cheer` / `wave` / `hips`) and the ending.\n- **Track world**, one per track, made by the `loading` scene. At most one is alive besides the hangar: dispose the\n  previous with `world.dispose()`. Boot makes PORT SOLENNE's, so the title and attract start at once.\n\n```js\nnew E.World3D(game, {\n  terrain: { size: 65536 /* 4 km */, height: theme.height, color: theme.color, far: 26000, cell: 64, rock: theme.rock, bottom: -3000 },\n  sky: theme.sky, fog: theme.fog, ambient: theme.ambient, sun: Object.assign({ shadow: true, area: 900 }, theme.sun),\n  torchLights: 0, lights: 4, glowLights: 8, shadows: game.settings.shadows3d !== false,\n  filter: { look: game.settings.filter3d || 'clean', bloom: game.settings.bloom !== false },\n  camera: { mode: 'fixed', far: 26000, near: 4 }, particleGround: (x, y, z) => track.groundBelow(x, y, z),\n  onDraw: (w, r) => SN.render.onDraw(w, r)\n});\n```\n\n**Terrain carving.** `theme.height(x, y)` = the theme's natural height, combined with a **corridor grid** (cell 16 m,\nbuilt from the slices at load):\n- near the track: `min(natural, deckZ − clearance(d))`, where `clearance` grows from 3 m at the edge to 0 at 60 m, so\n  the ground falls away under elevated decks and meets the track at grade;\n- under tunnel slices: `max(natural, ceilZ + 4 m)`, so the rock covers the tunnel;\n- portal frames hide the seams.\n\nKeep `height()` fast: it is a few grid lookups and noise (`E.noise2`).\n\n**Materials** (make them all when the world is made, never mid-race):\n- `MeshLambertNodeMaterial({ vertexColors: true })` for the track surface, walls and scenery;\n- `MeshBasicNodeMaterial` for emissive neon, pads, engine glow and beams. They are bright, so the bloom catches them.\n  Set `fog: false` on the overclock skin;\n- `MeshToonNodeMaterial` for the craft hulls;\n- transparent additive materials for the shield shells, ghosts and beams.\n\nTextures are canvases drawn pixel by pixel at 64–256 px (`NearestFilter`, the engine's native crisp look): track\npanels, lane dashes, chevrons, sponsor boards, team logos, window grids. **Pads and painted markings** use\n`polygonOffset` (factor −2, units −2) and sit 1 u above the surface. That avoids z-fighting at distance.\n\n**Track meshes** (`64-trackmesh.js`), built in chunks of 40 slices (80 m) for frustum culling:\n- **Surface:** 6 lateral strips. Vertex colours: dark graphite panels `#22252c`/`#2a2e36` alternating every 8 m,\n  bright edge lines, centre dashes, a tint per theme. The grid boxes and the start/finish chequer are painted near\n  `s = 0`.\n- **Walls:** 1.6 m barrier panels with a glowing top strip in the theme's neon (`#29c8e8` coast, `#ffb347` desert,\n  `#ff3ab4` city, `#7af0ff` arctic). On the outside of curves, **directional chevrons** (emissive arrows pointing the\n  way of the turn) every 6 m. Open edges have no wall but a dashed hazard line on the edge.\n- **Underside and supports:**\n  - the deck's underside and thickness (1.2 m), so the deck reads as a bridge;\n  - pylons every 40 m where the deck is more than 4 m above the terrain, at the deck edges; skipped where they would\n    stand in another section's driving envelope;\n  - overpass decks get piers outside the lower deck's walls.\n- **Tunnels:** a 10-segment arch to 12 m, ribs every 12 m, emissive light strips along both upper sides, portal\n  facades by style (stone arches, neon frames, ice). Three world lights follow the player through tunnels (warm,\n  cool, theme).\n- **Pads:**\n  - speed pad: an 8 × 6 m quad with 3 chevrons whose colours cycle front to back at 6 Hz (the pad meshes' colour\n    attribute rewritten each frame, `needsUpdate`), cyan `#3ad8ff`;\n  - weapon pad: a 6 × 6 m amber `#ffb000` quad with a pulsing triangle sigil and a light post at the edge;\n  - pit strip: green `#3aff8a` with \"+\" marks and a gantry sign PIT.\n- **Gantries:** the start/finish gantry has the 3-light start lights (red → green), a timing board (canvas texture\n  showing the race time) and team flags. Sponsor gantries go every ~350 m over the track. Each track also has a\n  landmark arch.\n- **Drop and gap edges:** the lip face (a vertical face), the far-edge face, and a hazard stripe painted on the lip.\n- **Overclock skin:** a **separate world** that the `loading` scene builds for OVERCLOCK runs (and the attract's\n  overclock segment), so no fog or sky changes are needed at runtime:\n  - theme `overclock`: black sky, black fog close in (near 2400 u, far 9600 u), flat black terrain at −400 m, no\n    scenery;\n  - the same track chunks built with the overclock materials: a black surface with an emissive grid (lines every 4 m)\n    and neon wall lines;\n  - each zone changes only the materials' colour, `hsl(zone·37°, 100%, 60%)` (no new materials, so no shader builds);\n  - sky colour pulses on the beat; bloom up.\n\n**Craft (`62-shipkit.js`)**, built from code as BufferGeometry, flat-shaded, 200–600 triangles each:\n- **Hull:** lofted through 6 cross-sections (an octagon scaled per section, from the needle nose to the tail), with\n  per-design profiles;\n- **canopy:** dark glossy, with an emissive rim;\n- **wings:** flat wedges, swept, with team-coloured tips;\n- **fins:** 0–2;\n- **engine pods:** 1–3, cylinders with emissive inner discs (team engine colour);\n- **airbrake flaps:** 2 hinged boxes at the rear sides (rotate);\n- **livery** by vertex colour per part (primary, secondary, accent stripe), the race number, and the team logo\n  (a 32 px canvas decal on the top);\n- **exhaust trail:** a ribbon of the last 0.35 s of tail positions, alpha fading, team colour;\n- **boost flame:** a cone that grows;\n- **shield shell:** an ellipsoid at opacity 0 that flashes to 0.6 on a hit, bulwark-blue for BULWARK;\n- **explosion:** 8 hull shards flying ballistically for 1.5 s, plus `particles.explosion` and a light flash;\n- **rescue drone:** a 4-rotor drone mesh with a tractor beam cone.\n\nThe six designs are in §4.1. **Ghosts** (hub players, time-trial ghost) use the same mesh in a transparent additive\nmaterial (opacity 0.35) tinted with the seat or ghost colour, plus a name tag.\n\n**Effects (`68-fx.js`)**:\n- wall sparks via `game.particles.sparks` at the contact point;\n- dust and spray on landings (`dust`; water spray at Solenne and Borealis);\n- weapon visuals: rocket meshes with smoke trails, the seeker's spiral trail, mines (spinning spheres, blinking red),\n  cannon tracers, the rail beam (a 0.6 m white-cyan cylinder fading over 0.4 s, plus a screen flash), the tremor wave\n  (a glowing band of quads riding the surface), the bulwark hex bubble, the autopilot ring, nitro flames, the siphon\n  zigzag beam;\n- **speed lines** in the HUD (screen-space streaks from the centre, density ∝ `(v/top)²`, more while boosting);\n- weather: Borealis snow (instanced flakes near the camera), Karakum heat-haze dust, Meridian light rain (streak\n  particles), Solenne sea spray.\n\n**Split screen.** `game.splitScreen(2, { layout: 'rows' })` with `world.addCamera({ mode: 'fixed', far: 26000 })`.\nEach viewport's `camera.fixed` is set from its own player's chase or cockpit cam. World3D turns filters off while\nsplit, which is expected.\n\n**Warm-up.** In `loading`, after everything is built, do one hidden frame with every pooled mesh visible in front of\nthe camera (each weapon FX, both skins, ghosts), call `world.prepare()`, then hide them. No shader stalls mid-race.\n\n### 3.8 HUD (`70-hud.js`): pixel art at game resolution, anchored to `r.W × r.H`\n\nLayout at 427 × 240 (16:9; everything is anchored and scales with `HUD size`):\n- **Top left:** POSITION as a big number (`E.font.title`, scale 4) plus `/8` small. LAP `2/3` below it. In SNIPEOUT\n  this is the points table (top 4) instead.\n- **Top centre:** the race time `1:23.45`. On a lap: the lap time with ±delta vs best (green/red), held 3 s.\n  \"FINAL LAP\" banner.\n- **Top right:** the minimap (72 px), craft as team-coloured dots, the player blinking, ghosts hollow.\n- **Bottom left:** the weapon slot. A 24 × 24 pixel icon per weapon (§4.4), its name, and prompts `□ FIRE  ○ ABSORB`\n  drawn with the glyph icons (§3.9). The pickup roll spin. The railshot charge ring. The autopilot/bulwark countdown.\n- **Bottom right:**\n  - speed: a segmented bar of 24 segments, cyan → white → magenta in boost, with km/h at scale 2;\n  - energy: 20 segments, green > 50 %, yellow > 25 %, red and blinking below; it shakes on damage; \"PIT\" hint when\n    low;\n  - the boost indicator.\n- **Centre:**\n  - the countdown digits (scale 6, pop tween);\n  - the rev bar during the countdown;\n  - **callouts:** weapon names, PERFECT START, BARREL ROLL, SNIPED!, ELIMINATED, WRONG WAY, PERFECT LAP, NEW RECORD,\n    ZONE n. They pop with scale and alpha, last 1.2 s, and stack at most 2;\n  - the lock reticle on the projected target (`world.project`), a rotating bracket that turns red when locked;\n  - the incoming-lock arrow at the bottom centre.\n- **Name tags:** pilot name and position above craft within 2500 u (projected), fading with distance.\n- **Radio box:** a small portrait (`rig.drawPortrait`, 28 px) and a subtitle line at the top left under the position\n  for pilot banter and the announcer (§3.10).\n- **Split screen:** per viewport a compact HUD (position, lap, speed, energy, weapon) via `r.viewport`. Countdown and\n  results go over the whole screen in `scene.hud(r)`.\n- **Overclock:** ZONE number (scale 4), the zone progress bar (12 s), speed, energy. No position or lap.\n- **Hub session:** the ghost players' names and live positions.\n- The HUD stays clear of `game.cornerArea()` when the corner shows (it is hidden in play).\n\n### 3.9 Front-end, UI and UX: 10-foot and controller-first (`75-ui.js`, `55-glyphs.js`, `01-input.js`)\n\n**Rules for every screen** (TASK.md: a TV at 10 feet, no dense web-style data screens):\n- At most 6 focusable items per screen.\n- Labels at font scale ≥ 2 (14 px of 240). Titles at scale 3–4. Body text at scale 2, at most 3 lines.\n- One focus at a time. It is drawn as a thick animated chevron frame plus a colour shift plus a 1 px \"scanline\"\n  shimmer. It is never shown by colour alone (TASK and engine rule).\n- Navigation:\n  - d-pad, stick or arrows (WASD too in menus) move the focus, with `input.repeat` when held;\n  - ✕, Enter or Space confirms; ○, Esc or Backspace goes back;\n  - L1/R1, Q/E or the mouse wheel switch tabs or pages;\n  - **mouse hover moves the focus**, a left click activates, and every screen has a clickable BACK chip at the bottom\n    left.\n- **A prompt bar** at the bottom of every screen shows the actions for the **last device used**\n  (`input.lastDevice`):\n  - gamepad: glyph icons;\n  - keyboard: keycaps;\n  - mouse: mouse icons (left click SELECT, BACK chip).\n\n  It switches the moment another device is touched.\n- **Glyph icons (`55-glyphs.js`):**\n  - **PlayStation** (the default): ✕ blue `#7cb2e8`, ○ red `#ff6b6b`, □ pink `#ff79c6`, △ green `#3fd8a6`, drawn in\n    dark discs of 11 px; L1/R1/L2/R2 as rounded tabs with text; Options and Create as pill icons; the d-pad and stick\n    as small icons.\n  - **Xbox** (Settings → Button symbols): A green, B red, X blue, Y yellow; LB/RB/LT/RT; Menu and View.\n  - **Keyboard:** keycaps sized to the label from `input.label(action, 'keyboard')`.\n  - **Mouse:** a mouse with the left or right button lit.\n\n  `SN.glyph.draw(g, action, x, y, { device })` returns the width drawn. **Never hard-code key names.** Always go\n  through `input.label` and the actual bindings (rebinding works).\n- Animations: menu tiles slide in with `game.tween` (0.18 s, `outBack`), focus chevrons pulse, background light\n  streaks drift, and screen changes use the engine's `'wipe'` fade (0.25 s).\n\n**Input mapping (`01-input.js`).** The game's preset, in this order (the order matters for the engine's half-keyboard\nsplit, §3.16):\n\n```js\nSN.INPUT = {\n  up: ['KeyW', 'ArrowUp', 'Pad12'], down: ['KeyS', 'ArrowDown', 'Pad13'], left: ['KeyA', 'ArrowLeft', 'Pad14'], right: ['KeyD', 'ArrowRight', 'Pad15'],\n  start: ['Enter', 'Pad9'], pause: ['Escape', 'KeyP', 'Pad9'], confirm: ['Enter', 'Space', 'Pad0'], cancel: ['Escape', 'Backspace', 'Pad1'],\n  thrust: ['KeyW', 'Pad0'], fire: ['Space', 'Mouse0', 'Pad2'], absorb: ['ShiftLeft', 'Mouse2', 'Pad1'],\n  brakeL: ['KeyQ', 'Pad6'], brakeR: ['KeyE', 'Pad7'], camera: ['KeyC', 'Pad3'], shiftL: ['KeyZ', 'Pad4'], shiftR: ['KeyX', 'Pad5'],\n  brake: ['KeyS'], lookBack: ['KeyB', 'Pad11']\n};\n```\n\n- In a race, **steer and pitch are not read from up/down/left/right as actions**:\n  - steer = `input.padMove[0]` (analog) + digital A/D/←/→/d-pad (ramped);\n  - pitch = `−input.padMove[1]` + ↑/↓/d-pad (stick up = nose down).\n\n  W and S are therefore only thrust and brake in a race, while still moving the menu focus elsewhere.\n- Airbrakes: `max(input.value('brakeL'), down('brake'))` (analog L2/R2 via engine edit 3).\n- Double-tapping Q or E (within 0.25 s) = side-shift.\n- Mouse buttons fire and absorb in a race.\n- The **virtual pad** `SN.vpad[playerIndex]` (analog values) is merged into the controls. The tests' bots, the\n  autopilot and the attract mode drive craft through it, the same path as a human.\n- The menu's Controls screen names the actions:\n  `menu: { controls: { thrust: 'Thrust', fire: 'Fire weapon', absorb: 'Absorb weapon', brakeL: 'Airbrake left',\n  brakeR: 'Airbrake right', brake: 'Both airbrakes', shiftL: 'Side-shift / roll left', shiftR: 'Side-shift / roll right',\n  camera: 'Camera', lookBack: 'Look back' } }`.\n\n**Screens:**\n\n| Screen | Contents (10-foot: big, few, focused) |\n| --- | --- |\n| **Title** | The Solenne track world in a slow TV-director flyby. The SNIPEOUT HD logo: `E.font.title` scale 5, chrome gradient `['#ffffff', '#9ff4ff', '#29c8e8', '#1a2a4a']`, with a pixel \"HD\" badge and an animated light sweep. The tagline. \"PRESS ✕ / ENTER\" pulsing (glyph of the last device). The version (`E.versionLabel()`) small at the bottom right. Idle for 10 s → attract |\n| **Touch-only notice** | **Detection:** `!matchMedia('(any-pointer: fine)').matches && navigator.maxTouchPoints > 0`, no gamepad connected, and no key pressed yet. Re-check on every key press and on `gamepadconnected`; the notice goes away as soon as one appears. **Shows:** over the title, \"CONTROLLER OR KEYBOARD REQUIRED\" (scale 2, centred, in a panel) and one big **SETTINGS** button (tap → `game.menu('settings')`). `game.input.touchEnabled = false` and no scene declares `touch`, so there are no touch controls anywhere. The attract still starts after 10 s, and a tap returns to this notice |\n| **Main menu** | Hangar world (the player's last craft on the turntable). A vertical list of 6 big tiles: **SEASON · QUICK RACE · CHALLENGES ▸ · VERSUS · ACADEMY · OPTIONS ▸**. CHALLENGES opens TIME TRIAL / HOT LAP / SNIPEOUT / OVERCLOCK; OPTIONS opens SETTINGS / CONTROLS / HOW TO PLAY / RECORDS / ABOUT / DEV MODE. When an autosave exists, the first tile reads **CONTINUE SEASON** (it loads `saves.latest()` and opens the season hub) |\n| **Class select** | 4 tiles in a row: SPARK / FLARE / STORM / SINGULARITY, with a top-speed figure and a lock icon plus the unlock hint (\"WIN THE ROOKIE LICENCE\") |\n| **Track select** | One big card at a time (←/→ or L1/R1 or the wheel or a click on the arrows): the track outline at 150 px drawn with px.line, the name (scale 3), place, length, a difficulty pip row, your best time, and a one-line blurb. The hangar background tints to the theme |\n| **Team and pilot select** | The craft on the turntable (mouse drag rotates it, the right stick rotates). Team name (scale 3) and logo. **4 stat bars** (SPEED, THRUST, HANDLING, SHIELD) as 10-segment bars. One-line bio. The pilot toggle (2 pilots, portraits via `rig.drawPortrait` at 48 px). ←/→ change team |\n| **Laps / confirm** | A summary card (mode, class, track, team, laps), START RACE |\n| **Loading** | The track name card, a progress bar, and one tip line (\"Absorb a weapon you can't use: shield is worth more than a miss.\") |\n| **Race** | the HUD (§3.8) |\n| **Results** | The top 8 as **one row per craft**: position, team colour chip, pilot, time or gap, best-lap star. The player's row is highlighted. Medal and record banners. Actions: CONTINUE · RETRY · REPLAY · MENU. A podium cutaway (hangar world, top 3 pilot cards cheering, confetti) plays first for 4 s when the player is top 3 |\n| **Season hub** | 4 columns (ROOKIE LICENCE, AUTHORITY NOTICE, STORM WARNING, GRAND PRIX), each with 2–4 event tiles: mode icon, track, medal earned. Locked columns are dimmed with the rule shown. Before an event's first run, a briefing (§3.11) |\n| **GP standings** | Between races: 8 rows, points, the gap to the leader, NEXT RACE |\n| **How to play** | 5 pages (L1/R1): CONTROLS (the controller diagram drawn in pixels, or the keyboard map, by device), RACING (pads, pitch, airbrakes, side-shift, rolls), WEAPONS (10 icons with a one-line effect each, two pages), ENERGY (walls, damage, pit lane, absorb, elimination), MODES |\n| **Records** | per track: best race and best lap per class, pilot name. One track per page |\n| **About / Credits** | §3.18 |\n\n### 3.10 Audio (`50-audio.js`, `10-data-music.js`): all synthesized, no files\n\n**Music:** the engine's tracker (`game.audio.music(song, { sync: true })`) with the §2.7 extensions. Songs are data:\n`{ bpm, steps: 4, tracks: [{ name, wave, vol, lp, uni, det, pan, notes, on }] }`. **Layers** (`audio.layer(name, vol,\nfade)`) make the music react:\n- the countdown has pads and bass only;\n- the drums come in at GO;\n- the lead comes in on the final lap;\n- after the race, everything but the pads fades out;\n- Overclock adds a layer every 2 zones and runs `audio.tempo(min(176, bpm + 3·zone))`.\n\nWhen a race starts, a \"now playing\" toast shows (`♪ STACKLINE — NULLPOINT`). Fictional artists, all original.\n\n| Song (id) | Where | BPM / key | Character |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `zero` \"Zero Crossing\" by HALCYON DRIFT | title, menus | 112, D minor | airy pads, a soft arpeggio, a broken beat |\n| `solenne` \"Riviera Burn\" by SOLSTICE 9 | Port Solenne | 128, A minor | sunny electro-house, four-on-the-floor, offbeat open hats, a pumping saw bass, a pluck lead |\n| `karakum` \"Sandglass\" by DUNE//CODE | Karakum Spire | 140, E Phrygian | big beat, breakbeat drums (k/s pattern), a distorted acid bass (`lp` env), a call-and-response lead |\n| `meridian` \"Stackline\" by NULLPOINT | Meridian Stack | 172 (half-time feel), F minor | drum'n'bass breaks, a reese bass (`uni: 3, det: 18` saw, lowpass), stabs |\n| `borealis` \"Polar Vector\" by AURORA SYSTEMS | Borealis Vault | 136, B minor | trance: rolling 16th bass, a supersaw lead, a long riser every 8 bars |\n| `overclock` \"Clock Skew\" by THE AUTHORITY | Overclock | 120 → 176 | minimal techno that adds a layer per 2 zones |\n| stings | lap, final lap, win, podium, eliminated, unlock, medal | — | 1–3 s motifs (`audio.sting`) |\n\nExample, the start of `solenne`, to set the format and the bar:\n\n```js\nSN.SONGS.solenne = { bpm: 128, steps: 4, tracks: [\n  { name: 'kick',  wave: 'drums', vol: .22, notes: 'k . . . k . . . k . . . k . . . | k . . . k . . . k . . . k . k .' },\n  { name: 'hats',  wave: 'drums', vol: .10, notes: '. . o . . . o . . . o . . . o h | . . o . . . o . . . o . . h o h' },\n  { name: 'clap',  wave: 'drums', vol: .14, notes: '. . . . p . . . . . . . p . . . | . . . . p . . . . . . . p . p .' },\n  { name: 'bass',  wave: 'saw', vol: .16, lp: { f: 300, q: 9, env: 1800, dec: .12 },\n    notes: 'A1 . A2 . A1 A2 . A1 . A2 . A1 G2 . A2! . | F1 . F2 . F1 F2 . F1 . F2 . F1 E2 . F2! .' },\n  { name: 'pad',   wave: 'saw', vol: .05, uni: 3, det: 14, lp: { f: 1400, q: 1 }, notes: 'A3 - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - | F3 - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -' },\n  { name: 'lead',  wave: 'pulse', vol: .07, on: false, notes: 'E5 . C5 . A4 . C5 E5 . G5 . E5 . C5 . . | F5 . C5 . A4 . C5 F5 . A5 . F5 . E5 . .' }\n] };\n```\n\nEach song needs at least 16 bars of material (A/B sections, a breakdown) so that a 3-minute race doesn't drone.\n\n**SFX** (`audio.define` voices, plus our own WebAudio graphs on the effects bus where a voice can't do it). These\nnames are referenced by events (§2.5):\n\n| Group | Sounds |\n| --- | --- |\n| UI | `ui_move` (short pulse blip), `ui_ok` (two-tone up), `ui_back` (down), `ui_locked` (buzz), `ui_tab` (click) |\n| Race | `count_beep`, `count_go` (chord), `lap` (chime), `final_lap` (a rising sting), `finish` (fanfare), `wrongway` (siren blip), `pos_up` / `pos_down` (tiny arps) |\n| Craft | engine hum (continuous, below), `boost_pad` (whoosh plus a pitch sweep), `pickup_roll` (a ticking arp), `weapon_pad` (sparkle), `airbrake` (filtered noise hiss, looped while braking), `sideshift` (puff), `roll` (a whirr), `roll_boost`, `botch`, `land_soft`, `land_hard` (thud plus clank), `wall_hit` (metal bang, pitch by impact), `scrape` (looped band-passed noise, volume by speed), `bump`, `pit_charge` (looped rising tone), `low_shield` (beep every 0.8 s), `explode` (noise boom plus a sub drop), `eliminated`, `respawn`, `rescue` (drone whine) |\n| Weapons | `swarm_fire`, `seeker_lock` (beeps faster to a solid tone), `seeker_fire`, `mine_drop`, `cannon_fire`, `rail_charge` (a rising whine), `rail_fire` (crack plus a long zap), `tremor` (sub rumble), `bulwark_on/off`, `autopilot_on/off`, `nitro`, `siphon` (a crackling loop), `absorb` (a reverse whoosh with a chime), `hit_light`, `hit_heavy` |\n\n**Engine hum.** The four nearest craft each get a persistent graph: saw + detuned square → lowpass → gain →\nStereoPanner → the effects bus.\n- `f = 48 + 120·(v/top)` Hz with a thrust wobble.\n- Cutoff `500 + 2500·(v/top)` (+1500 in boost).\n- Others: volume by distance (1/(1 + d/800 u)), Doppler pitch `×clamp(1 + vRel/6000, .85, 1.15)`, pan by the screen\n  x of `world.project`.\n- The player's hum is louder and centred.\n- In a split screen: player 1 pans left, player 2 right.\n- All of it is muted on pause, on `game.audio.muted`, and on the hub's `end`.\n\n**Gibberish voice (Animalese/Simlish style), `SN.Voice.say(text, voice)`:**\n- Every word is turned into syllables seeded by the word's hash, so the same word always sounds the same (\"SEEKER\"\n  is always \"see-kra\").\n- Syllable count = `max(1, round(letters / 2.6))`.\n- Each syllable is a consonant burst (noise, band-passed at 2–5 kHz, 18 ms; picked by the word's letters) followed by\n  a vowel: a saw at `f0` through two band-pass \"formants\" `[F1, F2]` from a 5-vowel table (a: 800/1200, e: 400/2000,\n  i: 300/2300, o: 450/800, u: 325/700), lasting `70–110 ms / speed`.\n- Pitch: per-syllable jitter ±8 %; down 12 % at a full stop, up 18 % at \"?\", +10 % and louder at \"!\".\n- Breathiness: 15 % noise.\n- `say()` returns its duration. Subtitles and dialog pages wait on it. Headless, it is computed without sound.\n\n| Voice | f0 | Speed | Use |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ANNOUNCER (race control's \"ORACLE\") | 205 Hz | 0.85 | calm, slightly ring-modulated (×0.4 at 60 Hz) |\n| pilots | 95–240 Hz | 1.0–1.3 | per pilot: radio banter, podium |\n| principals | 110–190 Hz | 0.9 | briefings |\n| KAI-ZERO | 140 Hz | 1.1 | bitcrushed (a WaveShaper step curve) |\n\n`E.Dialog` boxes use `voice: null` (no letter blips) and call `SN.Voice.say` per page.\n\n**Announcer lines** (each spoken as gibberish **and** shown as a subtitle, Settings → Subtitles):\n- every weapon name on pickup;\n- \"THREE\", \"TWO\", \"ONE\", \"GO\";\n- \"FINAL LAP\", \"PERFECT START\", \"BARREL ROLL\", \"SNIPED\", \"ELIMINATED\", \"WRONG WAY\", \"NEW LAP RECORD\";\n- \"ZONE {n}\", \"OVERCLOCKED\", \"RACE OVER\", \"WINNER\".\n\n### 3.11 Narrative and writing style (`09-data-story.js`)\n\nThe source's register: clipped, corporate, cool, a little ironic. It sounds like a league that sells speed like\nmineral water. Race control speaks in capitals and in rules. Teams speak like brochures. Pilots are terse and\ncompetitive. Sponsors are absurd and deadpan. No melodrama, no jokes that wink at the player. Everything is\noriginal: invented league, teams, people and brands.\n\n- **The league:** the **Hoverline Championship**, Season 2161, run by the **Hoverline Authority** (\"THE AUTHORITY\").\n  Its race-control intelligence is called **ORACLE**.\n  - Announcement style: `AUTHORITY NOTICE 0417 — ROOKIE LICENCE GRANTED. CLASS: SPARK. GRAVITY: OPTIONAL.`\n- **Team copy** (one line each, §4.1). Example:\n  `HAMMERHEAD HEAVY INDUSTRIES builds cranes, bridges and the occasional champion. All three survive impact.`\n- **Track copy.** Example: `PORT SOLENNE. Old stone, new money. The harbour lights are on a sponsorship contract.`\n- **Sponsor boards** (canvas textures, §4.6):\n  - `QWIK-FUEL — FILL UP. FALL UP.`\n  - `OKTA NOODLE — EAT AT 600 KM/H`\n  - `HALCYON BANK — YOUR MONEY, FASTER`\n  - `DO NOT LOOK DIRECTLY AT THE FUTURE`\n  - `AXON AIR — BREATHE PREMIUM`\n  - `VANTA PAINTS — DARKER THAN NOTHING`\n- **Story beats (the Season).** You are a test pilot signed to a race seat with your chosen team. Your team principal\n  briefs you. The rival collective NULL//SET (pilot KAI-ZERO) needles you. The Authority watches. The beats are listed\n  per event in §4.5.\n\n  The arc:\n  1. you are a rookie;\n  2. you get noticed;\n  3. a sponsor ultimatum, and NULL//SET's overclocking scandal (which is why OVERCLOCK trials exist);\n  4. the STORM class promotion;\n  5. the Grand Prix showdown;\n  6. champion, and SINGULARITY unlocked, with a deadpan Authority sign-off.\n\n### 3.12 Season, progression, saves (`08-data-season.js`, `78-season-ui.js`)\n\n- **Tiers:**\n  - Tier 1 (SPARK) is open from the start.\n  - Tier 2 (FLARE) opens with 3 medals in tier 1, which also **unlocks the FLARE class** everywhere.\n  - Tier 3 (STORM) opens with 3 medals in tier 2 and unlocks STORM.\n  - The GRAND PRIX opens with both tier-3 events at bronze or better.\n  - Winning the GP (any medal) **unlocks SINGULARITY**, the CHAMPION livery (gold trim on every team's craft, a\n    toggle in team select) and the ending.\n- Events can be replayed to improve a medal. The best medal is kept.\n- **Saves:** `game.saves` autosaves after every event and GP race. `game.saves.write` returns\n  `{ data, place: 'SEASON 2161', level: 'TIER 2' }`:\n\n  ```js\n  data = { v: 1, medals: { [eventId]: 'gold'|'silver'|'bronze' }, gp: { round, points: {pilotId: n}, done }, unlocked: { classes: [...], champion: bool },\n           seen: { [briefingId]: true }, records: { 'track/cls/mode': { ms, pilot } }, ghosts: { 'track/cls/mode': base64 }, team, pilot }\n  ```\n\n  `menu: { saves: true }` is **not** used (no save points). CONTINUE on the main menu loads `saves.latest()`. In a hub\n  session, storage is the hub's in-memory one, so nothing persists. That is expected.\n\n### 3.13 Replays, ghosts, records (`45-replay.js`)\n\n- **Replay** = re-simulate from the race's `{ seed, …, tune, frames }` (§2.8). The `replay` scene runs the sim at\n  `timeScale` 1, 2 or 4 (R1/L1, or a click on the speed chip) with the TV director (△ cycles: TV, chase, cockpit,\n  heli). A **click on any craft in the picture** (a hit test via `world.project` within 18 px) follows that craft.\n  ✕ pauses, ○ exits. On the last frame, assert that `R.hash()` equals the recorded hash. In dev builds, show \"REPLAY\n  DESYNC\" if not (a test guarantees it doesn't happen).\n- **Ghosts** (TIME TRIAL, HOT LAP): record the player's `(s, u, h, yaw relative to the track, roll)` at 20 Hz,\n  quantised to Int16, base64 in the save. Play back interpolated, as a translucent craft. The ghost never collides.\n  Save it only on a new best.\n- **Records:** best race and best lap per track/class/mode, with the pilot name. The NEW RECORD callout plus the\n  announcer.\n\n### 3.14 Attract mode (`85-attract.js`)\n\n- **Trigger:** 10 s with no input on the title or any front-end screen (`input.anyPressed()`, any `move()` above the\n  dead zone, any mouse move or click, or any key). The clock resets on input. It runs on touch-only devices too.\n- **Playlist** (loops; each segment 25–40 s, loading the track world in between behind a \"DEMO\" card):\n  1. a SPARK race at Port Solenne with 8 AI, weapons forced in rotation (all 10 weapons appear across the loop), a\n     barrel roll on the jump;\n  2. a STORM SNIPEOUT at Meridian Stack, with eliminations and respawns, and the Stack Drop;\n  3. OVERCLOCK at Karakum Spire, an AI from zone 1 jumping to zone 14 at one zone per 2 s, skin and music climbing;\n  4. a FLARE race at Borealis Vault, the Vault jump and the ice tunnel;\n  5. a 6 s title card with the logo and \"PRESS START\".\n\n  Each segment uses the TV director plus occasional chase and cockpit cuts.\n- **Cheats allowed:** infinite energy, forced pickups, no rescues, AI aggression 1.5.\n- **Overlay:** a \"DEMO\" chip at the top centre, the logo small at the top left, and \"PRESS ANY BUTTON\" blinking at the\n  bottom (the glyph of the last device). The HUD stays minimal: position list and weapon callouts, so the features\n  read.\n- **Exit:** **any** input (key, pad button, stick, mouse button, a click, a touch) returns to the title within one\n  step. The input is consumed (`input.consumeAll()`), so it doesn't also select anything. The race world stays loaded\n  for the title.\n\n### 3.15 Dev mode and live tuning (`80-dev.js`, `SN.Tune` in `00-core.js`)\n\n- **Reach:** the pause menu item **Dev mode**. It is present in every race mode except hub sessions. Front-end\n  screens get it through OPTIONS ▸ DEV MODE, so it is reachable without a race too. The panel opens over the paused\n  game. ○ or Esc closes it back to the pause menu, and Options resumes. Controller, keyboard and mouse all work (the\n  §3.9 widget kit). Tabs switch with L1/R1, Q/E, or a click on a tab.\n- **Tune registry:** `SN.Tune.def(key, { def, min, max, step, label, group })`. Read values with `SN.Tune.T[key]`.\n  `SN.Tune.reset(key?)` restores one or all defaults. Values live in memory for the session (a \"RESET ALL TO\n  DEFAULTS\" button is always visible). Every replay snapshots them.\n\n| Tab | Contents |\n| --- | --- |\n| **CHEATS** | God mode (no damage) · Infinite weapon · Give weapon ◀ name ▶ (applies on ✕) · AI weapons off · Freeze AI · Ghost AI (no collisions) · Refill energy · Energy to 10 % · Skip to final lap · Win now (finish 1st / max points / zone +10) · Eliminate all AI · Unlock everything · Reset season progress (asks first, in-panel) |\n| **TUNING** (live sliders, ◀ ▶ adjust, hold to speed up, mouse drag on the bar, a reset ↺ per row, RESET ALL) | **Handling:** thrustMul 1 [0.5–2], topSpeedMul 1 [0.6–1.6], dragMul 1 [0.5–2], steerRate 1.9 [0.8–3.5], steerResponse 9 [2–20], gripMul 1 [0.3–2], airbrakeYaw 1.4 [0–3], airbrakeDrag 0.9 [0–2], gripMaxMul 1 [0.4–2], slipMax 35° [10–60], scrubK 0.35 [0–1], sideShiftSpeed 768 [0–1500], shiftDecay 12 [4–30]. **Hover:** hoverHeight 14 [6–30], hoverStiffness 220 [60–600], hoverDamping 28 [5–60], magnetPull 1800 [600–4000], airGravity 640 [200–1500], pitchEffect 1 [0–2]. **Walls & energy:** wallBounce 0.35 [0–1], wallFriction 0.25 [0–1], wallDamage 1 [0–3], pitRecharge 25 [0–100], rollCost 10 [0–30], rollBoost 1.2 [1–1.6]. **Pads & weapons:** padBoost 1.25 [1–1.8], padBoostTime 0.9 [0.2–2.5], weaponDamageMul 1 [0–3], absorbMul 1 [0–3], pickupLuck 1 [0–2]. **AI:** aiSkill 1 [0.5–1.2], aiRubberBand 1 [0–2], aiAggression 1 [0–2]. **Camera:** camDistance 150 [60–300], camHeight 46 [10–120], camFov 72 [50–100], camFovBoost 16 [0–40], camLag 8 [1–20] |\n| **WORLD** | Time scale (0.25 / 0.5 / 1 / 2) · Teleport: lap position % slider + GO · Free camera · Overclock zone +1 · Weather on/off · HUD on/off · Debug overlay (centre line, slice frames, racing line coloured by target speed, craft collision spheres, pad rectangles, AI targets, camera spots) |\n| **INFO** | live: s, u, h, p, speed (u/s and km/h), energy, lap, sector, position, airborne time, slice index, surface kind, seed, `R.hash()`, World3D backend and `world.stats` (calls, tris, ms), steps per second |\n\n### 3.16 Multiplayer: local split screen and AI Hub sessions\n","numLines":420,"startLine":780,"totalLines":2083}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_015zZ1M9noWu7MayY3QCkbfk","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh3YNe6g6rsXCyqhdtrQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01L38mFHarpxYmq7EusHx4sy","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261103-184630__xa320fb/work/PLAN.md","offset":1199,"limit":420},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":16128,"cache_read_input_tokens":52800,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":16128},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4110026b-2798-4dbf-ae8a-e81d8e816e30","uuid":"9bf6f1e1-084d-41dd-a667-e1a40c418369","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:47:08.569Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh3YNQT952YHsWMR4New","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01L38mFHarpxYmq7EusHx4sy":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261103-184630__xa320fb/work/PLAN.md","offset":1199,"limit":420}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01L38mFHarpxYmq7EusHx4sy","type":"tool_result","content":"1199\t\n1200\t**Local (the game on its own): VERSUS for 2 players on one machine.**\n1201\t- On the VERSUS screen, `game.allowJoin({ max: 2 })`: player 2 presses Start on another pad, or 2 on the keyboard.\n1202\t- With two on the keyboard, the engine splits it with `Input.halfKeys` in our preset order (§3.9):\n1203\t  - **P1:** W/S pitch, A/D steer, F thrust, G fire, H absorb, R/T airbrakes, Y camera, V/B side-shift;\n1204\t  - **P2:** ↑/↓ pitch, ←/→ steer, `.` (Numpad 1) thrust, `/` (Numpad 2) fire, `,` (Numpad 3) absorb, L / `;`\n1205\t    (Numpad 4/5) airbrakes, `'` (Numpad 6) camera, K / M (Numpad 7/8) side-shift.\n1206\t\n1207\t  Both airbrakes together brake (`brake` and `lookBack` get no key in a half). Show both layouts on the join screen\n1208\t  with keycap glyphs, read from `players[i].label()`, never typed in by hand.\n1209\t- Both pick teams in turn, then choose RACE or SNIPEOUT, class and track. Split rows, with a compact HUD per\n1210\t  viewport.\n1211\t- Each player's prompts use their own device (`players[i].label()`). A pause says \"P2 PAUSED\" (engine).\n1212\t\n1213\t**AI Hub (`90-hub.js`): mode `ghost`**, following the protocol (`lib/hub/README.md`, client 1.4.0). Everyone races the\n1214\tsame seeded event on their own device and sees the others as ghosts.\n1215\t1. **Tags** in `<head>` (§2.3): players `1-4`, mode `ghost`, minutes `3`, goal and howto ≤ 60/80 characters.\n1216\t2. **`AIHub.active`** → the boot goes straight to the `session` scene: no title, menus, attract or prompts. The engine\n1217\t   options for the session: `autoPause: false`, the race `pausable: false`, `menu.quit: false`.\n1218\t3. `const info = await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'ghost', seats: [1, 4], card: true })`. If `null`, run the game normally.\n1219\t4. **The event:**\n1220\t   - track = `['solenne', 'karakum', 'meridian', 'borealis'][floor(AIHub.rng('event')() * 4)]`;\n1221\t   - class FLARE, 3 laps;\n1222\t   - race seed = `floor(AIHub.rng('race')() * 2^32)`;\n1223\t   - each human's team by seat (`['kestrel', 'soratek', 'volta', 'caldera'][seat]`), livery accent = seat colour;\n1224\t   - grid: the humans take slots by seat at the back of the grid (slots 5–8), and AI fill slots 1–4 plus any free\n1225\t     slots (8 − N AI);\n1226\t   - every copy simulates its own craft plus the AI. The other humans are **ghosts**: drawn from messages, never\n1227\t     collided with or targeted.\n1228\t5. **Own card** (`card: true`): the session scene shows a 3D grid shot of the chosen track with the players' craft\n1229\t   lined up in seat colours, the names, the ready ticks from the `card` event, the time left (`left`), the goal, and\n1230\t   this player's controls (the glyphs of the device seen so far, keyboard by default).\n1231\t   - **Ready:** Enter, ✕ or a tap/click on READY → `AIHub.answer('ready')`.\n1232\t   - **More time:** △, M, or a tap/click on MORE TIME → `AIHub.answer('more')`; pressing again takes it back.\n1233\t   - No `Math.random` on the card (use `AIHub.rng('card')` if needed). No menus or choices.\n1234\t6. Call `AIHub.ready()` once, as soon as the world is built and warm (boot plus the track loading), with no key press.\n1235\t7. **`start`**: the countdown lights follow `AIHub.time()` (−3000 → 0 ms), and the launch revs work. Racing begins\n1236\t   when `AIHub.time() ≥ 0`. The race clock is `AIHub.time()`.\n1237\t8. **Ghost traffic:** `AIHub.send({ t: 'g', p, u, h, y, r, v, lap, fin }, { reliable: false })` at 10 Hz (well under\n1238\t   20/s), plus `{ t: 'done', ms }` reliable on finishing.\n1239\t   - On `message`, update that ghost: interpolate toward the latest, 0.1 s behind. Draw it as a ghost craft (§3.7)\n1240\t     with the name in the seat colour, and add it to the HUD standings.\n1241\t   - On `leave`, remove it.\n1242\t9. **Progress:** about once a second, `AIHub.progress({ score: Math.round(p / 16), label: 'LAP 2/3 · 3RD' })`.\n1243\t10. **Result:**\n1244\t    - on finishing: `AIHub.result({ time: finishMs, stats: { 'Best lap': '0:41.22', 'Place vs AI': '2nd' },\n1245\t      awards: [...] })`;\n1246\t    - eliminations respawn in sessions, so everyone can finish;\n1247\t    - on `time-up`, if not finished: `AIHub.result({ score: Math.round(p / 16) })` at once.\n1248\t11. **`end`:** stop the sim, stop all input (ignore `game.input`), stop music, engine hums and SFX, and show \"ROUND\n1249\t    OVER\" with the standings from the event. The hub removes the page.\n1250\t12. **Rules:** network only through the hub (the CDN module loads are the game's own files); no `alert`, `confirm`,\n1251\t    `prompt` or `window.open` (none anywhere in the game); no chat or custom names. Restart and quit do nothing in a\n1252\t    session (the items are hidden).\n1253\t\n1254\t### 3.17 Settings: the game's own, beside the engine's standard ones\n1255\t\n1256\t`new E.Game({ menu: { settings: [...] } })`, groups `Game` and `Display`:\n1257\t- **Difficulty:** Easy / Normal / Hard.\n1258\t- **Speed units:** km/h / mph.\n1259\t- **Default camera:** Chase / Far chase / Cockpit.\n1260\t- **HUD size:** Normal / Large (×1.25).\n1261\t- **Subtitles:** on / off. They cover the announcer and radio; dialog boxes are always text.\n1262\t- **Announcer voice:** on / off.\n1263\t- **Speed lines:** on / off.\n1264\t- **Neon glow** (`bloom`): on / off.\n1265\t- **Picture** (`picture3d`): PIXELS (the engine's native default) / BALANCED / **HD**. HD is World3D's `'full'`.\n1266\t- **Shadows** (`shadows3d`): on / off.\n1267\t- **Filter** (`filter3d`): None / Comic cel / Pixel.\n1268\t- **Button symbols:** PlayStation (default) / Xbox. This is the engine's `glyphs`, moved to Display (§2.7.1).\n1269\t\n1270\tWorld3D reads `picture3d`, `shadows3d` and `filter3d` by those keys. Define them ourselves (same keys, values and\n1271\tlabels), because `E.World3D.SETTINGS` does not exist yet when `new E.Game` runs (§2.3). The engine provides the rest:\n1272\tvolume, music, effects, reduce motion, shake, flashes, full screen, frame rate, and the Controls screen (rebinding,\n1273\tdead zone, vibration).\n1274\t\n1275\t### 3.18 About / Credits and the exit interview (`11-data-about.js`)\n1276\t\n1277\t`SN.ABOUT` is the single source for the **About / Credits** screen (OPTIONS ▸ ABOUT, and after the ending credits) and\n1278\tfor `tools/exit-interview.mjs`, which writes `../exit-interview.json` in exactly TASK.md's shape and checks it parses.\n1279\t\n1280\tThe screen pages (L1/R1), each page big-type and short:\n1281\t1. **SOURCE INFORMATION:** every TASK.md field, \"unknown\" where it can't be confirmed. Planned values:\n1282\t   - Date: 2026-11-03 17:47:28\n1283\t   - Source: Wipeout HD (Studio Liverpool / Sony, 2008)\n1284\t   - Plan: PLAN.md\n1285\t   - Genre and perspective: anti-gravity combat racing; third-person chase camera with cockpit view and trackside TV\n1286\t     cameras\n1287\t   - Tech: my-3D2dge v0.85.2 handoff engine + my-3D2dge 3D v0.85.2, three.js r182 (WebGPU/WebGL 2), Rapier 0.19.3,\n1288\t     AI Hub client 1.4.0\n1289\t   - Art direction: the engine's native style (pixel-resolution 3D, toon/lambert light, pixel HUD and fonts) plus new\n1290\t     procedural craft, tracks and neon\n1291\t   - Animation: the engine's rigs and tweens, plus procedural craft animation\n1292\t   - Audio: synthesized music, SFX and gibberish voices\n1293\t   - Online: AI Hub ghost sessions; local split screen\n1294\t   - Testing; research; environment; model; usage\n1295\t2. **TESTING FEEDBACK:** the 4 answers.\n1296\t3. **ENGINE FEEDBACK:** the 6 answers, including the §2.7 changes.\n1297\t4. **PROMPT FEEDBACK:** the 4 answers.\n1298\t5. **CREDITS:**\n1299\t   - \"Snipeout HD. An original game inspired by Wipeout HD (not affiliated with Sony Interactive Entertainment).\"\n1300\t   - Engine credits (my-3D2dge, three.js MIT, Rapier Apache-2.0), \"all music, sound and voices synthesized in code\",\n1301\t     \"built by Anthropic claude-opus-5-5\".\n1302\t   - The fictional teams and artists, with a note that they are fictional.\n1303\t\n1304\tThe builder fills in the feedback answers truthfully at the end of the build (M12). The chat reply repeats them, as\n1305\tTASK.md demands. The `aiHub` block for the exit interview:\n1306\t\n1307\t```json\n1308\t{ \"name\": \"Snipeout HD\", \"tagline\": \"Anti-gravity. Anti-everyone.\",\n1309\t  \"description\": \"An anti-gravity combat racer: thread banked neon tracks at 600 km/h, snipe rivals with ten weapons and survive Overclock. Season, time trials, split screen and AI Hub ghost races.\",\n1310\t  \"type\": \"Game\", \"genre\": \"Racing\", \"source\": \"Wipeout HD\", \"series\": \"Wipeout\", \"players\": \"1–4\",\n1311\t  \"controls\": \"Stick or A/D steer · ✕ or W thrust · L2/R2 or Q/E airbrakes · □ or Space fire · ○ or Shift absorb\",\n1312\t  \"tags\": [\"3d\", \"racing\", \"sci-fi\", \"vehicles\", \"arcade\", \"versus\"] }\n1313\t```\n1314\t\n1315\t---\n1316\t\n1317\t## 4. Content\n1318\t\n1319\t### 4.1 Teams, craft, pilots, principals (`05-data-teams.js`)\n1320\t\n1321\tStats run 1–10 (§3.2 turns them into physics). The totals are close (22–24). NULL//SET trades shield for speed, which\n1322\tmakes it the rival.\n1323\t\n1324\t| Team (base) | SPD | THR | HND | SHD | Livery: primary / secondary / accent / engine glow | Craft and silhouette | One-line copy |\n1325\t| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n1326\t| **KESTREL DYNAMICS** (Oslo) | 6 | 6 | 6 | 6 | `#f2f5f8` / `#29c8e8` / `#1a2a4a` / `#7af0ff` | **KD-9 FJORD:** a dart hull, swept delta wings, twin canted tail fins, 2 engines | \"Precision is a form of courage. Kestrel has been brave since 2109.\" |\n1327\t| **HAMMERHEAD HEAVY INDUSTRIES** (Lagos) | 6 | 4 | 3 | 9 | `#ff7a1a` / `#2b2d33` / `#ffd23f` / `#ffb347` | **HH ANVIL:** a wide flat slab hull, twin hammerhead nose pods, stub wings, 3 engines | \"Builds cranes, bridges and the occasional champion. All three survive impact.\" |\n1328\t| **SORA-TEK** (Osaka) | 5 | 6 | 9 | 4 | `#f7f7f7` / `#e0213a` / `#16161c` / `#ff5a6e` | **ST TSUBAME:** a narrow needle hull, forward canards, one central fin, long swept wings, 1 large engine | \"Sora-Tek does not turn corners. Corners are informed of a change in direction.\" |\n1329\t| **VOLTA NERO** (Turin) | 9 | 4 | 4 | 5 | `#141418` / `#e8b84a` / `#c8202a` / `#ffd36a` | **VN SAETTA:** a very long needle nose, a big rear-mounted engine, small rear wings, twin low fins | \"Straight lines, beautifully. Everything else, eventually.\" |\n1330\t| **CALDERA SYSTEMS** (Santiago) | 5 | 9 | 5 | 5 | `#d8361c` / `#6a2bd8` / `#24202a` / `#ff6a2a` | **CS VOLCÁN:** a twin-boom catamaran, two big engines on the booms, a centre pilot pod | \"Geothermal engineering. Zero to everything in four seconds.\" |\n1331\t| **NULL//SET** (Berlin; a collective) | 8 | 7 | 5 | 3 | `#0b0b0e` / `#6aff3a` / `#ff2a8a` / `#6aff3a` | **N//S GHOSTLINE:** a faceted stealth wedge, no fins, 2 flat slot engines | \"No sponsor. No logo. No comment.\" |\n1332\t\n1333\tCraft geometry parameters (ShipKit), in u. Every design is 96 u long and fits inside 96 × 52 × 24 u, so all craft\n1334\tshare one collision shape (§3.2).\n1335\t\n1336\t| Craft | Hull sections (half-width w, height h at 0 / 20 / 40 / 60 / 80 / 100 % of length, nose to tail) | Wings (half-span from the centre line, sweep) | Fins | Engines (count, radius) |\n1337\t| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n1338\t| FJORD | w 2/9/14/16/14/10, h 2/6/9/9/8/6 | 24, sweep 40° | 2 canted 20°, 10 tall | 2 × r5 |\n1339\t| ANVIL | w 10/16/18/18/18/16, h 3/6/7/7/7/6, plus 2 nose pods r5 at ±14 | 22, sweep 10° (stubs) | 0 | 3 × r4 |\n1340\t| TSUBAME | w 1/6/10/12/10/8, h 2/5/7/8/7/5, plus canards (half-span 10 at 25 %) | 26, sweep 50° | 1, 14 tall | 1 × r7 |\n1341\t| SAETTA | w 1/4/8/12/14/12, h 1/4/6/8/9/8 | 20, sweep 30° (rear third) | 2 low, 6 tall | 1 × r9 |\n1342\t| VOLCÁN | two booms w 6 at ±15, a pod w 7 in the centre (front 70 %) | 24, straight, joining the booms | 2 on the booms | 2 × r7 |\n1343\t| GHOSTLINE | a faceted wedge: w 4/12/18/20/20/18, h 2/4/6/6/5/3 (flat-shaded facets) | none (the wedge is the wing) | 0 | 2 slots 14 × 3 |\n1344\t\n1345\t**Pilots** (2 per team, 12 in all). Each has two Humanoid rigs: helmeted for the race and podium cards, bare-headed\n1346\tfor portraits. Common rig options: `{ size: 1.3, build: 'heroic', weapon: null, outfit: 'coat', colors: { cloth:\n1347\tprimary, coat: secondary, pants: accent, trim: secondary, glove: accent, boot: '#1a1a20' } }` and the helmet\n1348\t`hat: { style: 'helmet', color: secondary }`. Voice `f0` is for §3.10. `skill` is an offset on the difficulty's AI\n1349\tskill.\n1350\t\n1351\t| # | Pilot | Team | Look (hair, skin) | Voice f0 | skill | aggression | Banter line |\n1352\t| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n1353\t| 1 | INGRID VALE | Kestrel | ponytail, `#f0d080` / `#f2d0b8` | 210 | +0.01 | 0.8 | \"Clean lines. Clean wins.\" |\n1354\t| 2 | TOMAS BREKKE | Kestrel | short, `#6a4a30` / `#e8c8a8` | 120 | 0 | 0.7 | \"Holding position.\" |\n1355\t| 3 | AMARA OKAFOR | Hammerhead | short, `#1a1410` / `#8a5a3a` | 200 | +0.01 | 1.0 | \"Shield's fine. Is yours?\" |\n1356\t| 4 | DAYO ADEYEMI | Hammerhead | bald / `#6a4028` | 105 | 0 | 1.2 | \"Coming through. Literally.\" |\n1357\t| 5 | RIN TAKAHARA | Sora-Tek | long, `#14141a` / `#f0d4b8` | 230 | +0.02 | 0.7 | \"Too wide. Again.\" |\n1358\t| 6 | KENJI MORI | Sora-Tek | spiky, `#202028` / `#e8c8a0` | 130 | 0 | 0.9 | \"Apex. Apex. Apex.\" |\n1359\t| 7 | LUCA FERRANTE | Volta Nero | short, `#2a1a12` / `#e0b890` | 125 | +0.02 | 1.0 | \"Watch the straight. Watch it go.\" |\n1360\t| 8 | GIULIA MARCHETTI | Volta Nero | long, `#5a3420` / `#f0c8a0` | 215 | +0.01 | 1.1 | \"Ciao. Behind you.\" |\n1361\t| 9 | VALENTINA SOTO | Caldera | ponytail, `#2a1810` / `#d8a880` | 205 | +0.01 | 1.2 | \"Hot engine. Hotter temper.\" |\n1362\t| 10 | MATEO ARAYA | Caldera | short, `#1a1008` / `#c89870` | 115 | 0 | 1.0 | \"Launching.\" |\n1363\t| 11 | KAI-ZERO | NULL//SET | hood (`hood: true`) and visor, `#0b0b0e` / `#c8b8a8` | 140, bitcrushed | +0.03 | 1.3 | \"Rookies make the best wreckage.\" |\n1364\t| 12 | HEX | NULL//SET | spiky, `#ff2a8a` / `#e8d0c0` | 175 | +0.02 | 1.2 | \"Signal lost. Yours.\" |\n1365\t\n1366\t**The race field.** The player plus 7 AI. Every team is represented, the rival is always present, and the player's\n1367\tteammate is included. AI grid order is by skill, fastest at the front. The player starts **8th, at the back**, as in\n1368\tthe source. In VERSUS the two humans start 7th and 8th.\n1369\t\n1370\t**Principals** (portraits, briefings): DIRECTOR SOLVEIG HALE (Kestrel, f0 180), CHIEF EMEKA OBI (Hammerhead, 100),\n1371\tDR. HARUKA ISE (Sora-Tek, 190), SIGNOR ARMANDO VELLUTI (Volta Nero, 110), INGENIERA PAZ ROJAS (Caldera, 170), THE ADMIN\n1372\t(NULL//SET, 90, bitcrushed; their portrait is a pixel glitch mask, a drawn function).\n1373\t\n1374\t**The rival** is KAI-ZERO, unless the player races for NULL//SET; then it is LUCA FERRANTE. Lines use `{$rival}` and\n1375\t`{$rivalTeam}` (E.Dialog vars).\n1376\t\n1377\t**ORACLE**, the Authority's race control, has as its portrait a drawn emblem: a triangle eye in a hexagon, cycling\n1378\twhite and cyan.\n1379\t\n1380\t### 4.2 Speed classes\n1381\t\n1382\t| Class | Top (m/s) | Top (u/s) | km/h | Unlock | Ideal-line lap estimate: Solenne / Karakum / Meridian / Borealis |\n1383\t| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n1384\t| SPARK | 90 | 1440 | 324 | from the start | 45.9 / 53.8 / 47.8 / 59.4 s |\n1385\t| FLARE | 115 | 1840 | 414 | Season tier 1 | 37.3 / 43.3 / 38.1 / 47.7 s |\n1386\t| STORM | 140 | 2240 | 504 | Season tier 2 | 31.8 / 36.7 / 32.2 / 40.3 s |\n1387\t| SINGULARITY | 170 | 2720 | 612 | a Grand Prix medal | 27.5 / 31.4 / 27.5 / 34.4 s |\n1388\t\n1389\tThe estimates come from the planning script (App. C): `alat = 40 m/s² × (top/90)^1.5`, thrust `0.55·top`, airbrake\n1390\tdeceleration 28 m/s², on a line about 15 % wider than the centre line. Real AI laps should land within ±25 % of\n1391\tthem, which is a test (§7). Displayed speeds with boosts reach about 830 km/h at SINGULARITY.\n1392\t\n1393\t**Medal targets** (TIME TRIAL 3 laps, HOT LAP 1 lap) are **measured, not guessed**. In M12, run\n1394\t`node tools/medals.mjs`: the player bot at skill 1.0, 3 runs per track and class, no rubber band. Then\n1395\tgold = best × 1.04, silver = × 1.10, bronze = × 1.20, rounded to 0.1 s. Write the numbers into\n1396\t`07-data-tracks.js`. The test suite checks that every medal number exists and that the bot earns gold.\n1397\t\n1398\t### 4.3 Tracks (`07-data-tracks.js`): layouts checked during planning\n1399\t\n1400\tMetres, x east, y south, z up, origin `[2048, 2048, 0]`, driving order. The `cp` indices below refer to these arrays.\n1401\t`tools/trackcheck.mjs` must reproduce the numbers in each heading. They were computed with the App. A spline at a 2 m\n1402\tresample.\n1403\t\n1404\t#### PORT SOLENNE: tier 1, beginner. 3.84 km · tightest 56 m (lighthouse hairpin) · slopes ±5 % (−15 % only inside the jump) · 1 drop jump\n1405\t\n1406\t> *Old stone, new money. The harbour lights are on a sponsorship contract.* Golden hour on a Mediterranean resort\n1407\t> city: a seafront main straight, a climb through cliff villas, a tunnel under the old town, the Harbour Step, the\n1408\t> marina, and a hairpin around the lighthouse pier.\n1409\t\n1410\t```js\n1411\tpoints: [[0,0,3],[300,0,3],[600,0,4],[790,-50,7],[890,-210,14],[905,-420,24],[820,-600,32],[640,-690,36],[420,-670,38],\n1412\t  [220,-705,36],[40,-645,30],[-110,-565,25.5],[-176,-470,23.6],[-188,-440,23.8],[-205,-375,15],[-195,-250,10],[-255,-120,6],\n1413\t  [-320,60,4],[-300,260,3],[-200,340,3],[-100,280,3],[-80,120,3],[-40,35,3]],\n1414\twidth: 28, widths: { 18: 30, 19: 30, 20: 30 }, start: 230,   // widths: per control point, metres (the hairpin is wider)\n1415\tjumps: [{ from: 12, to: 14, kind: 'drop', name: 'THE HARBOUR STEP' }],   // lip 23.6 m, lower deck 15.0 m: an 8.6 m step, 0.65 s air at every speed\n1416\ttunnels: [{ a: { cp: 7, d: 30 }, b: { cp: 9, d: 40 }, style: 'stone' }],  // under the old town, about 436 m\n1417\tspeedPads: [{ cp: 1, d: 120, u: 0 }, { cp: 4, d: 80, u: -4 }, { cp: 10, d: 80, u: 3 }, { cp: 16, d: 100, u: 0 }, { cp: 21, d: 30, u: -3 }],\n1418\tweaponPads: [{ cp: 2, d: 80 }, { cp: 7, d: -60 }, { cp: 11, d: 40 }, { cp: 17, d: 60 }],\n1419\tpit: { a: { cp: 0, d: 20 }, b: { cp: 1, d: 259 }, side: 'right', w: 8 },   // sea side of the main straight\n1420\topenEdges: [], banks: [],\n1421\t```\n1422\t\n1423\tControl points along the track (m, raw from cp0): 0, 302, 602, 800, 992, 1204, 1406, 1610, 1832, 2036, 2226, 2398,\n1424\t2514, 2546, 2614, 2740, 2884, 3076, 3280, 3412, 3532, 3696, 3790.\n1425\t\n1426\t- **Theme `coast`:**\n1427\t  - sky `['#2a1a4a', '#c8506a', '#ffb070']`;\n1428\t  - sun low in the west (`dir [-0.8, 0.3, -0.35]`, `#ffc890`, 2.4);\n1429\t  - ambient `['#ffd0c0', '#4a3a5a', 1.6]`;\n1430\t  - fog `#e89878`, near 12000 u, far 26000 u.\n1431\t- **Terrain:** the sea to the south (local y > 60: height −4 m, under a water plane at 0 m with gradient bands and a\n1432\t  sun-glint strip), a beach, then hills rising north to 120 m (noise). The old town plateau covers the tunnel at about\n1433\t  55 m.\n1434\t- **Scenery:**\n1435\t  - the promenade with 60 palm pylons and 14 sponsor boards along the main straight;\n1436\t  - crowd stands at the start;\n1437\t  - a glass pit building;\n1438\t  - 300 old-town houses (white, ochre and pink boxes with terracotta roofs) on the hill;\n1439\t  - cliff villas with pools;\n1440\t  - harbour cranes;\n1441\t  - 40 marina boats (hull and mast);\n1442\t  - the lighthouse on the pier (red and white rings, a rotating beam light, a landmark for the hairpin);\n1443\t  - a Ferris wheel turning slowly behind the marina;\n1444\t  - beach umbrellas;\n1445\t  - the landmark arch \"SOLENNE 2161\" at cp3.\n1446\t- **Music:** `solenne`.\n1447\t\n1448\t#### KARAKUM SPIRE: tier 1, intermediate. 4.59 km · tightest 55 m · a gorge **gap** jump · a spiral that passes over its own track (24.5 m clearance)\n1449\t\n1450\t> *A canyon the colour of rust, a spire nobody climbs, and a gorge that keeps what it catches.* Noon in a red-rock\n1451\t> desert: canyon-floor straights, a plateau with an open edge, the gorge jump (it needs 270 km/h), a tunnel through a\n1452\t> mesa, a 28°-banked spiral climbing around the Spire, over its own entry, and a long dive home.\n1453\t\n1454\t```js\n1455\tpoints: [[0,0,0],[0,-330,0],[30,-575,2],[130,-740,8],[295,-820,18],[490,-820,29],[620,-778,32],[720,-712,36.5],[742,-696,37.5],\n1456\t  [765,-680,28],[840,-610,21],[905,-525,16],[935,-360,11],[905,-195,9],[885,-65,7],[870,65,9],[790,165,15],[675,130,21],[655,15,26],\n1457\t  [740,-50,30],[855,-50,32],[985,30,30],[1035,180,22],[945,310,14],[740,355,8],[490,345,4],[245,345,2],[50,295,0],[-25,165,0]],\n1458\twidth: 26, start: 200,\n1459\tjumps: [{ from: 7, to: 9, kind: 'gap', name: 'THE GORGE', minSpeed: 75 }],   // cp8 is a virtual apex inside the gap (not drawn); 57 m gap\n1460\ttunnels: [{ a: { cp: 11, d: 60 }, b: { cp: 13, d: 40 }, style: 'rock' }],   // through the mesa, about 316 m\n1461\tspeedPads: [{ cp: 2, d: 40, u: 0 }, { cp: 6, d: 40, u: -3 }, { cp: 6, d: 80, u: 3 }, { cp: 13, d: 60, u: 0 }, { cp: 20, d: 40, u: 0 }, { cp: 24, d: 120, u: -4 }],\n1462\tweaponPads: [{ cp: 3, d: 40 }, { cp: 10, d: 60 }, { cp: 14, d: 60 }, { cp: 22, d: 60 }, { cp: 26, d: 60 }],\n1463\tpit: { a: { cp: 0, d: 10 }, b: { cp: 1, d: 0 }, side: 'left', w: 8 },\n1464\topenEdges: [{ a: { cp: 5, d: 0 }, b: { cp: 6, d: 60 }, side: 'left' }],   // the plateau rim: fall into the canyon\n1465\tbanks: [{ from: 15, to: 20, deg: 28 }],                                    // the Spire spiral\n1466\t```\n1467\t\n1468\tControl points along the track: 0, 330, 578, 773, 958, 1155, 1292, 1412 (lip), 1439 (virtual), 1469 (far edge),\n1469\t1572, 1680, 1848, 2016, 2148, 2279, 2411, 2536, 2657, 2767, 2883, 3038, 3200, 3362, 3574, 3825, 4070, 4274, 4427.\n1470\t\n1471\t**Overpass:** raw s ≈ 2208 (lower, under the spiral exit) and ≈ 2928 (upper). **Gorge** (App. C):\n1472\t- 45–60 m/s hit the far wall: a rescue;\n1473\t- 75 m/s just clears;\n1474\t- 90 m/s lands 18 m past the far edge at −13°;\n1475\t- 170 m/s lands 129 m past at −10°.\n1476\t\n1477\t- **Theme `desert`:**\n1478\t  - sky `['#3a78d8', '#9cc8f0', '#f0e0c0']`;\n1479\t  - sun high (`[-0.3, 0.2, -0.93]`, `#fff2d0`, 3.0);\n1480\t  - fog `#e8d0a0`, near 14000, far 30000.\n1481\t- **Terrain:** a meandering canyon floor along the low sections, mesas (flat tops 40–80 m with strata walls: World3D\n1482\t  `rock: { colors: ['#b85a30', '#d8884a', '#8a3a20', '#e8b070'], band: 48 }`), the gorge cut −60 m under the jump with\n1483\t  a thin river (an emissive blue strip), and dunes outside.\n1484\t- **Scenery:**\n1485\t  - **the Spire:** a 220 m stacked rock column at local (762, 72) inside the spiral (tapering cylinders, strata\n1486\t    colours);\n1487\t  - 24 wind turbines with turning rotors on the plateaus;\n1488\t  - solar fields;\n1489\t  - carved mesa portals;\n1490\t  - canyon-wall banners;\n1491\t  - a half-buried old craft wreck as a landmark at the gorge;\n1492\t  - dust devils (particles);\n1493\t  - heat haze.\n1494\t- **Music:** `karakum`.\n1495\t\n1496\t#### MERIDIAN STACK: tier 2, advanced. 4.18 km · tightest 52 m · the Stack **drop** · a figure-eight crossover (31.9 m clearance) · night\n1497\t\n1498\t> *Three hundred storeys of people who have never seen the ground. Tonight they watch you fall past their windows.* A\n1499\t> vertical megacity at night: an elevated start, the Stack Drop between towers, neon tunnels through buildings, a low\n1500\t> pass under its own upper deck, and a long climb back to the sky deck.\n1501\t\n1502\t```js\n1503\tpoints: [[0,0,42],[250,-40,42],[480,-160,40],[615,-300,37],[650,-395,36.2],[653,-425,36.4],[655,-490,22],[630,-585,17],\n1504\t  [460,-700,15],[240,-680,13],[100,-540,11],[0,-360,10],[-100,-180,10],[-260,-40,12],[-480,0,18],[-680,-80,24],[-780,-280,30],\n1505\t  [-700,-480,36],[-500,-560,40],[-300,-480,42],[-160,-300,42],[-60,-120,42]],\n1506\twidth: 24, start: 190,\n1507\tjumps: [{ from: 4, to: 6, kind: 'drop', name: 'THE STACK DROP' }],   // cp5 virtual; lip 36.2 m to a lower deck at 22.0 m: a 14.2 m step\n1508\ttunnels: [{ a: { cp: 8, d: 20 }, b: { cp: 9, d: 80 }, style: 'neon' }, { a: { cp: 13, d: 50 }, b: { cp: 14, d: 40 }, style: 'neon' }],\n1509\tspeedPads: [{ cp: 1, d: 60, u: 0 }, { cp: 3, d: 50, u: 0 }, { cp: 10, d: 80, u: 3 }, { cp: 12, d: 30, u: 0 }, { cp: 17, d: 60, u: -3 }, { cp: 20, d: 60, u: 0 }],\n1510\tweaponPads: [{ cp: 2, d: 40 }, { cp: 7, d: 60 }, { cp: 12, d: 120 }, { cp: 15, d: 60 }, { cp: 19, d: -40 }],\n1511\tpit: { a: { cp: 19, d: 35 }, b: { cp: 20, d: 126 }, side: 'right', w: 8 },   // on the sky deck, ending before the crossover\n1512\topenEdges: [], banks: [],\n1513\t```\n1514\t\n1515\tControl points along the track: 0, 258, 518, 714, 815 (lip), 846 (virtual), 912 (far edge), 1012, 1220, 1446, 1646,\n1516\t1852, 2058, 2272, 2498, 2718, 2946, 3165, 3385, 3605, 3833, 4039.\n1517\t\n1518\t**Overpass:** raw s ≈ 2082 (low, z ≈ 10 m) under s ≈ 3983 (high, z ≈ 42 m). **The drop** (App. C): every speed\n1519\tlands. Slow craft land hard (45 m/s: −37°, damage); fast ones smoothly (140 m/s: −12°). The drop sits on a 19°\n1520\tcurve, so the lower deck follows the plan path (§3.1).\n1521\t\n1522\t- **Theme `city`:**\n1523\t  - sky `['#05030f', '#1a0f3a', '#3a1a5a']`;\n1524\t  - moonlight `#8090ff`, 0.5;\n1525\t  - ambient `['#3a3a8a', '#100818', 1.0]`;\n1526\t  - fog `#1a1035`, near 6000, far 22000;\n1527\t  - bloom strong.\n1528\t- **Terrain:** flat street level at −40 m, dark concrete.\n1529\t- **Scenery:**\n1530\t  - 260 megatowers (60–350 m, window-grid emissive textures in three palettes);\n1531\t  - neon signs and holo billboards (hue-cycling) with the sponsor list;\n1532\t  - maglev rails with trains moving on loops;\n1533\t  - sweeping searchlights;\n1534\t  - flying traffic lanes (small emissive craft on paths);\n1535\t  - **the Meridian Spire** (a 500 m tower with a beacon) next to the crossover;\n1536\t  - rooftop helipads with blinking lights;\n1537\t  - light rain.\n1538\t- **Music:** `meridian`.\n1539\t\n1540\t#### BOREALIS VAULT: tier 3, expert. 5.03 km · tightest 44 m (switchbacks) · climbs to +11 % · the Vault **drop** (17.2 m) · a 490 m ice tunnel\n1541\t\n1542\t> *Minus forty, plus aurora. The Authority recommends not stopping.* An arctic research basin at night: a station\n1543\t> plateau start, sweeping descents, the Vault drop, the ice tunnel, a frozen lake with an open edge, and a brutal\n1544\t> switchback climb under the aurora.\n1545\t\n1546\t```js\n1547\tpoints: [[0,0,110],[-350,0,110],[-650,60,104],[-850,220,92],[-905,420,80],[-892,478,76.5],[-878,524,77.2],[-870,552,77.6],\n1548\t  [-852,612,60],[-800,690,53],[-600,770,47],[-380,800,38],[-150,760,30],[60,820,22],[260,950,14],[480,1000,10],[700,960,10],\n1549\t  [880,860,12],[1000,700,18],[1020,520,30],[930,380,44],[1000,250,58],[900,120,72],[720,140,84],[560,60,96],[380,0,106],[190,-15,110]],\n1550\twidth: 26, start: 200,\n1551\tjumps: [{ from: 6, to: 8, kind: 'drop', name: 'THE VAULT' }],   // cp7 virtual; lip 77.2 m, lower deck 60.0 m; a ski-jump lip at +1.7 %\n1552\ttunnels: [{ a: { cp: 12, d: 30 }, b: { cp: 14, d: 60 }, style: 'ice' }],\n1553\tspeedPads: [{ cp: 2, d: 40, u: 0 }, { cp: 5, d: 15, u: 0 }, { cp: 10, d: 80, u: -3 }, { cp: 15, d: 100, u: 0 }, { cp: 24, d: 60, u: 3 }, { cp: 26, d: 80, u: 0 }],\n1554\tweaponPads: [{ cp: 3, d: 40 }, { cp: 11, d: 60 }, { cp: 14, d: 100 }, { cp: 17, d: 40 }, { cp: 22, d: 40 }],\n1555\tpit: { a: { cp: 0, d: 30 }, b: { cp: 1, d: -10 }, side: 'left', w: 8 },\n1556\topenEdges: [{ a: { cp: 15, d: 0 }, b: { cp: 16, d: 100 }, side: 'right' }],   // the frozen lake\n1557\tbanks: [{ from: 19, to: 22, deg: 26 }],                                        // the switchbacks\n1558\t```\n1559\t\n1560\tControl points along the track: 0, 350, 658, 918, 1126, 1186, 1234 (lip), 1264 (virtual), 1330 (far edge), 1424,\n1561\t1642, 1864, 2098, 2318, 2558, 2784, 3010, 3216, 3418, 3602, 3772, 3924, 4094, 4278, 4458, 4648, 4840.\n1562\t\n1563\t**The Vault** (App. C): slow craft land hard (45 m/s: −40°); 115–170 m/s land 31–111 m past the far edge at −12 to\n1564\t−15°. Air time is about 1.0–1.2 s, room for two rolls.\n1565\t\n1566\t- **Theme `arctic`:**\n1567\t  - sky `['#020814', '#0a2a4a', '#1a4a6a']`;\n1568\t  - moon `#a0c8ff`, 0.9;\n1569\t  - fog `#9ab8d8`, near 9000, far 26000.\n1570\t- **Terrain:** snowy ridges (`E.noise2` octaves), a glacier valley, the frozen lake (flat at 8 m) around local\n1571\t  (480, 1000), and dark rock strata on the steep parts.\n1572\t- **Scenery:**\n1573\t  - the research station at the start (domes, a radar dish turning, masts with blinking red lights);\n1574\t  - ice spikes;\n1575\t  - **aurora ribbons:** 5 tall translucent emissive strips, animated in waves, high in the sky;\n1576\t  - snowfall near the camera;\n1577\t  - the ice tunnel (translucent blue walls with inner glow);\n1578\t  - lake cracks (decals);\n1579\t  - a frozen-in icebreaker ship as the landmark.\n1580\t- **Music:** `borealis`.\n1581\t\n1582\t**Grid, sectors, records:** automatic (§3.1). **Overclock skin:** any track (§3.7).\n1583\t\n1584\t### 4.4 Weapon icons and pickup look\n1585\t\n1586\t24 × 24 pixel icons (`E.sprite` strings or px drawing, shaded with `E.tones`), each in its §3.4 colour on a dark\n1587\trounded tile:\n1588\t\n1589\t| Icon | Drawing |\n1590\t| --- | --- |\n1591\t| SWARM | three small rockets fanned |\n1592\t| SEEKER | a missile inside a target ring |\n1593\t| MINEFIELD | a spiked disc |\n1594\t| CANNON | three tracer dashes |\n1595\t| RAILSHOT | crosshairs with a long beam to the right |\n1596\t| TREMOR | a sine wave over a ground line |\n1597\t| BULWARK | a hexagon shield |\n1598\t| AUTOPILOT | a steering yoke with an \"A\" |\n1599\t| NITRO | a double flame chevron |\n1600\t| SIPHON | a zigzag arrow into a droplet |\n1601\t\n1602\tThe same icons go on the How to Play pages and in the dev panel's Give weapon. In 3D, the weapon pad's sigil is the\n1603\tamber triangle. The HUD shows the icon.\n1604\t\n1605\t### 4.5 Season events, story beats, academy drills, radio (`08-data-season.js`, `09-data-story.js`)\n1606\t\n1607\tSpeakers: **ORACLE** (the Authority), **PRINCIPAL** (the player's team's principal), **RIVAL** (`{$rival}`), and\n1608\t**PILOT** (`{$pilot}`, the player). Briefings play before an event's first attempt (then from the event tile's\n1609\tBRIEFING button). Debriefs play after a result. Each line is one dialog page with a portrait and a gibberish voice.\n1610\t✕ advances, △ skips all.\n1611\t\n1612\t| # | Tier / class | Event | Track | Target (gold / silver / bronze) | Briefing → debrief beats |\n1613\t| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n1614\t| — | Season open | PROLOGUE (first entry) | — | — | ORACLE: \"AUTHORITY NOTICE 0417. ROOKIE LICENCE GRANTED. CLASS: SPARK. GRAVITY: OPTIONAL.\" · PRINCIPAL: \"Welcome to {$team}. Your test laps were adequate. Adequate is where champions start.\" · PRINCIPAL: \"Bring back three medals and the Authority lets you go faster.\" · RIVAL: \"Another rookie. I'll learn your name when I need it for the wreck report.\" |\n1615\t| E1 | 1 · SPARK | ACADEMY | Port Solenne | all drills first try / ≤ 3 retries / completed | ORACLE: \"ELEVEN DRILLS. REPEAT EACH UNTIL COMPLIANT.\" → ORACLE: \"TRAINING RECORD FILED. YOU MAY NOW RACE OTHER PEOPLE.\" |\n1616\t| E2 | 1 · SPARK | RACE 3 laps | Port Solenne | 1st / 2nd / 3rd | PRINCIPAL: \"Port Solenne. Wide, forgiving, full of yachts. Win, and the sponsors notice.\" → win: \"First place. The harbour lights flashed our colours. That was contractual.\" / podium: \"A podium. Keep the trophy dust-free; we photograph it.\" / else: \"Finishing is a habit. So is losing. Choose.\" |\n1617\t| E3 | 1 · SPARK | TIME TRIAL 3 laps | Karakum Spire | medal times | PRINCIPAL: \"No weapons, no excuses. The gorge wants two hundred and seventy kilometres an hour. Arrive with them.\" → \"The clock has accepted your apology.\" |\n1618\t| E4 | 1 · SPARK | RACE 3 laps | Karakum Spire | 1st / 2nd / 3rd | RIVAL: \"Karakum has a gorge. Most rookies meet the bottom of it.\" · PRINCIPAL: \"Ignore {$rival}. Take the speed pads before the ramp.\" → win: RIVAL: \"Luck. Statistically you're due a wall.\" |"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4110026b-2798-4dbf-ae8a-e81d8e816e30","uuid":"bb5aa981-93a8-4016-a442-da6ef19470c0","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:47:08.735Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261103-184630__xa320fb/work/PLAN.md","content":"\n**Local (the game on its own): VERSUS for 2 players on one machine.**\n- On the VERSUS screen, `game.allowJoin({ max: 2 })`: player 2 presses Start on another pad, or 2 on the keyboard.\n- With two on the keyboard, the engine splits it with `Input.halfKeys` in our preset order (§3.9):\n  - **P1:** W/S pitch, A/D steer, F thrust, G fire, H absorb, R/T airbrakes, Y camera, V/B side-shift;\n  - **P2:** ↑/↓ pitch, ←/→ steer, `.` (Numpad 1) thrust, `/` (Numpad 2) fire, `,` (Numpad 3) absorb, L / `;`\n    (Numpad 4/5) airbrakes, `'` (Numpad 6) camera, K / M (Numpad 7/8) side-shift.\n\n  Both airbrakes together brake (`brake` and `lookBack` get no key in a half). Show both layouts on the join screen\n  with keycap glyphs, read from `players[i].label()`, never typed in by hand.\n- Both pick teams in turn, then choose RACE or SNIPEOUT, class and track. Split rows, with a compact HUD per\n  viewport.\n- Each player's prompts use their own device (`players[i].label()`). A pause says \"P2 PAUSED\" (engine).\n\n**AI Hub (`90-hub.js`): mode `ghost`**, following the protocol (`lib/hub/README.md`, client 1.4.0). Everyone races the\nsame seeded event on their own device and sees the others as ghosts.\n1. **Tags** in `<head>` (§2.3): players `1-4`, mode `ghost`, minutes `3`, goal and howto ≤ 60/80 characters.\n2. **`AIHub.active`** → the boot goes straight to the `session` scene: no title, menus, attract or prompts. The engine\n   options for the session: `autoPause: false`, the race `pausable: false`, `menu.quit: false`.\n3. `const info = await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'ghost', seats: [1, 4], card: true })`. If `null`, run the game normally.\n4. **The event:**\n   - track = `['solenne', 'karakum', 'meridian', 'borealis'][floor(AIHub.rng('event')() * 4)]`;\n   - class FLARE, 3 laps;\n   - race seed = `floor(AIHub.rng('race')() * 2^32)`;\n   - each human's team by seat (`['kestrel', 'soratek', 'volta', 'caldera'][seat]`), livery accent = seat colour;\n   - grid: the humans take slots by seat at the back of the grid (slots 5–8), and AI fill slots 1–4 plus any free\n     slots (8 − N AI);\n   - every copy simulates its own craft plus the AI. The other humans are **ghosts**: drawn from messages, never\n     collided with or targeted.\n5. **Own card** (`card: true`): the session scene shows a 3D grid shot of the chosen track with the players' craft\n   lined up in seat colours, the names, the ready ticks from the `card` event, the time left (`left`), the goal, and\n   this player's controls (the glyphs of the device seen so far, keyboard by default).\n   - **Ready:** Enter, ✕ or a tap/click on READY → `AIHub.answer('ready')`.\n   - **More time:** △, M, or a tap/click on MORE TIME → `AIHub.answer('more')`; pressing again takes it back.\n   - No `Math.random` on the card (use `AIHub.rng('card')` if needed). No menus or choices.\n6. Call `AIHub.ready()` once, as soon as the world is built and warm (boot plus the track loading), with no key press.\n7. **`start`**: the countdown lights follow `AIHub.time()` (−3000 → 0 ms), and the launch revs work. Racing begins\n   when `AIHub.time() ≥ 0`. The race clock is `AIHub.time()`.\n8. **Ghost traffic:** `AIHub.send({ t: 'g', p, u, h, y, r, v, lap, fin }, { reliable: false })` at 10 Hz (well under\n   20/s), plus `{ t: 'done', ms }` reliable on finishing.\n   - On `message`, update that ghost: interpolate toward the latest, 0.1 s behind. Draw it as a ghost craft (§3.7)\n     with the name in the seat colour, and add it to the HUD standings.\n   - On `leave`, remove it.\n9. **Progress:** about once a second, `AIHub.progress({ score: Math.round(p / 16), label: 'LAP 2/3 · 3RD' })`.\n10. **Result:**\n    - on finishing: `AIHub.result({ time: finishMs, stats: { 'Best lap': '0:41.22', 'Place vs AI': '2nd' },\n      awards: [...] })`;\n    - eliminations respawn in sessions, so everyone can finish;\n    - on `time-up`, if not finished: `AIHub.result({ score: Math.round(p / 16) })` at once.\n11. **`end`:** stop the sim, stop all input (ignore `game.input`), stop music, engine hums and SFX, and show \"ROUND\n    OVER\" with the standings from the event. The hub removes the page.\n12. **Rules:** network only through the hub (the CDN module loads are the game's own files); no `alert`, `confirm`,\n    `prompt` or `window.open` (none anywhere in the game); no chat or custom names. Restart and quit do nothing in a\n    session (the items are hidden).\n\n### 3.17 Settings: the game's own, beside the engine's standard ones\n\n`new E.Game({ menu: { settings: [...] } })`, groups `Game` and `Display`:\n- **Difficulty:** Easy / Normal / Hard.\n- **Speed units:** km/h / mph.\n- **Default camera:** Chase / Far chase / Cockpit.\n- **HUD size:** Normal / Large (×1.25).\n- **Subtitles:** on / off. They cover the announcer and radio; dialog boxes are always text.\n- **Announcer voice:** on / off.\n- **Speed lines:** on / off.\n- **Neon glow** (`bloom`): on / off.\n- **Picture** (`picture3d`): PIXELS (the engine's native default) / BALANCED / **HD**. HD is World3D's `'full'`.\n- **Shadows** (`shadows3d`): on / off.\n- **Filter** (`filter3d`): None / Comic cel / Pixel.\n- **Button symbols:** PlayStation (default) / Xbox. This is the engine's `glyphs`, moved to Display (§2.7.1).\n\nWorld3D reads `picture3d`, `shadows3d` and `filter3d` by those keys. Define them ourselves (same keys, values and\nlabels), because `E.World3D.SETTINGS` does not exist yet when `new E.Game` runs (§2.3). The engine provides the rest:\nvolume, music, effects, reduce motion, shake, flashes, full screen, frame rate, and the Controls screen (rebinding,\ndead zone, vibration).\n\n### 3.18 About / Credits and the exit interview (`11-data-about.js`)\n\n`SN.ABOUT` is the single source for the **About / Credits** screen (OPTIONS ▸ ABOUT, and after the ending credits) and\nfor `tools/exit-interview.mjs`, which writes `../exit-interview.json` in exactly TASK.md's shape and checks it parses.\n\nThe screen pages (L1/R1), each page big-type and short:\n1. **SOURCE INFORMATION:** every TASK.md field, \"unknown\" where it can't be confirmed. Planned values:\n   - Date: 2026-11-03 17:47:28\n   - Source: Wipeout HD (Studio Liverpool / Sony, 2008)\n   - Plan: PLAN.md\n   - Genre and perspective: anti-gravity combat racing; third-person chase camera with cockpit view and trackside TV\n     cameras\n   - Tech: my-3D2dge v0.85.2 handoff engine + my-3D2dge 3D v0.85.2, three.js r182 (WebGPU/WebGL 2), Rapier 0.19.3,\n     AI Hub client 1.4.0\n   - Art direction: the engine's native style (pixel-resolution 3D, toon/lambert light, pixel HUD and fonts) plus new\n     procedural craft, tracks and neon\n   - Animation: the engine's rigs and tweens, plus procedural craft animation\n   - Audio: synthesized music, SFX and gibberish voices\n   - Online: AI Hub ghost sessions; local split screen\n   - Testing; research; environment; model; usage\n2. **TESTING FEEDBACK:** the 4 answers.\n3. **ENGINE FEEDBACK:** the 6 answers, including the §2.7 changes.\n4. **PROMPT FEEDBACK:** the 4 answers.\n5. **CREDITS:**\n   - \"Snipeout HD. An original game inspired by Wipeout HD (not affiliated with Sony Interactive Entertainment).\"\n   - Engine credits (my-3D2dge, three.js MIT, Rapier Apache-2.0), \"all music, sound and voices synthesized in code\",\n     \"built by Anthropic claude-opus-5-5\".\n   - The fictional teams and artists, with a note that they are fictional.\n\nThe builder fills in the feedback answers truthfully at the end of the build (M12). The chat reply repeats them, as\nTASK.md demands. The `aiHub` block for the exit interview:\n\n```json\n{ \"name\": \"Snipeout HD\", \"tagline\": \"Anti-gravity. Anti-everyone.\",\n  \"description\": \"An anti-gravity combat racer: thread banked neon tracks at 600 km/h, snipe rivals with ten weapons and survive Overclock. Season, time trials, split screen and AI Hub ghost races.\",\n  \"type\": \"Game\", \"genre\": \"Racing\", \"source\": \"Wipeout HD\", \"series\": \"Wipeout\", \"players\": \"1–4\",\n  \"controls\": \"Stick or A/D steer · ✕ or W thrust · L2/R2 or Q/E airbrakes · □ or Space fire · ○ or Shift absorb\",\n  \"tags\": [\"3d\", \"racing\", \"sci-fi\", \"vehicles\", \"arcade\", \"versus\"] }\n```\n\n---\n\n## 4. Content\n\n### 4.1 Teams, craft, pilots, principals (`05-data-teams.js`)\n\nStats run 1–10 (§3.2 turns them into physics). The totals are close (22–24). NULL//SET trades shield for speed, which\nmakes it the rival.\n\n| Team (base) | SPD | THR | HND | SHD | Livery: primary / secondary / accent / engine glow | Craft and silhouette | One-line copy |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **KESTREL DYNAMICS** (Oslo) | 6 | 6 | 6 | 6 | `#f2f5f8` / `#29c8e8` / `#1a2a4a` / `#7af0ff` | **KD-9 FJORD:** a dart hull, swept delta wings, twin canted tail fins, 2 engines | \"Precision is a form of courage. Kestrel has been brave since 2109.\" |\n| **HAMMERHEAD HEAVY INDUSTRIES** (Lagos) | 6 | 4 | 3 | 9 | `#ff7a1a` / `#2b2d33` / `#ffd23f` / `#ffb347` | **HH ANVIL:** a wide flat slab hull, twin hammerhead nose pods, stub wings, 3 engines | \"Builds cranes, bridges and the occasional champion. All three survive impact.\" |\n| **SORA-TEK** (Osaka) | 5 | 6 | 9 | 4 | `#f7f7f7` / `#e0213a` / `#16161c` / `#ff5a6e` | **ST TSUBAME:** a narrow needle hull, forward canards, one central fin, long swept wings, 1 large engine | \"Sora-Tek does not turn corners. Corners are informed of a change in direction.\" |\n| **VOLTA NERO** (Turin) | 9 | 4 | 4 | 5 | `#141418` / `#e8b84a` / `#c8202a` / `#ffd36a` | **VN SAETTA:** a very long needle nose, a big rear-mounted engine, small rear wings, twin low fins | \"Straight lines, beautifully. Everything else, eventually.\" |\n| **CALDERA SYSTEMS** (Santiago) | 5 | 9 | 5 | 5 | `#d8361c` / `#6a2bd8` / `#24202a` / `#ff6a2a` | **CS VOLCÁN:** a twin-boom catamaran, two big engines on the booms, a centre pilot pod | \"Geothermal engineering. Zero to everything in four seconds.\" |\n| **NULL//SET** (Berlin; a collective) | 8 | 7 | 5 | 3 | `#0b0b0e` / `#6aff3a` / `#ff2a8a` / `#6aff3a` | **N//S GHOSTLINE:** a faceted stealth wedge, no fins, 2 flat slot engines | \"No sponsor. No logo. No comment.\" |\n\nCraft geometry parameters (ShipKit), in u. Every design is 96 u long and fits inside 96 × 52 × 24 u, so all craft\nshare one collision shape (§3.2).\n\n| Craft | Hull sections (half-width w, height h at 0 / 20 / 40 / 60 / 80 / 100 % of length, nose to tail) | Wings (half-span from the centre line, sweep) | Fins | Engines (count, radius) |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| FJORD | w 2/9/14/16/14/10, h 2/6/9/9/8/6 | 24, sweep 40° | 2 canted 20°, 10 tall | 2 × r5 |\n| ANVIL | w 10/16/18/18/18/16, h 3/6/7/7/7/6, plus 2 nose pods r5 at ±14 | 22, sweep 10° (stubs) | 0 | 3 × r4 |\n| TSUBAME | w 1/6/10/12/10/8, h 2/5/7/8/7/5, plus canards (half-span 10 at 25 %) | 26, sweep 50° | 1, 14 tall | 1 × r7 |\n| SAETTA | w 1/4/8/12/14/12, h 1/4/6/8/9/8 | 20, sweep 30° (rear third) | 2 low, 6 tall | 1 × r9 |\n| VOLCÁN | two booms w 6 at ±15, a pod w 7 in the centre (front 70 %) | 24, straight, joining the booms | 2 on the booms | 2 × r7 |\n| GHOSTLINE | a faceted wedge: w 4/12/18/20/20/18, h 2/4/6/6/5/3 (flat-shaded facets) | none (the wedge is the wing) | 0 | 2 slots 14 × 3 |\n\n**Pilots** (2 per team, 12 in all). Each has two Humanoid rigs: helmeted for the race and podium cards, bare-headed\nfor portraits. Common rig options: `{ size: 1.3, build: 'heroic', weapon: null, outfit: 'coat', colors: { cloth:\nprimary, coat: secondary, pants: accent, trim: secondary, glove: accent, boot: '#1a1a20' } }` and the helmet\n`hat: { style: 'helmet', color: secondary }`. Voice `f0` is for §3.10. `skill` is an offset on the difficulty's AI\nskill.\n\n| # | Pilot | Team | Look (hair, skin) | Voice f0 | skill | aggression | Banter line |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | INGRID VALE | Kestrel | ponytail, `#f0d080` / `#f2d0b8` | 210 | +0.01 | 0.8 | \"Clean lines. Clean wins.\" |\n| 2 | TOMAS BREKKE | Kestrel | short, `#6a4a30` / `#e8c8a8` | 120 | 0 | 0.7 | \"Holding position.\" |\n| 3 | AMARA OKAFOR | Hammerhead | short, `#1a1410` / `#8a5a3a` | 200 | +0.01 | 1.0 | \"Shield's fine. Is yours?\" |\n| 4 | DAYO ADEYEMI | Hammerhead | bald / `#6a4028` | 105 | 0 | 1.2 | \"Coming through. Literally.\" |\n| 5 | RIN TAKAHARA | Sora-Tek | long, `#14141a` / `#f0d4b8` | 230 | +0.02 | 0.7 | \"Too wide. Again.\" |\n| 6 | KENJI MORI | Sora-Tek | spiky, `#202028` / `#e8c8a0` | 130 | 0 | 0.9 | \"Apex. Apex. Apex.\" |\n| 7 | LUCA FERRANTE | Volta Nero | short, `#2a1a12` / `#e0b890` | 125 | +0.02 | 1.0 | \"Watch the straight. Watch it go.\" |\n| 8 | GIULIA MARCHETTI | Volta Nero | long, `#5a3420` / `#f0c8a0` | 215 | +0.01 | 1.1 | \"Ciao. Behind you.\" |\n| 9 | VALENTINA SOTO | Caldera | ponytail, `#2a1810` / `#d8a880` | 205 | +0.01 | 1.2 | \"Hot engine. Hotter temper.\" |\n| 10 | MATEO ARAYA | Caldera | short, `#1a1008` / `#c89870` | 115 | 0 | 1.0 | \"Launching.\" |\n| 11 | KAI-ZERO | NULL//SET | hood (`hood: true`) and visor, `#0b0b0e` / `#c8b8a8` | 140, bitcrushed | +0.03 | 1.3 | \"Rookies make the best wreckage.\" |\n| 12 | HEX | NULL//SET | spiky, `#ff2a8a` / `#e8d0c0` | 175 | +0.02 | 1.2 | \"Signal lost. Yours.\" |\n\n**The race field.** The player plus 7 AI. Every team is represented, the rival is always present, and the player's\nteammate is included. AI grid order is by skill, fastest at the front. The player starts **8th, at the back**, as in\nthe source. In VERSUS the two humans start 7th and 8th.\n\n**Principals** (portraits, briefings): DIRECTOR SOLVEIG HALE (Kestrel, f0 180), CHIEF EMEKA OBI (Hammerhead, 100),\nDR. HARUKA ISE (Sora-Tek, 190), SIGNOR ARMANDO VELLUTI (Volta Nero, 110), INGENIERA PAZ ROJAS (Caldera, 170), THE ADMIN\n(NULL//SET, 90, bitcrushed; their portrait is a pixel glitch mask, a drawn function).\n\n**The rival** is KAI-ZERO, unless the player races for NULL//SET; then it is LUCA FERRANTE. Lines use `{$rival}` and\n`{$rivalTeam}` (E.Dialog vars).\n\n**ORACLE**, the Authority's race control, has as its portrait a drawn emblem: a triangle eye in a hexagon, cycling\nwhite and cyan.\n\n### 4.2 Speed classes\n\n| Class | Top (m/s) | Top (u/s) | km/h | Unlock | Ideal-line lap estimate: Solenne / Karakum / Meridian / Borealis |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| SPARK | 90 | 1440 | 324 | from the start | 45.9 / 53.8 / 47.8 / 59.4 s |\n| FLARE | 115 | 1840 | 414 | Season tier 1 | 37.3 / 43.3 / 38.1 / 47.7 s |\n| STORM | 140 | 2240 | 504 | Season tier 2 | 31.8 / 36.7 / 32.2 / 40.3 s |\n| SINGULARITY | 170 | 2720 | 612 | a Grand Prix medal | 27.5 / 31.4 / 27.5 / 34.4 s |\n\nThe estimates come from the planning script (App. C): `alat = 40 m/s² × (top/90)^1.5`, thrust `0.55·top`, airbrake\ndeceleration 28 m/s², on a line about 15 % wider than the centre line. Real AI laps should land within ±25 % of\nthem, which is a test (§7). Displayed speeds with boosts reach about 830 km/h at SINGULARITY.\n\n**Medal targets** (TIME TRIAL 3 laps, HOT LAP 1 lap) are **measured, not guessed**. In M12, run\n`node tools/medals.mjs`: the player bot at skill 1.0, 3 runs per track and class, no rubber band. Then\ngold = best × 1.04, silver = × 1.10, bronze = × 1.20, rounded to 0.1 s. Write the numbers into\n`07-data-tracks.js`. The test suite checks that every medal number exists and that the bot earns gold.\n\n### 4.3 Tracks (`07-data-tracks.js`): layouts checked during planning\n\nMetres, x east, y south, z up, origin `[2048, 2048, 0]`, driving order. The `cp` indices below refer to these arrays.\n`tools/trackcheck.mjs` must reproduce the numbers in each heading. They were computed with the App. A spline at a 2 m\nresample.\n\n#### PORT SOLENNE: tier 1, beginner. 3.84 km · tightest 56 m (lighthouse hairpin) · slopes ±5 % (−15 % only inside the jump) · 1 drop jump\n\n> *Old stone, new money. The harbour lights are on a sponsorship contract.* Golden hour on a Mediterranean resort\n> city: a seafront main straight, a climb through cliff villas, a tunnel under the old town, the Harbour Step, the\n> marina, and a hairpin around the lighthouse pier.\n\n```js\npoints: [[0,0,3],[300,0,3],[600,0,4],[790,-50,7],[890,-210,14],[905,-420,24],[820,-600,32],[640,-690,36],[420,-670,38],\n  [220,-705,36],[40,-645,30],[-110,-565,25.5],[-176,-470,23.6],[-188,-440,23.8],[-205,-375,15],[-195,-250,10],[-255,-120,6],\n  [-320,60,4],[-300,260,3],[-200,340,3],[-100,280,3],[-80,120,3],[-40,35,3]],\nwidth: 28, widths: { 18: 30, 19: 30, 20: 30 }, start: 230,   // widths: per control point, metres (the hairpin is wider)\njumps: [{ from: 12, to: 14, kind: 'drop', name: 'THE HARBOUR STEP' }],   // lip 23.6 m, lower deck 15.0 m: an 8.6 m step, 0.65 s air at every speed\ntunnels: [{ a: { cp: 7, d: 30 }, b: { cp: 9, d: 40 }, style: 'stone' }],  // under the old town, about 436 m\nspeedPads: [{ cp: 1, d: 120, u: 0 }, { cp: 4, d: 80, u: -4 }, { cp: 10, d: 80, u: 3 }, { cp: 16, d: 100, u: 0 }, { cp: 21, d: 30, u: -3 }],\nweaponPads: [{ cp: 2, d: 80 }, { cp: 7, d: -60 }, { cp: 11, d: 40 }, { cp: 17, d: 60 }],\npit: { a: { cp: 0, d: 20 }, b: { cp: 1, d: 259 }, side: 'right', w: 8 },   // sea side of the main straight\nopenEdges: [], banks: [],\n```\n\nControl points along the track (m, raw from cp0): 0, 302, 602, 800, 992, 1204, 1406, 1610, 1832, 2036, 2226, 2398,\n2514, 2546, 2614, 2740, 2884, 3076, 3280, 3412, 3532, 3696, 3790.\n\n- **Theme `coast`:**\n  - sky `['#2a1a4a', '#c8506a', '#ffb070']`;\n  - sun low in the west (`dir [-0.8, 0.3, -0.35]`, `#ffc890`, 2.4);\n  - ambient `['#ffd0c0', '#4a3a5a', 1.6]`;\n  - fog `#e89878`, near 12000 u, far 26000 u.\n- **Terrain:** the sea to the south (local y > 60: height −4 m, under a water plane at 0 m with gradient bands and a\n  sun-glint strip), a beach, then hills rising north to 120 m (noise). The old town plateau covers the tunnel at about\n  55 m.\n- **Scenery:**\n  - the promenade with 60 palm pylons and 14 sponsor boards along the main straight;\n  - crowd stands at the start;\n  - a glass pit building;\n  - 300 old-town houses (white, ochre and pink boxes with terracotta roofs) on the hill;\n  - cliff villas with pools;\n  - harbour cranes;\n  - 40 marina boats (hull and mast);\n  - the lighthouse on the pier (red and white rings, a rotating beam light, a landmark for the hairpin);\n  - a Ferris wheel turning slowly behind the marina;\n  - beach umbrellas;\n  - the landmark arch \"SOLENNE 2161\" at cp3.\n- **Music:** `solenne`.\n\n#### KARAKUM SPIRE: tier 1, intermediate. 4.59 km · tightest 55 m · a gorge **gap** jump · a spiral that passes over its own track (24.5 m clearance)\n\n> *A canyon the colour of rust, a spire nobody climbs, and a gorge that keeps what it catches.* Noon in a red-rock\n> desert: canyon-floor straights, a plateau with an open edge, the gorge jump (it needs 270 km/h), a tunnel through a\n> mesa, a 28°-banked spiral climbing around the Spire, over its own entry, and a long dive home.\n\n```js\npoints: [[0,0,0],[0,-330,0],[30,-575,2],[130,-740,8],[295,-820,18],[490,-820,29],[620,-778,32],[720,-712,36.5],[742,-696,37.5],\n  [765,-680,28],[840,-610,21],[905,-525,16],[935,-360,11],[905,-195,9],[885,-65,7],[870,65,9],[790,165,15],[675,130,21],[655,15,26],\n  [740,-50,30],[855,-50,32],[985,30,30],[1035,180,22],[945,310,14],[740,355,8],[490,345,4],[245,345,2],[50,295,0],[-25,165,0]],\nwidth: 26, start: 200,\njumps: [{ from: 7, to: 9, kind: 'gap', name: 'THE GORGE', minSpeed: 75 }],   // cp8 is a virtual apex inside the gap (not drawn); 57 m gap\ntunnels: [{ a: { cp: 11, d: 60 }, b: { cp: 13, d: 40 }, style: 'rock' }],   // through the mesa, about 316 m\nspeedPads: [{ cp: 2, d: 40, u: 0 }, { cp: 6, d: 40, u: -3 }, { cp: 6, d: 80, u: 3 }, { cp: 13, d: 60, u: 0 }, { cp: 20, d: 40, u: 0 }, { cp: 24, d: 120, u: -4 }],\nweaponPads: [{ cp: 3, d: 40 }, { cp: 10, d: 60 }, { cp: 14, d: 60 }, { cp: 22, d: 60 }, { cp: 26, d: 60 }],\npit: { a: { cp: 0, d: 10 }, b: { cp: 1, d: 0 }, side: 'left', w: 8 },\nopenEdges: [{ a: { cp: 5, d: 0 }, b: { cp: 6, d: 60 }, side: 'left' }],   // the plateau rim: fall into the canyon\nbanks: [{ from: 15, to: 20, deg: 28 }],                                    // the Spire spiral\n```\n\nControl points along the track: 0, 330, 578, 773, 958, 1155, 1292, 1412 (lip), 1439 (virtual), 1469 (far edge),\n1572, 1680, 1848, 2016, 2148, 2279, 2411, 2536, 2657, 2767, 2883, 3038, 3200, 3362, 3574, 3825, 4070, 4274, 4427.\n\n**Overpass:** raw s ≈ 2208 (lower, under the spiral exit) and ≈ 2928 (upper). **Gorge** (App. C):\n- 45–60 m/s hit the far wall: a rescue;\n- 75 m/s just clears;\n- 90 m/s lands 18 m past the far edge at −13°;\n- 170 m/s lands 129 m past at −10°.\n\n- **Theme `desert`:**\n  - sky `['#3a78d8', '#9cc8f0', '#f0e0c0']`;\n  - sun high (`[-0.3, 0.2, -0.93]`, `#fff2d0`, 3.0);\n  - fog `#e8d0a0`, near 14000, far 30000.\n- **Terrain:** a meandering canyon floor along the low sections, mesas (flat tops 40–80 m with strata walls: World3D\n  `rock: { colors: ['#b85a30', '#d8884a', '#8a3a20', '#e8b070'], band: 48 }`), the gorge cut −60 m under the jump with\n  a thin river (an emissive blue strip), and dunes outside.\n- **Scenery:**\n  - **the Spire:** a 220 m stacked rock column at local (762, 72) inside the spiral (tapering cylinders, strata\n    colours);\n  - 24 wind turbines with turning rotors on the plateaus;\n  - solar fields;\n  - carved mesa portals;\n  - canyon-wall banners;\n  - a half-buried old craft wreck as a landmark at the gorge;\n  - dust devils (particles);\n  - heat haze.\n- **Music:** `karakum`.\n\n#### MERIDIAN STACK: tier 2, advanced. 4.18 km · tightest 52 m · the Stack **drop** · a figure-eight crossover (31.9 m clearance) · night\n\n> *Three hundred storeys of people who have never seen the ground. Tonight they watch you fall past their windows.* A\n> vertical megacity at night: an elevated start, the Stack Drop between towers, neon tunnels through buildings, a low\n> pass under its own upper deck, and a long climb back to the sky deck.\n\n```js\npoints: [[0,0,42],[250,-40,42],[480,-160,40],[615,-300,37],[650,-395,36.2],[653,-425,36.4],[655,-490,22],[630,-585,17],\n  [460,-700,15],[240,-680,13],[100,-540,11],[0,-360,10],[-100,-180,10],[-260,-40,12],[-480,0,18],[-680,-80,24],[-780,-280,30],\n  [-700,-480,36],[-500,-560,40],[-300,-480,42],[-160,-300,42],[-60,-120,42]],\nwidth: 24, start: 190,\njumps: [{ from: 4, to: 6, kind: 'drop', name: 'THE STACK DROP' }],   // cp5 virtual; lip 36.2 m to a lower deck at 22.0 m: a 14.2 m step\ntunnels: [{ a: { cp: 8, d: 20 }, b: { cp: 9, d: 80 }, style: 'neon' }, { a: { cp: 13, d: 50 }, b: { cp: 14, d: 40 }, style: 'neon' }],\nspeedPads: [{ cp: 1, d: 60, u: 0 }, { cp: 3, d: 50, u: 0 }, { cp: 10, d: 80, u: 3 }, { cp: 12, d: 30, u: 0 }, { cp: 17, d: 60, u: -3 }, { cp: 20, d: 60, u: 0 }],\nweaponPads: [{ cp: 2, d: 40 }, { cp: 7, d: 60 }, { cp: 12, d: 120 }, { cp: 15, d: 60 }, { cp: 19, d: -40 }],\npit: { a: { cp: 19, d: 35 }, b: { cp: 20, d: 126 }, side: 'right', w: 8 },   // on the sky deck, ending before the crossover\nopenEdges: [], banks: [],\n```\n\nControl points along the track: 0, 258, 518, 714, 815 (lip), 846 (virtual), 912 (far edge), 1012, 1220, 1446, 1646,\n1852, 2058, 2272, 2498, 2718, 2946, 3165, 3385, 3605, 3833, 4039.\n\n**Overpass:** raw s ≈ 2082 (low, z ≈ 10 m) under s ≈ 3983 (high, z ≈ 42 m). **The drop** (App. C): every speed\nlands. Slow craft land hard (45 m/s: −37°, damage); fast ones smoothly (140 m/s: −12°). The drop sits on a 19°\ncurve, so the lower deck follows the plan path (§3.1).\n\n- **Theme `city`:**\n  - sky `['#05030f', '#1a0f3a', '#3a1a5a']`;\n  - moonlight `#8090ff`, 0.5;\n  - ambient `['#3a3a8a', '#100818', 1.0]`;\n  - fog `#1a1035`, near 6000, far 22000;\n  - bloom strong.\n- **Terrain:** flat street level at −40 m, dark concrete.\n- **Scenery:**\n  - 260 megatowers (60–350 m, window-grid emissive textures in three palettes);\n  - neon signs and holo billboards (hue-cycling) with the sponsor list;\n  - maglev rails with trains moving on loops;\n  - sweeping searchlights;\n  - flying traffic lanes (small emissive craft on paths);\n  - **the Meridian Spire** (a 500 m tower with a beacon) next to the crossover;\n  - rooftop helipads with blinking lights;\n  - light rain.\n- **Music:** `meridian`.\n\n#### BOREALIS VAULT: tier 3, expert. 5.03 km · tightest 44 m (switchbacks) · climbs to +11 % · the Vault **drop** (17.2 m) · a 490 m ice tunnel\n\n> *Minus forty, plus aurora. The Authority recommends not stopping.* An arctic research basin at night: a station\n> plateau start, sweeping descents, the Vault drop, the ice tunnel, a frozen lake with an open edge, and a brutal\n> switchback climb under the aurora.\n\n```js\npoints: [[0,0,110],[-350,0,110],[-650,60,104],[-850,220,92],[-905,420,80],[-892,478,76.5],[-878,524,77.2],[-870,552,77.6],\n  [-852,612,60],[-800,690,53],[-600,770,47],[-380,800,38],[-150,760,30],[60,820,22],[260,950,14],[480,1000,10],[700,960,10],\n  [880,860,12],[1000,700,18],[1020,520,30],[930,380,44],[1000,250,58],[900,120,72],[720,140,84],[560,60,96],[380,0,106],[190,-15,110]],\nwidth: 26, start: 200,\njumps: [{ from: 6, to: 8, kind: 'drop', name: 'THE VAULT' }],   // cp7 virtual; lip 77.2 m, lower deck 60.0 m; a ski-jump lip at +1.7 %\ntunnels: [{ a: { cp: 12, d: 30 }, b: { cp: 14, d: 60 }, style: 'ice' }],\nspeedPads: [{ cp: 2, d: 40, u: 0 }, { cp: 5, d: 15, u: 0 }, { cp: 10, d: 80, u: -3 }, { cp: 15, d: 100, u: 0 }, { cp: 24, d: 60, u: 3 }, { cp: 26, d: 80, u: 0 }],\nweaponPads: [{ cp: 3, d: 40 }, { cp: 11, d: 60 }, { cp: 14, d: 100 }, { cp: 17, d: 40 }, { cp: 22, d: 40 }],\npit: { a: { cp: 0, d: 30 }, b: { cp: 1, d: -10 }, side: 'left', w: 8 },\nopenEdges: [{ a: { cp: 15, d: 0 }, b: { cp: 16, d: 100 }, side: 'right' }],   // the frozen lake\nbanks: [{ from: 19, to: 22, deg: 26 }],                                        // the switchbacks\n```\n\nControl points along the track: 0, 350, 658, 918, 1126, 1186, 1234 (lip), 1264 (virtual), 1330 (far edge), 1424,\n1642, 1864, 2098, 2318, 2558, 2784, 3010, 3216, 3418, 3602, 3772, 3924, 4094, 4278, 4458, 4648, 4840.\n\n**The Vault** (App. C): slow craft land hard (45 m/s: −40°); 115–170 m/s land 31–111 m past the far edge at −12 to\n−15°. Air time is about 1.0–1.2 s, room for two rolls.\n\n- **Theme `arctic`:**\n  - sky `['#020814', '#0a2a4a', '#1a4a6a']`;\n  - moon `#a0c8ff`, 0.9;\n  - fog `#9ab8d8`, near 9000, far 26000.\n- **Terrain:** snowy ridges (`E.noise2` octaves), a glacier valley, the frozen lake (flat at 8 m) around local\n  (480, 1000), and dark rock strata on the steep parts.\n- **Scenery:**\n  - the research station at the start (domes, a radar dish turning, masts with blinking red lights);\n  - ice spikes;\n  - **aurora ribbons:** 5 tall translucent emissive strips, animated in waves, high in the sky;\n  - snowfall near the camera;\n  - the ice tunnel (translucent blue walls with inner glow);\n  - lake cracks (decals);\n  - a frozen-in icebreaker ship as the landmark.\n- **Music:** `borealis`.\n\n**Grid, sectors, records:** automatic (§3.1). **Overclock skin:** any track (§3.7).\n\n### 4.4 Weapon icons and pickup look\n\n24 × 24 pixel icons (`E.sprite` strings or px drawing, shaded with `E.tones`), each in its §3.4 colour on a dark\nrounded tile:\n\n| Icon | Drawing |\n| --- | --- |\n| SWARM | three small rockets fanned |\n| SEEKER | a missile inside a target ring |\n| MINEFIELD | a spiked disc |\n| CANNON | three tracer dashes |\n| RAILSHOT | crosshairs with a long beam to the right |\n| TREMOR | a sine wave over a ground line |\n| BULWARK | a hexagon shield |\n| AUTOPILOT | a steering yoke with an \"A\" |\n| NITRO | a double flame chevron |\n| SIPHON | a zigzag arrow into a droplet |\n\nThe same icons go on the How to Play pages and in the dev panel's Give weapon. In 3D, the weapon pad's sigil is the\namber triangle. The HUD shows the icon.\n\n### 4.5 Season events, story beats, academy drills, radio (`08-data-season.js`, `09-data-story.js`)\n\nSpeakers: **ORACLE** (the Authority), **PRINCIPAL** (the player's team's principal), **RIVAL** (`{$rival}`), and\n**PILOT** (`{$pilot}`, the player). Briefings play before an event's first attempt (then from the event tile's\nBRIEFING button). Debriefs play after a result. Each line is one dialog page with a portrait and a gibberish voice.\n✕ advances, △ skips all.\n\n| # | Tier / class | Event | Track | Target (gold / silver / bronze) | Briefing → debrief beats |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| — | Season open | PROLOGUE (first entry) | — | — | ORACLE: \"AUTHORITY NOTICE 0417. ROOKIE LICENCE GRANTED. CLASS: SPARK. GRAVITY: OPTIONAL.\" · PRINCIPAL: \"Welcome to {$team}. Your test laps were adequate. Adequate is where champions start.\" · PRINCIPAL: \"Bring back three medals and the Authority lets you go faster.\" · RIVAL: \"Another rookie. I'll learn your name when I need it for the wreck report.\" |\n| E1 | 1 · SPARK | ACADEMY | Port Solenne | all drills first try / ≤ 3 retries / completed | ORACLE: \"ELEVEN DRILLS. REPEAT EACH UNTIL COMPLIANT.\" → ORACLE: \"TRAINING RECORD FILED. YOU MAY NOW RACE OTHER PEOPLE.\" |\n| E2 | 1 · SPARK | RACE 3 laps | Port Solenne | 1st / 2nd / 3rd | PRINCIPAL: \"Port Solenne. Wide, forgiving, full of yachts. Win, and the sponsors notice.\" → win: \"First place. The harbour lights flashed our colours. That was contractual.\" / podium: \"A podium. Keep the trophy dust-free; we photograph it.\" / else: \"Finishing is a habit. So is losing. Choose.\" |\n| E3 | 1 · SPARK | TIME TRIAL 3 laps | Karakum Spire | medal times | PRINCIPAL: \"No weapons, no excuses. The gorge wants two hundred and seventy kilometres an hour. Arrive with them.\" → \"The clock has accepted your apology.\" |\n| E4 | 1 · SPARK | RACE 3 laps | Karakum Spire | 1st / 2nd / 3rd | RIVAL: \"Karakum has a gorge. Most rookies meet the bottom of it.\" · PRINCIPAL: \"Ignore {$rival}. Take the speed pads before the ramp.\" → win: RIVAL: \"Luck. Statistically you're due a wall.\" |","numLines":420,"startLine":1199,"totalLines":2083}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01L38mFHarpxYmq7EusHx4sy","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
