{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MckpxjUF6q9uBmwC4Djd7R","type":"tool_result","content":"265:/* =============================================================================\n266: * 1. SETUP  units, helpers, collision groups, the page's renderer (World3D.init)\n346:/* =============================================================================\n347: * 2. TEXTURES AND MATERIALS  everything drawn by code, pixel by pixel, baked into crisp (nearest) textures\n488:/* =============================================================================\n489: * 3. LEVEL  written as text, one character per floor tile (1 metre, 16 units); row 0 is the far (north) edge, y grows\n863:/* =============================================================================\n864: * 3b. TERRAIN  an open world instead of a level: new E.World3D(game, { terrain: { size, height, color, ... } })\n1103:/* =============================================================================\n1104: * 4. PARTS DRAWN BY CODE  instanced batches of four shapes (tube, ball, box, cone) in a toon look with outlines, and\n1243:/* =============================================================================\n1244: * 5. THINGS  pickups and set dressing drawn by code with the pen: world.thing(kind, x, y, z, o). A thing has\n1313:/* =============================================================================\n1314: * 5b. SHAPES  the 2D engine's shapes (docs/ASSETS.md: E.SHAPES ids, a store set's 'SET:id', or an entry) in 3D, from the\n1410:/* =============================================================================\n1411: * 6. CHARACTERS DRAWN  each rig as it stands (the game poses it; this only reads it), as a Puppet (3D parts on the\n1611:/* =============================================================================\n1612: * 7. CAMERA  world.camera: every camera a real 3D one, its pose worked out in the game's fixed steps (so the controls\n1899:/* =============================================================================\n1900: * 8. ACTORS  world.hero(o): a kinematic capsule that Rapier's character controller walks (it slides along walls,\n1956:/* =============================================================================\n1957: * 8b. VEHICLES AND FLYERS  world.vehicle(o): a kart, a car or a hovercraft, a ball that Rapier rolls (walls, bumps,\n2214:/* =============================================================================\n2215: * 9. THE WORLD  new E.World3D(game, o) (after await E.World3D.init(game)): a level, its physics, its actors, props,\n2668:/* =============================================================================\n2669: * 10. DRAWING  effects (arcs and rings on the ground, weapon trails, glows, the game's particles), lights (the torches\n3173:/* =============================================================================\n3174: * 10b. FILTERS  one look over the finished picture: world.filter = { look, apply, bloom, fxaa, ... } (change it any time)\n3257:/* =============================================================================\n3258: * 11. THE ENGINE'S HANDLES  E.World3D (init, the registries, the input preset and settings), E.THREE, E.TSL, E.RAPIER\n258:Headless Chromium runs it on WebGL 2 (?backend=webgl) and WebGPU (SwiftShader). world.hash() is the proof; game.advance(s)\n297:const PAGE = { ready: null, renderer: null, canvas: null, backend: 'none', game: null, worlds: new Set(), active: null };\n312:    const qs = new URLSearchParams(location.search), webgl = o.backend === 'webgl' || qs.get('backend') === 'webgl';\n318:    Object.assign(PAGE, { renderer: r, canvas: cv, backend: r.backend.isWebGPUBackend ? 'WebGPU' : 'WebGL 2' });\n2903:    g.particles.ground = (x, y, z) => this.level.floorAt(x, y, z);\n3261: *  o: { backend: 'webgl' (force WebGL 2; the address's ?backend=webgl does too), canvas (a canvas or its id: #view by\n3274:World3D.INPUT = Object.assign({}, E.Input.DEFAULT, {\n3280:World3D.SETTINGS = [\n3291:  backend: { get: () => PAGE.backend },","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4110026b-2798-4dbf-ae8a-e81d8e816e30","uuid":"536f3cf4-9773-4833-9142-efe21b919420","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:48:36.760Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"265:/* =============================================================================\n266: * 1. SETUP  units, helpers, collision groups, the page's renderer (World3D.init)\n346:/* =============================================================================\n347: * 2. TEXTURES AND MATERIALS  everything drawn by code, pixel by pixel, baked into crisp (nearest) textures\n488:/* =============================================================================\n489: * 3. LEVEL  written as text, one character per floor tile (1 metre, 16 units); row 0 is the far (north) edge, y grows\n863:/* =============================================================================\n864: * 3b. TERRAIN  an open world instead of a level: new E.World3D(game, { terrain: { size, height, color, ... } })\n1103:/* =============================================================================\n1104: * 4. PARTS DRAWN BY CODE  instanced batches of four shapes (tube, ball, box, cone) in a toon look with outlines, and\n1243:/* =============================================================================\n1244: * 5. THINGS  pickups and set dressing drawn by code with the pen: world.thing(kind, x, y, z, o). A thing has\n1313:/* =============================================================================\n1314: * 5b. SHAPES  the 2D engine's shapes (docs/ASSETS.md: E.SHAPES ids, a store set's 'SET:id', or an entry) in 3D, from the\n1410:/* =============================================================================\n1411: * 6. CHARACTERS DRAWN  each rig as it stands (the game poses it; this only reads it), as a Puppet (3D parts on the\n1611:/* =============================================================================\n1612: * 7. CAMERA  world.camera: every camera a real 3D one, its pose worked out in the game's fixed steps (so the controls\n1899:/* =============================================================================\n1900: * 8. ACTORS  world.hero(o): a kinematic capsule that Rapier's character controller walks (it slides along walls,\n1956:/* =============================================================================\n1957: * 8b. VEHICLES AND FLYERS  world.vehicle(o): a kart, a car or a hovercraft, a ball that Rapier rolls (walls, bumps,\n2214:/* =============================================================================\n2215: * 9. THE WORLD  new E.World3D(game, o) (after await E.World3D.init(game)): a level, its physics, its actors, props,\n2668:/* =============================================================================\n2669: * 10. DRAWING  effects (arcs and rings on the ground, weapon trails, glows, the game's particles), lights (the torches\n3173:/* =============================================================================\n3174: * 10b. FILTERS  one look over the finished picture: world.filter = { look, apply, bloom, fxaa, ... } (change it any time)\n3257:/* =============================================================================\n3258: * 11. THE ENGINE'S HANDLES  E.World3D (init, the registries, the input preset and settings), E.THREE, E.TSL, E.RAPIER\n258:Headless Chromium runs it on WebGL 2 (?backend=webgl) and WebGPU (SwiftShader). world.hash() is the proof; game.advance(s)\n297:const PAGE = { ready: null, renderer: null, canvas: null, backend: 'none', game: null, worlds: new Set(), active: null };\n312:    const qs = new URLSearchParams(location.search), webgl = o.backend === 'webgl' || qs.get('backend') === 'webgl';\n318:    Object.assign(PAGE, { renderer: r, canvas: cv, backend: r.backend.isWebGPUBackend ? 'WebGPU' : 'WebGL 2' });\n2903:    g.particles.ground = (x, y, z) => this.level.floorAt(x, y, z);\n3261: *  o: { backend: 'webgl' (force WebGL 2; the address's ?backend=webgl does too), canvas (a canvas or its id: #view by\n3274:World3D.INPUT = Object.assign({}, E.Input.DEFAULT, {\n3280:World3D.SETTINGS = [\n3291:  backend: { get: () => PAGE.backend },","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01MckpxjUF6q9uBmwC4Djd7R","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
