{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XRuvbtbetLk7vfEyhS6ExL","type":"tool_result","content":"863\t/* =============================================================================\n864\t * 3b. TERRAIN  an open world instead of a level: new E.World3D(game, { terrain: { size, height, color, ... } })\n865\t *    The ground is the game's height function (x, y) -> z in engine units, sampled every `cell` units (32: 2 m) into\n866\t *    chunks of `chunk` cells (32: 64 m square), each chunk sampled the first time anything asks about it, so a world\n867\t *    kilometres across costs only where someone goes. The same samples make all three of what the ground is:\n868\t *      physics  a Rapier heightfield per chunk, for the chunks within `physics` units of any actor (world.step streams\n869\t *               them: the same moves stream the same colliders, so a run replays exactly)\n870\t *      queries  world.ground, floorAt, topH (and terrain.normal, slope) read the same triangles Rapier collides with (each\n871\t *               cell split from its north-west corner to its south-east), and world.ray marches the height out where\n872\t *               no collider is made yet\n873\t *      picture  a quadtree of meshes, 2 m cells near the camera, coarser with distance out to `far`, a few built a frame\n874\t *               (world.draw streams them; a coarser one stands in until its finer ones are ready), skirts hiding the\n875\t *               seams between sizes, vertex colors from the game's color(x, y, z, nz) and, where the slope is steep,\n876\t *               rock in strata (rock: { colors, band }), with a fine speckle and a broad mottle over all of it\n877\t *    Everything in one material, every mesh from one pool made with the world: streaming never builds a shader\n878\t * ============================================================================= */\n879\tconst TERRAIN_POOL = 220, TERRAIN_BUILDS = 6;\n880\tclass Terrain {\n881\t  constructor(world, def) {\n882\t    if (typeof def.height !== 'function') throw new Error('my-3D2dge 3D: a terrain needs height: (x, y) => z, the ground\\'s height in engine units');\n883\t    const cell = def.cell || 32, n = def.chunk || 32, cs = cell * n, size = Array.isArray(def.size) ? def.size : [def.size || 32768, def.size || 32768];\n884\t    // chunks across: a power of two, so the quadtree's root covers the map exactly\n885\t    const cw = 2 ** Math.ceil(Math.log2(Math.max(1, Math.ceil(Math.max(size[0], size[1]) / cs))));\n886\t    Object.assign(this, { isTerrain: true, world, def, cell, n, cs, cw, ch: cw, gw: cw * n, width: cw * cs, depth: cw * cs, levels: Math.log2(cw) });\n887\t    /** mw, mh: the map in 1-metre tiles (as a level's); bottom: below every valley (a fall past it is lost) */\n888\t    this.mw = this.width / T; this.mh = this.depth / T; this.bottom = def.bottom ?? -800;\n889\t    this.marks = def.marks || {}; this.torches = []; this.shapes = []; this.rows = [];\n890\t    this.far = def.far || 24000; this.physics = def.physics || 2400; this.split = def.detail || 1.7;\n891\t    this._h = new Map(); this._cols = new Map(); this._pw = null;\n892\t  }\n893\t  /* ---- the samples ---- */\n894\t  /** chunk (cx, cy)'s heights, (n + 1) x (n + 1) samples, row by row from its north-west corner (made when first asked for) */\n895\t  heights(cx, cy) {\n896\t    const key = cy * this.cw + cx; let H = this._h.get(key); if (H) return H;\n897\t    const n = this.n, c = this.cell, x0 = cx * this.cs, y0 = cy * this.cs, f = this.def.height; H = new Float32Array((n + 1) * (n + 1));\n898\t    for (let j = 0; j <= n; j++) for (let i = 0; i <= n; i++) H[j * (n + 1) + i] = f(x0 + i * c, y0 + j * c);\n899\t    this._h.set(key, H); return H;\n900\t  }\n901\t  /** the height at grid point (gx, gy) (whole cells from the map's north-west corner): a made chunk's sample, else the\n902\t   *  function itself (the same number: far meshes read it without making the chunks they span) */\n903\t  sample(gx, gy) {\n904\t    const g = this.gw; gx = gx < 0 ? 0 : gx > g ? g : gx; gy = gy < 0 ? 0 : gy > g ? g : gy;\n905\t    const n = this.n, cx = Math.min(this.cw - 1, Math.floor(gx / n)), cy = Math.min(this.cw - 1, Math.floor(gy / n)), H = this._h.get(cy * this.cw + cx);\n906\t    return H ? H[(gy - cy * n) * (n + 1) + gx - cx * n] : this.def.height(gx * this.cell, gy * this.cell);\n907\t  }\n908\t  _corners(x, y, need) {\n909\t    const c = this.cell, gx = clamp(x / c, 0, this.gw - 1e-6), gy = clamp(y / c, 0, this.gw - 1e-6), i = Math.floor(gx), j = Math.floor(gy);\n910\t    if (need) { const n = this.n; this.heights(Math.min(this.cw - 1, Math.floor(i / n)), Math.min(this.cw - 1, Math.floor(j / n))); if ((i + 1) % n === 0 || (j + 1) % n === 0) { this.heights(Math.min(this.cw - 1, Math.floor((i + 1) / n)), Math.min(this.cw - 1, Math.floor((j + 1) / n))); this.heights(Math.min(this.cw - 1, Math.floor((i + 1) / n)), Math.min(this.cw - 1, Math.floor(j / n))); this.heights(Math.min(this.cw - 1, Math.floor(i / n)), Math.min(this.cw - 1, Math.floor((j + 1) / n))); } }\n911\t    const C = _tc; C[0] = this.sample(i, j); C[1] = this.sample(i + 1, j); C[2] = this.sample(i, j + 1); C[3] = this.sample(i + 1, j + 1); C[4] = gx - i; C[5] = gy - j;\n912\t    return C;\n913\t  }\n914\t  /** the ground's height at (x, y): the triangle Rapier collides with (a cell is split from its north-west corner to its\n915\t   *  south-east one) */\n916\t  ground(x, y) {\n917\t    const [nw, ne, sw, se, u, s] = this._corners(x, y, true);\n918\t    return u <= s ? sw + (se - sw) * u + (nw - sw) * (1 - s) : ne + (nw - ne) * (1 - u) + (se - ne) * s;\n919\t  }\n920\t  /** the ground's normal at (x, y): [x, y, z], length 1, z up (the triangle's) */\n921\t  normal(x, y, out = [0, 0, 1]) {\n922\t    const [nw, ne, sw, se, u, s] = this._corners(x, y, true), c = this.cell;\n923\t    const gx = (u <= s ? se - sw : ne - nw) / c, gy = (u <= s ? sw - nw : se - ne) / c, l = Math.hypot(gx, gy, 1);\n924\t    out[0] = -gx / l; out[1] = -gy / l; out[2] = 1 / l; return out;\n925\t  }\n926\t  /** how steep the ground is at (x, y): 0 flat .. 1 a cliff */\n927\t  slope(x, y) { return 1 - this.normal(x, y, _tn)[2]; }\n928\t  floorAt(x, y, z = 1e9) { const g = this.ground(x, y); return g <= z + 4 ? g : this.bottom; }\n929\t  topH(x, y) { return this.ground(x, y); }\n930\t  index() { return -1; }\n931\t  spec() { return null; }\n932\t  solidTile() { return false; }\n933\t  placeWalls() {}\n934\t  placePillars() {}\n935\t  animateBraziers() {}\n936\t  /** the first point a ray (unit direction) meets the ground within len units, as its distance, or null: marched a cell at\n937\t   *  a time, then narrowed down */\n938\t  rayDist(x, y, z, dx, dy, dz, len) {\n939\t    const st = this.cell * .5; let t0 = 0, above = z - this.ground(x, y);\n940\t    if (above < 0) return 0;\n941\t    for (let t = st; t <= len + st; t += st) {\n942\t      const tt = Math.min(t, len), h = z + dz * tt - this.ground(x + dx * tt, y + dy * tt);\n943\t      if (h < 0) { let a = t0, b = tt; for (let k = 0; k < 12; k++) { const m = (a + b) / 2; if (z + dz * m - this.ground(x + dx * m, y + dy * m) < 0) b = m; else a = m; } return (a + b) / 2; }\n944\t      t0 = tt; if (tt >= len) break;\n945\t    }\n946\t    return null;\n947\t  }\n948\t\n949\t  /* ---- physics: the chunks near the actors ---- */\n950\t  colliders(pw) { this._pw = pw; this._cols.clear(); }\n951\t  /** a step of world.step: a heightfield for every chunk within `physics` of an actor, none for the rest (with room to\n952\t   *  spare, so one walking along a chunk's edge doesn't make and drop it every step) */\n953\t  stream(world) {\n954\t    const pw = this._pw; if (!pw) return;\n955\t    const R = this.physics, cs = this.cs, want = this._want || (this._want = new Set()); want.clear();\n956\t    for (const a of world.actors) {\n957\t      if (!a.body) continue;\n958\t      const x0 = Math.max(0, Math.floor((a.x - R) / cs)), x1 = Math.min(this.cw - 1, Math.floor((a.x + R) / cs)), y0 = Math.max(0, Math.floor((a.y - R) / cs)), y1 = Math.min(this.cw - 1, Math.floor((a.y + R) / cs));\n959\t      for (let cy = y0; cy <= y1; cy++) for (let cx = x0; cx <= x1; cx++) want.add(cy * this.cw + cx);\n960\t    }\n961\t    for (const k of want) if (!this._cols.has(k)) this._cols.set(k, this._collider(pw, k % this.cw, Math.floor(k / this.cw)));\n962\t    for (const [k, b] of this._cols) {\n963\t      if (want.has(k)) continue;\n964\t      const cx = k % this.cw, cy = Math.floor(k / this.cw), x = (cx + .5) * cs, y = (cy + .5) * cs;\n965\t      if (world.actors.some(a => a.body && Math.max(Math.abs(a.x - x), Math.abs(a.y - y)) < R + cs)) continue;\n966\t      pw.removeRigidBody(b); this._cols.delete(k);\n967\t    }\n968\t  }\n969\t  _collider(pw, cx, cy) {\n970\t    const n = this.n, H = this.heights(cx, cy), F = new Float32Array((n + 1) * (n + 1));\n971\t    // Rapier's heightfield lies in its own x-z plane, y up, rows along +z; turned to stand z up (Z_UP), its +z is our -y,\n972\t    // so row i is the samples' row n - i (from the chunk's south edge north)\n973\t    for (let j = 0; j <= n; j++) for (let i = 0; i <= n; i++) F[i + j * (n + 1)] = H[(n - i) * (n + 1) + j];\n974\t    const b = pw.createRigidBody(RAPIER.RigidBodyDesc.fixed().setTranslation((cx + .5) * this.cs, (cy + .5) * this.cs, 0).setRotation(Z_UP));\n975\t    const flags = RAPIER.HeightFieldFlags ? RAPIER.HeightFieldFlags.FIX_INTERNAL_EDGES : undefined;\n976\t    const col = pw.createCollider(RAPIER.ColliderDesc.heightfield(n, n, F, { x: this.cs, y: 1, z: this.cs }, flags).setFriction(.8).setCollisionGroups(GROUPS.level), b);\n977\t    this.world._owners.set(col.handle, this);\n978\t    return b;\n979\t  }\n980\t}\n981\tconst _tc = new Float64Array(6), _tn = [0, 0, 1];\n982\t/* ---- the terrain's picture: one material (vertex colors, rock strata by height where it is steep, a speckle and a\n983\t *      mottle), a pool of meshes sharing one index, and the quadtree that picks which to draw ---- */\n984\tTerrain.prototype.meshes = function (world) {\n985\t  const def = this.def, n = this.n, V = (n + 1) * (n + 1) + 4 * (n + 1), own = x => world._own(x);\n986\t  const { attribute, positionWorld, normalWorld, texture, vec2, vec3, mix, smoothstep, float } = TSL;\n987\t  // the speckle and mottle: value noise in grey (linear filtering, mipmaps: it is seen from far off)\n988\t  const noiseTex = (w, f) => { const cv = document.createElement('canvas'); cv.width = cv.height = w; const g = cv.getContext('2d'), img = g.createImageData(w, w);\n989\t    for (let y = 0; y < w; y++) for (let x = 0; x < w; x++) { const v = f(x, y) * 255, i = (y * w + x) * 4; img.data[i] = img.data[i + 1] = img.data[i + 2] = v; img.data[i + 3] = 255; }\n990\t    g.putImageData(img, 0, 0); const t = own(new THREE.CanvasTexture(cv)); t.wrapS = t.wrapT = THREE.RepeatWrapping; t.colorSpace = THREE.NoColorSpace; t.anisotropy = 4; return t; };\n991\t  // value noise that wraps every `per` lattice cells (the texture repeats without a seam)\n992\t  const wrapNoise = (x, y, per) => {\n993\t    const xi = Math.floor(x), yi = Math.floor(y), u = x - xi, v = y - yi, su = u * u * (3 - 2 * u), sv = v * v * (3 - 2 * v), m = a => ((a % per) + per) % per;\n994\t    const h = (a, b) => E.hash2(m(a) + 91, m(b) + 37);\n995\t    return lerp(lerp(h(xi, yi), h(xi + 1, yi), su), lerp(h(xi, yi + 1), h(xi + 1, yi + 1), su), sv);\n996\t  };\n997\t  const fbm = (x, y, oct) => { let v = 0, a = .5, t = 0; for (let o = 0, f = 4; o < oct; o++, f *= 2) { v += a * wrapNoise(x / 64 * f, y / 64 * f, f); t += a; a *= .5; } return v / t; };\n998\t  const speck = noiseTex(64, (x, y) => clamp(.5 + (E.hash2(x, y) - .5) * .65 + (fbm(x, y, 2) - .5) * .7, 0, 1));\n999\t  const mottle = noiseTex(64, (x, y) => clamp((fbm(x, y, 4) - .5) * 1.6 + .5, 0, 1));\n1000\t  // the strata: a column of bands (rock.colors repeated, each band split by a thin darker line), read by world height\n1001\t  const R = def.rock || {}, bands = (R.colors || ['#9c6a4c', '#b98058', '#8a5a40', '#c49268', '#a87050', '#7c5038']).map(c => E.hex(c)), bh = 16;\n1002\t  const scv = document.createElement('canvas'); scv.width = 1; scv.height = bands.length * bh; const sg = scv.getContext('2d'), simg = sg.createImageData(1, scv.height);\n1003\t  for (let y = 0; y < scv.height; y++) { const c = bands[Math.floor(y / bh)], k = y % bh === 0 ? .72 : y % bh === 1 ? .86 : 1 + (E.hash2(y, 3) - .5) * .12, i = y * 4; simg.data[i] = clamp(c[0] * k, 0, 255); simg.data[i + 1] = clamp(c[1] * k, 0, 255); simg.data[i + 2] = clamp(c[2] * k, 0, 255); simg.data[i + 3] = 255; }\n1004\t  sg.putImageData(simg, 0, 0); const strata = own(new THREE.CanvasTexture(scv)); strata.wrapS = strata.wrapT = THREE.RepeatWrapping; strata.colorSpace = THREE.SRGBColorSpace; strata.magFilter = THREE.LinearFilter;\n1005\t  const band = (R.band || 40) / U * bands.length, s0 = R.slope ? R.slope[0] : .32, s1 = R.slope ? R.slope[1] : .5, dk = def.speckle ?? .22, mk = def.mottle ?? .3;\n1006\t  const wp = positionWorld, vcol = attribute('color', 'vec3');\n1007\t  const fine = texture(speck, wp.xz.mul(.75)).r.sub(.5).mul(dk).add(1), broad = texture(mottle, wp.xz.mul(.012)).r.sub(.5).mul(mk).add(1);\n1008\t  const wob = texture(mottle, wp.xz.mul(.05)).r.sub(.5).mul(.35);\n1009\t  const rockC = texture(strata, vec2(.5, wp.y.div(band).add(wob))).rgb.mul(texture(speck, vec2(wp.x.add(wp.z), wp.y).mul(.9)).r.sub(.5).mul(.3).add(1));\n1010\t  const steep = smoothstep(float(s0), float(s1), float(1).sub(normalWorld.y));\n1011\t  const mat = this.mat = world._obj(new THREE.MeshLambertNodeMaterial({ color: '#ffffff' }));\n1012\t  mat.colorNode = mix(vcol.mul(fine).mul(broad), rockC.mul(broad), steep);\n1013\t  world._own(mat);\n1014\t  // one index for every mesh: the grid's two triangles a cell (NW-SW-SE, NW-SE-NE: the colliders' split), then the skirts\n1015\t  const idx = [], at = (i, j) => j * (n + 1) + i, sk = (side, k) => (n + 1) * (n + 1) + side * (n + 1) + k;\n1016\t  for (let j = 0; j < n; j++) for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) { const nw = at(i, j), ne = at(i + 1, j), sw = at(i, j + 1), se = at(i + 1, j + 1); idx.push(nw, sw, se, nw, se, ne); }\n1017\t  const edge = [k => at(k, 0), k => at(n, k), k => at(n - k, n), k => at(0, n - k)];   // north, east, south, west, each running round clockwise\n1018\t  for (let side = 0; side < 4; side++) for (let k = 0; k < n; k++) { const a = edge[side](k), b = edge[side](k + 1), a2 = sk(side, k), b2 = sk(side, k + 1); idx.push(a, b, b2, a, b2, a2, a, b2, b, a, a2, b2); }\n1019\t  const index = new THREE.BufferAttribute(new Uint32Array(idx), 1);\n1020\t  this._pool = []; this._nodes = new Map(); this._edge = edge; this._V = V; this._frame = 0;\n1021\t  for (let k = 0, np = def.pool || (n <= 16 ? 400 : TERRAIN_POOL); k < np; k++) {\n1022\t    const geo = own(new THREE.BufferGeometry());\n1023\t    geo.setAttribute('position', new THREE.BufferAttribute(new Float32Array(V * 3), 3)); geo.setAttribute('normal', new THREE.BufferAttribute(new Float32Array(V * 3), 3));\n1024\t    geo.setAttribute('color', new THREE.BufferAttribute(new Float32Array(V * 3), 3)); geo.setIndex(index);\n1025\t    geo.boundingSphere = new THREE.Sphere(); geo.boundingBox = new THREE.Box3();\n1026\t    const m = new THREE.Mesh(geo, mat); m.visible = false; m.receiveShadow = true; m.matrixAutoUpdate = false; world.scene.add(m);\n1027\t    this._pool.push({ mesh: m, key: null, used: -1, shown: -1 });\n1028\t  }\n1029\t};\n1030\t/** fill a pooled mesh with node (L, nx, ny): (n + 1)^2 vertices 2^L cells apart, their normals from the samples round\n1031\t *  them, their colors from the game, and the skirts hanging below its edges */\n1032\tTerrain.prototype._build = function (slot, L, nx, ny) {\n1033\t  const n = this.n, s = 2 ** L, gx0 = nx * n * s, gy0 = ny * n * s, c = this.cell, colorOf = this.def.color, geo = slot.mesh.geometry;\n1034\t  const P = geo.attributes.position.array, N = geo.attributes.normal.array, C = geo.attributes.color.array, hs = this._hs || (this._hs = new Float32Array((n + 3) * (n + 3)));\n1035\t  // the heights, one sample beyond each edge for the normals\n1036\t  for (let j = -1; j <= n + 1; j++) for (let i = -1; i <= n + 1; i++) hs[(j + 1) * (n + 3) + i + 1] = this.sample(gx0 + i * s, gy0 + j * s);\n1037\t  let lo = 1e9, hi = -1e9; const nm = [0, 0, 1], col = [0, 0, 0], k2 = 1 / 255;\n1038\t  for (let j = 0; j <= n; j++) for (let i = 0; i <= n; i++) {\n1039\t    const v = j * (n + 1) + i, h = hs[(j + 1) * (n + 3) + i + 1], x = (gx0 + i * s) * c, y = (gy0 + j * s) * c;\n1040\t    const ddx = (hs[(j + 1) * (n + 3) + i + 2] - hs[(j + 1) * (n + 3) + i]) / (2 * s * c), ddy = (hs[(j + 2) * (n + 3) + i + 1] - hs[j * (n + 3) + i + 1]) / (2 * s * c), l = Math.hypot(ddx, ddy, 1);\n1041\t    nm[0] = -ddx / l; nm[1] = -ddy / l; nm[2] = 1 / l;\n1042\t    P[v * 3] = x / U; P[v * 3 + 1] = h / U; P[v * 3 + 2] = y / U; N[v * 3] = nm[0]; N[v * 3 + 1] = nm[2]; N[v * 3 + 2] = nm[1];\n1043\t    col[0] = 150; col[1] = 140; col[2] = 110;\n1044\t    const r = (colorOf && colorOf(x, y, h, nm[2], col)) || col;\n1045\t    C[v * 3] = srgbLin(r[0] * k2); C[v * 3 + 1] = srgbLin(r[1] * k2); C[v * 3 + 2] = srgbLin(r[2] * k2);\n1046\t    if (h < lo) lo = h; if (h > hi) hi = h;\n1047\t  }\n1048\t  const drop = (s * c) * .75 + 6;\n1049\t  for (let side = 0; side < 4; side++) for (let k = 0; k <= n; k++) {\n1050\t    const a = this._edge[side](k), b = (n + 1) * (n + 1) + side * (n + 1) + k;\n1051\t    P[b * 3] = P[a * 3]; P[b * 3 + 1] = P[a * 3 + 1] - drop / U; P[b * 3 + 2] = P[a * 3 + 2];\n1052\t    for (let q = 0; q < 3; q++) { N[b * 3 + q] = N[a * 3 + q]; C[b * 3 + q] = C[a * 3 + q] * .8; }\n1053\t  }\n1054\t  for (const a of ['position', 'normal', 'color']) geo.attributes[a].needsUpdate = true;\n1055\t  const x0 = gx0 * c / U, y0 = gy0 * c / U, w = n * s * c / U;\n1056\t  geo.boundingBox.min.set(x0, (lo - drop) / U, y0); geo.boundingBox.max.set(x0 + w, hi / U, y0 + w); geo.boundingBox.getBoundingSphere(geo.boundingSphere);\n1057\t  slot.mesh.castShadow = L <= 1; slot.key = L + ':' + nx + ':' + ny; slot.L = L;\n1058\t};\n1059\t/** world.draw's step: pick the quadtree's nodes for a camera at (x, y, z) (engine units), build up to `budget` missing\n1060\t *  ones (all of them when budget is Infinity: the first frame), show those and hide the rest */\n1061\tTerrain.prototype.drawStream = function (world, x, y, z, budget = TERRAIN_BUILDS, again = false) {\n1062\t  // frame: what this frame built or showed is never taken for another node in it; pass: what the last look showed\n1063\t  const frame = again ? this._frame : ++this._frame, pass = this._pass = (this._pass || 0) + 1, show = this._show || (this._show = []), queue = this._queue || (this._queue = []); show.length = 0; queue.length = 0;\n1064\t  const nodes = this._nodes, n = this.n, cs = this.cs, far = this.far, K = this.split;\n1065\t  const ready = (L, nx, ny) => nodes.get(L + ':' + nx + ':' + ny);\n1066\t  // nearest first, so what stands closest is built first\n1067\t  // a node splits into its four when the camera is within K of its size; one whose four aren't all built yet stands in\n1068\t  // for them (and they are queued); one not built itself is queued, and its parent stands in\n1069\t  const visit = (L, nx, ny) => {\n1070\t    const size = cs * 2 ** L, x0 = nx * size, y0 = ny * size, dx = Math.max(x0 - x, 0, x - x0 - size), dy = Math.max(y0 - y, 0, y - y0 - size), d = Math.hypot(dx, dy);\n1071\t    if (d > far) return;\n1072\t    const me = ready(L, nx, ny);\n1073\t    if (L > 0 && d < size * K) {\n1074\t      const kids = [[2 * nx, 2 * ny], [2 * nx + 1, 2 * ny], [2 * nx, 2 * ny + 1], [2 * nx + 1, 2 * ny + 1]];\n1075\t      const missing = kids.filter(([a, b]) => !ready(L - 1, a, b) && !this._outside(L - 1, a, b, x, y));\n1076\t      if (!missing.length) { for (const [a, b] of kids) visit(L - 1, a, b); return; }\n1077\t      for (const [a, b] of missing) queue.push([d, L - 1, a, b]);\n1078\t    }\n1079\t    if (!me) { queue.push([d, L, nx, ny]); return; }\n1080\t    me.used = frame; me.shown = pass; show.push(me);\n1081\t  };\n1082\t  visit(this.levels, 0, 0);\n1083\t  queue.sort((a, b) => a[0] - b[0] || a[1] - b[1]);\n1084\t  let built = 0;\n1085\t  for (const [, L, nx, ny] of queue) {\n1086\t    if (built >= budget) break;\n1087\t    const key = L + ':' + nx + ':' + ny; if (nodes.has(key)) continue;\n1088\t    // the slot touched longest ago (never one shown or built this frame)\n1089\t    let slot = null; for (const p of this._pool) if (p.used < frame && (!slot || p.used < slot.used)) slot = p;\n1090\t    if (!slot) break;\n1091\t    if (slot.key) nodes.delete(slot.key);\n1092\t    this._build(slot, L, nx, ny); slot.used = frame; nodes.set(key, slot); built++;\n1093\t  }\n1094\t  for (const p of this._pool) p.mesh.visible = p.shown === pass;\n1095\t  if (built && budget === Infinity) return this.drawStream(world, x, y, z, Infinity, true);\n1096\t  return built;\n1097\t};\n1098\tTerrain.prototype._outside = function (L, nx, ny, x, y) { const size = this.cs * 2 ** L, dx = Math.max(nx * size - x, 0, x - nx * size - size), dy = Math.max(ny * size - y, 0, y - ny * size - size); return Math.hypot(dx, dy) > this.far; };\n1099\t/** straight lines over open ground: a terrain's flow field (world.flow()) never steers */\n1100\tclass TerrainFlow { to() { return this; } dir() { return null; } distance(x, y) { return 1e9; } }\n1101\tconst srgbLin = c => c <= .04045 ? c / 12.92 : Math.pow((c + .055) / 1.055, 2.4);\n1102\t\n1103\t/* =============================================================================\n1104\t * 4. PARTS DRAWN BY CODE  instanced batches of four shapes (tube, ball, box, cone) in a toon look with outlines, and\n1105\t *    two that glow (glow, halo); a pen that draws with them in engine units. Puppets, things and anything a game draws\n1106\t *    in 3D go through them, so thousands of parts cost a handful of draw calls\n1107\t * ============================================================================= */"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4110026b-2798-4dbf-ae8a-e81d8e816e30","uuid":"2c96c241-4724-4e3c-9df3-be36284aa70c","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:48:48.846Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261103-184630__xa320fb/work/SnipeoutHD-WipeoutHD-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261103-184630/engine/my-3d2dge-3d.js","content":"/* =============================================================================\n * 3b. TERRAIN  an open world instead of a level: new E.World3D(game, { terrain: { size, height, color, ... } })\n *    The ground is the game's height function (x, y) -> z in engine units, sampled every `cell` units (32: 2 m) into\n *    chunks of `chunk` cells (32: 64 m square), each chunk sampled the first time anything asks about it, so a world\n *    kilometres across costs only where someone goes. The same samples make all three of what the ground is:\n *      physics  a Rapier heightfield per chunk, for the chunks within `physics` units of any actor (world.step streams\n *               them: the same moves stream the same colliders, so a run replays exactly)\n *      queries  world.ground, floorAt, topH (and terrain.normal, slope) read the same triangles Rapier collides with (each\n *               cell split from its north-west corner to its south-east), and world.ray marches the height out where\n *               no collider is made yet\n *      picture  a quadtree of meshes, 2 m cells near the camera, coarser with distance out to `far`, a few built a frame\n *               (world.draw streams them; a coarser one stands in until its finer ones are ready), skirts hiding the\n *               seams between sizes, vertex colors from the game's color(x, y, z, nz) and, where the slope is steep,\n *               rock in strata (rock: { colors, band }), with a fine speckle and a broad mottle over all of it\n *    Everything in one material, every mesh from one pool made with the world: streaming never builds a shader\n * ============================================================================= */\nconst TERRAIN_POOL = 220, TERRAIN_BUILDS = 6;\nclass Terrain {\n  constructor(world, def) {\n    if (typeof def.height !== 'function') throw new Error('my-3D2dge 3D: a terrain needs height: (x, y) => z, the ground\\'s height in engine units');\n    const cell = def.cell || 32, n = def.chunk || 32, cs = cell * n, size = Array.isArray(def.size) ? def.size : [def.size || 32768, def.size || 32768];\n    // chunks across: a power of two, so the quadtree's root covers the map exactly\n    const cw = 2 ** Math.ceil(Math.log2(Math.max(1, Math.ceil(Math.max(size[0], size[1]) / cs))));\n    Object.assign(this, { isTerrain: true, world, def, cell, n, cs, cw, ch: cw, gw: cw * n, width: cw * cs, depth: cw * cs, levels: Math.log2(cw) });\n    /** mw, mh: the map in 1-metre tiles (as a level's); bottom: below every valley (a fall past it is lost) */\n    this.mw = this.width / T; this.mh = this.depth / T; this.bottom = def.bottom ?? -800;\n    this.marks = def.marks || {}; this.torches = []; this.shapes = []; this.rows = [];\n    this.far = def.far || 24000; this.physics = def.physics || 2400; this.split = def.detail || 1.7;\n    this._h = new Map(); this._cols = new Map(); this._pw = null;\n  }\n  /* ---- the samples ---- */\n  /** chunk (cx, cy)'s heights, (n + 1) x (n + 1) samples, row by row from its north-west corner (made when first asked for) */\n  heights(cx, cy) {\n    const key = cy * this.cw + cx; let H = this._h.get(key); if (H) return H;\n    const n = this.n, c = this.cell, x0 = cx * this.cs, y0 = cy * this.cs, f = this.def.height; H = new Float32Array((n + 1) * (n + 1));\n    for (let j = 0; j <= n; j++) for (let i = 0; i <= n; i++) H[j * (n + 1) + i] = f(x0 + i * c, y0 + j * c);\n    this._h.set(key, H); return H;\n  }\n  /** the height at grid point (gx, gy) (whole cells from the map's north-west corner): a made chunk's sample, else the\n   *  function itself (the same number: far meshes read it without making the chunks they span) */\n  sample(gx, gy) {\n    const g = this.gw; gx = gx < 0 ? 0 : gx > g ? g : gx; gy = gy < 0 ? 0 : gy > g ? g : gy;\n    const n = this.n, cx = Math.min(this.cw - 1, Math.floor(gx / n)), cy = Math.min(this.cw - 1, Math.floor(gy / n)), H = this._h.get(cy * this.cw + cx);\n    return H ? H[(gy - cy * n) * (n + 1) + gx - cx * n] : this.def.height(gx * this.cell, gy * this.cell);\n  }\n  _corners(x, y, need) {\n    const c = this.cell, gx = clamp(x / c, 0, this.gw - 1e-6), gy = clamp(y / c, 0, this.gw - 1e-6), i = Math.floor(gx), j = Math.floor(gy);\n    if (need) { const n = this.n; this.heights(Math.min(this.cw - 1, Math.floor(i / n)), Math.min(this.cw - 1, Math.floor(j / n))); if ((i + 1) % n === 0 || (j + 1) % n === 0) { this.heights(Math.min(this.cw - 1, Math.floor((i + 1) / n)), Math.min(this.cw - 1, Math.floor((j + 1) / n))); this.heights(Math.min(this.cw - 1, Math.floor((i + 1) / n)), Math.min(this.cw - 1, Math.floor(j / n))); this.heights(Math.min(this.cw - 1, Math.floor(i / n)), Math.min(this.cw - 1, Math.floor((j + 1) / n))); } }\n    const C = _tc; C[0] = this.sample(i, j); C[1] = this.sample(i + 1, j); C[2] = this.sample(i, j + 1); C[3] = this.sample(i + 1, j + 1); C[4] = gx - i; C[5] = gy - j;\n    return C;\n  }\n  /** the ground's height at (x, y): the triangle Rapier collides with (a cell is split from its north-west corner to its\n   *  south-east one) */\n  ground(x, y) {\n    const [nw, ne, sw, se, u, s] = this._corners(x, y, true);\n    return u <= s ? sw + (se - sw) * u + (nw - sw) * (1 - s) : ne + (nw - ne) * (1 - u) + (se - ne) * s;\n  }\n  /** the ground's normal at (x, y): [x, y, z], length 1, z up (the triangle's) */\n  normal(x, y, out = [0, 0, 1]) {\n    const [nw, ne, sw, se, u, s] = this._corners(x, y, true), c = this.cell;\n    const gx = (u <= s ? se - sw : ne - nw) / c, gy = (u <= s ? sw - nw : se - ne) / c, l = Math.hypot(gx, gy, 1);\n    out[0] = -gx / l; out[1] = -gy / l; out[2] = 1 / l; return out;\n  }\n  /** how steep the ground is at (x, y): 0 flat .. 1 a cliff */\n  slope(x, y) { return 1 - this.normal(x, y, _tn)[2]; }\n  floorAt(x, y, z = 1e9) { const g = this.ground(x, y); return g <= z + 4 ? g : this.bottom; }\n  topH(x, y) { return this.ground(x, y); }\n  index() { return -1; }\n  spec() { return null; }\n  solidTile() { return false; }\n  placeWalls() {}\n  placePillars() {}\n  animateBraziers() {}\n  /** the first point a ray (unit direction) meets the ground within len units, as its distance, or null: marched a cell at\n   *  a time, then narrowed down */\n  rayDist(x, y, z, dx, dy, dz, len) {\n    const st = this.cell * .5; let t0 = 0, above = z - this.ground(x, y);\n    if (above < 0) return 0;\n    for (let t = st; t <= len + st; t += st) {\n      const tt = Math.min(t, len), h = z + dz * tt - this.ground(x + dx * tt, y + dy * tt);\n      if (h < 0) { let a = t0, b = tt; for (let k = 0; k < 12; k++) { const m = (a + b) / 2; if (z + dz * m - this.ground(x + dx * m, y + dy * m) < 0) b = m; else a = m; } return (a + b) / 2; }\n      t0 = tt; if (tt >= len) break;\n    }\n    return null;\n  }\n\n  /* ---- physics: the chunks near the actors ---- */\n  colliders(pw) { this._pw = pw; this._cols.clear(); }\n  /** a step of world.step: a heightfield for every chunk within `physics` of an actor, none for the rest (with room to\n   *  spare, so one walking along a chunk's edge doesn't make and drop it every step) */\n  stream(world) {\n    const pw = this._pw; if (!pw) return;\n    const R = this.physics, cs = this.cs, want = this._want || (this._want = new Set()); want.clear();\n    for (const a of world.actors) {\n      if (!a.body) continue;\n      const x0 = Math.max(0, Math.floor((a.x - R) / cs)), x1 = Math.min(this.cw - 1, Math.floor((a.x + R) / cs)), y0 = Math.max(0, Math.floor((a.y - R) / cs)), y1 = Math.min(this.cw - 1, Math.floor((a.y + R) / cs));\n      for (let cy = y0; cy <= y1; cy++) for (let cx = x0; cx <= x1; cx++) want.add(cy * this.cw + cx);\n    }\n    for (const k of want) if (!this._cols.has(k)) this._cols.set(k, this._collider(pw, k % this.cw, Math.floor(k / this.cw)));\n    for (const [k, b] of this._cols) {\n      if (want.has(k)) continue;\n      const cx = k % this.cw, cy = Math.floor(k / this.cw), x = (cx + .5) * cs, y = (cy + .5) * cs;\n      if (world.actors.some(a => a.body && Math.max(Math.abs(a.x - x), Math.abs(a.y - y)) < R + cs)) continue;\n      pw.removeRigidBody(b); this._cols.delete(k);\n    }\n  }\n  _collider(pw, cx, cy) {\n    const n = this.n, H = this.heights(cx, cy), F = new Float32Array((n + 1) * (n + 1));\n    // Rapier's heightfield lies in its own x-z plane, y up, rows along +z; turned to stand z up (Z_UP), its +z is our -y,\n    // so row i is the samples' row n - i (from the chunk's south edge north)\n    for (let j = 0; j <= n; j++) for (let i = 0; i <= n; i++) F[i + j * (n + 1)] = H[(n - i) * (n + 1) + j];\n    const b = pw.createRigidBody(RAPIER.RigidBodyDesc.fixed().setTranslation((cx + .5) * this.cs, (cy + .5) * this.cs, 0).setRotation(Z_UP));\n    const flags = RAPIER.HeightFieldFlags ? RAPIER.HeightFieldFlags.FIX_INTERNAL_EDGES : undefined;\n    const col = pw.createCollider(RAPIER.ColliderDesc.heightfield(n, n, F, { x: this.cs, y: 1, z: this.cs }, flags).setFriction(.8).setCollisionGroups(GROUPS.level), b);\n    this.world._owners.set(col.handle, this);\n    return b;\n  }\n}\nconst _tc = new Float64Array(6), _tn = [0, 0, 1];\n/* ---- the terrain's picture: one material (vertex colors, rock strata by height where it is steep, a speckle and a\n *      mottle), a pool of meshes sharing one index, and the quadtree that picks which to draw ---- */\nTerrain.prototype.meshes = function (world) {\n  const def = this.def, n = this.n, V = (n + 1) * (n + 1) + 4 * (n + 1), own = x => world._own(x);\n  const { attribute, positionWorld, normalWorld, texture, vec2, vec3, mix, smoothstep, float } = TSL;\n  // the speckle and mottle: value noise in grey (linear filtering, mipmaps: it is seen from far off)\n  const noiseTex = (w, f) => { const cv = document.createElement('canvas'); cv.width = cv.height = w; const g = cv.getContext('2d'), img = g.createImageData(w, w);\n    for (let y = 0; y < w; y++) for (let x = 0; x < w; x++) { const v = f(x, y) * 255, i = (y * w + x) * 4; img.data[i] = img.data[i + 1] = img.data[i + 2] = v; img.data[i + 3] = 255; }\n    g.putImageData(img, 0, 0); const t = own(new THREE.CanvasTexture(cv)); t.wrapS = t.wrapT = THREE.RepeatWrapping; t.colorSpace = THREE.NoColorSpace; t.anisotropy = 4; return t; };\n  // value noise that wraps every `per` lattice cells (the texture repeats without a seam)\n  const wrapNoise = (x, y, per) => {\n    const xi = Math.floor(x), yi = Math.floor(y), u = x - xi, v = y - yi, su = u * u * (3 - 2 * u), sv = v * v * (3 - 2 * v), m = a => ((a % per) + per) % per;\n    const h = (a, b) => E.hash2(m(a) + 91, m(b) + 37);\n    return lerp(lerp(h(xi, yi), h(xi + 1, yi), su), lerp(h(xi, yi + 1), h(xi + 1, yi + 1), su), sv);\n  };\n  const fbm = (x, y, oct) => { let v = 0, a = .5, t = 0; for (let o = 0, f = 4; o < oct; o++, f *= 2) { v += a * wrapNoise(x / 64 * f, y / 64 * f, f); t += a; a *= .5; } return v / t; };\n  const speck = noiseTex(64, (x, y) => clamp(.5 + (E.hash2(x, y) - .5) * .65 + (fbm(x, y, 2) - .5) * .7, 0, 1));\n  const mottle = noiseTex(64, (x, y) => clamp((fbm(x, y, 4) - .5) * 1.6 + .5, 0, 1));\n  // the strata: a column of bands (rock.colors repeated, each band split by a thin darker line), read by world height\n  const R = def.rock || {}, bands = (R.colors || ['#9c6a4c', '#b98058', '#8a5a40', '#c49268', '#a87050', '#7c5038']).map(c => E.hex(c)), bh = 16;\n  const scv = document.createElement('canvas'); scv.width = 1; scv.height = bands.length * bh; const sg = scv.getContext('2d'), simg = sg.createImageData(1, scv.height);\n  for (let y = 0; y < scv.height; y++) { const c = bands[Math.floor(y / bh)], k = y % bh === 0 ? .72 : y % bh === 1 ? .86 : 1 + (E.hash2(y, 3) - .5) * .12, i = y * 4; simg.data[i] = clamp(c[0] * k, 0, 255); simg.data[i + 1] = clamp(c[1] * k, 0, 255); simg.data[i + 2] = clamp(c[2] * k, 0, 255); simg.data[i + 3] = 255; }\n  sg.putImageData(simg, 0, 0); const strata = own(new THREE.CanvasTexture(scv)); strata.wrapS = strata.wrapT = THREE.RepeatWrapping; strata.colorSpace = THREE.SRGBColorSpace; strata.magFilter = THREE.LinearFilter;\n  const band = (R.band || 40) / U * bands.length, s0 = R.slope ? R.slope[0] : .32, s1 = R.slope ? R.slope[1] : .5, dk = def.speckle ?? .22, mk = def.mottle ?? .3;\n  const wp = positionWorld, vcol = attribute('color', 'vec3');\n  const fine = texture(speck, wp.xz.mul(.75)).r.sub(.5).mul(dk).add(1), broad = texture(mottle, wp.xz.mul(.012)).r.sub(.5).mul(mk).add(1);\n  const wob = texture(mottle, wp.xz.mul(.05)).r.sub(.5).mul(.35);\n  const rockC = texture(strata, vec2(.5, wp.y.div(band).add(wob))).rgb.mul(texture(speck, vec2(wp.x.add(wp.z), wp.y).mul(.9)).r.sub(.5).mul(.3).add(1));\n  const steep = smoothstep(float(s0), float(s1), float(1).sub(normalWorld.y));\n  const mat = this.mat = world._obj(new THREE.MeshLambertNodeMaterial({ color: '#ffffff' }));\n  mat.colorNode = mix(vcol.mul(fine).mul(broad), rockC.mul(broad), steep);\n  world._own(mat);\n  // one index for every mesh: the grid's two triangles a cell (NW-SW-SE, NW-SE-NE: the colliders' split), then the skirts\n  const idx = [], at = (i, j) => j * (n + 1) + i, sk = (side, k) => (n + 1) * (n + 1) + side * (n + 1) + k;\n  for (let j = 0; j < n; j++) for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) { const nw = at(i, j), ne = at(i + 1, j), sw = at(i, j + 1), se = at(i + 1, j + 1); idx.push(nw, sw, se, nw, se, ne); }\n  const edge = [k => at(k, 0), k => at(n, k), k => at(n - k, n), k => at(0, n - k)];   // north, east, south, west, each running round clockwise\n  for (let side = 0; side < 4; side++) for (let k = 0; k < n; k++) { const a = edge[side](k), b = edge[side](k + 1), a2 = sk(side, k), b2 = sk(side, k + 1); idx.push(a, b, b2, a, b2, a2, a, b2, b, a, a2, b2); }\n  const index = new THREE.BufferAttribute(new Uint32Array(idx), 1);\n  this._pool = []; this._nodes = new Map(); this._edge = edge; this._V = V; this._frame = 0;\n  for (let k = 0, np = def.pool || (n <= 16 ? 400 : TERRAIN_POOL); k < np; k++) {\n    const geo = own(new THREE.BufferGeometry());\n    geo.setAttribute('position', new THREE.BufferAttribute(new Float32Array(V * 3), 3)); geo.setAttribute('normal', new THREE.BufferAttribute(new Float32Array(V * 3), 3));\n    geo.setAttribute('color', new THREE.BufferAttribute(new Float32Array(V * 3), 3)); geo.setIndex(index);\n    geo.boundingSphere = new THREE.Sphere(); geo.boundingBox = new THREE.Box3();\n    const m = new THREE.Mesh(geo, mat); m.visible = false; m.receiveShadow = true; m.matrixAutoUpdate = false; world.scene.add(m);\n    this._pool.push({ mesh: m, key: null, used: -1, shown: -1 });\n  }\n};\n/** fill a pooled mesh with node (L, nx, ny): (n + 1)^2 vertices 2^L cells apart, their normals from the samples round\n *  them, their colors from the game, and the skirts hanging below its edges */\nTerrain.prototype._build = function (slot, L, nx, ny) {\n  const n = this.n, s = 2 ** L, gx0 = nx * n * s, gy0 = ny * n * s, c = this.cell, colorOf = this.def.color, geo = slot.mesh.geometry;\n  const P = geo.attributes.position.array, N = geo.attributes.normal.array, C = geo.attributes.color.array, hs = this._hs || (this._hs = new Float32Array((n + 3) * (n + 3)));\n  // the heights, one sample beyond each edge for the normals\n  for (let j = -1; j <= n + 1; j++) for (let i = -1; i <= n + 1; i++) hs[(j + 1) * (n + 3) + i + 1] = this.sample(gx0 + i * s, gy0 + j * s);\n  let lo = 1e9, hi = -1e9; const nm = [0, 0, 1], col = [0, 0, 0], k2 = 1 / 255;\n  for (let j = 0; j <= n; j++) for (let i = 0; i <= n; i++) {\n    const v = j * (n + 1) + i, h = hs[(j + 1) * (n + 3) + i + 1], x = (gx0 + i * s) * c, y = (gy0 + j * s) * c;\n    const ddx = (hs[(j + 1) * (n + 3) + i + 2] - hs[(j + 1) * (n + 3) + i]) / (2 * s * c), ddy = (hs[(j + 2) * (n + 3) + i + 1] - hs[j * (n + 3) + i + 1]) / (2 * s * c), l = Math.hypot(ddx, ddy, 1);\n    nm[0] = -ddx / l; nm[1] = -ddy / l; nm[2] = 1 / l;\n    P[v * 3] = x / U; P[v * 3 + 1] = h / U; P[v * 3 + 2] = y / U; N[v * 3] = nm[0]; N[v * 3 + 1] = nm[2]; N[v * 3 + 2] = nm[1];\n    col[0] = 150; col[1] = 140; col[2] = 110;\n    const r = (colorOf && colorOf(x, y, h, nm[2], col)) || col;\n    C[v * 3] = srgbLin(r[0] * k2); C[v * 3 + 1] = srgbLin(r[1] * k2); C[v * 3 + 2] = srgbLin(r[2] * k2);\n    if (h < lo) lo = h; if (h > hi) hi = h;\n  }\n  const drop = (s * c) * .75 + 6;\n  for (let side = 0; side < 4; side++) for (let k = 0; k <= n; k++) {\n    const a = this._edge[side](k), b = (n + 1) * (n + 1) + side * (n + 1) + k;\n    P[b * 3] = P[a * 3]; P[b * 3 + 1] = P[a * 3 + 1] - drop / U; P[b * 3 + 2] = P[a * 3 + 2];\n    for (let q = 0; q < 3; q++) { N[b * 3 + q] = N[a * 3 + q]; C[b * 3 + q] = C[a * 3 + q] * .8; }\n  }\n  for (const a of ['position', 'normal', 'color']) geo.attributes[a].needsUpdate = true;\n  const x0 = gx0 * c / U, y0 = gy0 * c / U, w = n * s * c / U;\n  geo.boundingBox.min.set(x0, (lo - drop) / U, y0); geo.boundingBox.max.set(x0 + w, hi / U, y0 + w); geo.boundingBox.getBoundingSphere(geo.boundingSphere);\n  slot.mesh.castShadow = L <= 1; slot.key = L + ':' + nx + ':' + ny; slot.L = L;\n};\n/** world.draw's step: pick the quadtree's nodes for a camera at (x, y, z) (engine units), build up to `budget` missing\n *  ones (all of them when budget is Infinity: the first frame), show those and hide the rest */\nTerrain.prototype.drawStream = function (world, x, y, z, budget = TERRAIN_BUILDS, again = false) {\n  // frame: what this frame built or showed is never taken for another node in it; pass: what the last look showed\n  const frame = again ? this._frame : ++this._frame, pass = this._pass = (this._pass || 0) + 1, show = this._show || (this._show = []), queue = this._queue || (this._queue = []); show.length = 0; queue.length = 0;\n  const nodes = this._nodes, n = this.n, cs = this.cs, far = this.far, K = this.split;\n  const ready = (L, nx, ny) => nodes.get(L + ':' + nx + ':' + ny);\n  // nearest first, so what stands closest is built first\n  // a node splits into its four when the camera is within K of its size; one whose four aren't all built yet stands in\n  // for them (and they are queued); one not built itself is queued, and its parent stands in\n  const visit = (L, nx, ny) => {\n    const size = cs * 2 ** L, x0 = nx * size, y0 = ny * size, dx = Math.max(x0 - x, 0, x - x0 - size), dy = Math.max(y0 - y, 0, y - y0 - size), d = Math.hypot(dx, dy);\n    if (d > far) return;\n    const me = ready(L, nx, ny);\n    if (L > 0 && d < size * K) {\n      const kids = [[2 * nx, 2 * ny], [2 * nx + 1, 2 * ny], [2 * nx, 2 * ny + 1], [2 * nx + 1, 2 * ny + 1]];\n      const missing = kids.filter(([a, b]) => !ready(L - 1, a, b) && !this._outside(L - 1, a, b, x, y));\n      if (!missing.length) { for (const [a, b] of kids) visit(L - 1, a, b); return; }\n      for (const [a, b] of missing) queue.push([d, L - 1, a, b]);\n    }\n    if (!me) { queue.push([d, L, nx, ny]); return; }\n    me.used = frame; me.shown = pass; show.push(me);\n  };\n  visit(this.levels, 0, 0);\n  queue.sort((a, b) => a[0] - b[0] || a[1] - b[1]);\n  let built = 0;\n  for (const [, L, nx, ny] of queue) {\n    if (built >= budget) break;\n    const key = L + ':' + nx + ':' + ny; if (nodes.has(key)) continue;\n    // the slot touched longest ago (never one shown or built this frame)\n    let slot = null; for (const p of this._pool) if (p.used < frame && (!slot || p.used < slot.used)) slot = p;\n    if (!slot) break;\n    if (slot.key) nodes.delete(slot.key);\n    this._build(slot, L, nx, ny); slot.used = frame; nodes.set(key, slot); built++;\n  }\n  for (const p of this._pool) p.mesh.visible = p.shown === pass;\n  if (built && budget === Infinity) return this.drawStream(world, x, y, z, Infinity, true);\n  return built;\n};\nTerrain.prototype._outside = function (L, nx, ny, x, y) { const size = this.cs * 2 ** L, dx = Math.max(nx * size - x, 0, x - nx * size - size), dy = Math.max(ny * size - y, 0, y - ny * size - size); return Math.hypot(dx, dy) > this.far; };\n/** straight lines over open ground: a terrain's flow field (world.flow()) never steers */\nclass TerrainFlow { to() { return this; } dir() { return null; } distance(x, y) { return 1e9; } }\nconst srgbLin = c => c <= .04045 ? c / 12.92 : Math.pow((c + .055) / 1.055, 2.4);\n\n/* =============================================================================\n * 4. PARTS DRAWN BY CODE  instanced batches of four shapes (tube, ball, box, cone) in a toon look with outlines, and\n *    two that glow (glow, halo); a pen that draws with them in engine units. Puppets, things and anything a game draws\n *    in 3D go through them, so thousands of parts cost a handful of draw calls\n * ============================================================================= */","numLines":245,"startLine":863,"totalLines":3302}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01XRuvbtbetLk7vfEyhS6ExL","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
