 u 1.9 pads 0 kmh 200 \n5 go ds 0 u 1.9 pads 0 kmh 200 \n8 go ds 17 u 1.6 pads 0 kmh 231 \n12 go ds 45 u 0.4 pads 0 kmh 263 \n16 go ds 75 u -1.3 pads 0 kmh 285 \n20 go ds 108 u -2.6 pads 0 kmh 300 \n24 go ds 142 u -3.2 pads 0 kmh 307 \n28 go ds 176 u -1.5 pads 0 kmh 308 \n32 go ds 211 u -0.6 pads 1 kmh 338 \n36 go ds 250 u -1.5 pads 1 kmh 357 \n40 go ds 290 u -4.1 pads 1 kmh 347 \n44 go ds 327 u -6.0 pads 1 kmh 328 \n48 go ds 364 u -8.0 pads 1 kmh 327 \n52 go ds 401 u -8.4 pads 1 kmh 327 \n56 go ds 437 u -6.5 pads 1 kmh 291 \n60 go ds 468 u -3.5 pads 1 kmh 279 \n64 go ds 500 u -1.4 pads 1 kmh 285 \n68 go ds 532 u 0.4 pads 1 kmh 293 \n72 go ds 562 u 1.7 pads 1 kmh 255 \n76 go ds 588 u 2.1 pads 1 kmh 216","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"staleReadFileStateHint":"[This command modified 2 files you've previously read: tests/lib/bot.mjs, src/40-race.js. Call Read before editing.]","bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261103-184648__xa320fb/agent.out","hunks":[{"oldStart":1723,"oldLines":3,"newStart":1723,"newLines":8,"lines":[" {\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-5-5\",\"id\":\"msg_011Cgh9TMvjrizGotB1ZoLXq\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"toolu_01CqtfgKMQb9ixvv7BNKgQAU\",\"name\":\"Bash\",\"input\":{\"command\":\"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261103-184648__xa320fb/work/SnipeoutHD-WipeoutHD-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261103-184648 && python3 - <<'EOF'\\np='src/11-data-about.js'; s=open(p).read()\\na=s.index(\\\"  testingFeedback: [\\\"); b=s.index(\\\"  engineChanges: [\\\")\\nnew='''  testingFeedback: [\\n    'About 27 real issues, caught by the headless suites, the bot-driven scripts and the screenshot reviews (plus a few bugs in the tests themselves). Examples: two scene fields named view and res that the engine silently treats as scene options, a crash entering the menu, replays drifting out of sync (quantised controls, the intro skip, a test bot sharing the autopilot\\\\\\\\'s AI state), the AI Hub round never calling ready() after a rename, craft popping up onto the far side of the gorge instead of crashing into it, the railshot missing at range, mouse hover not moving the focus, menu buttons losing their hit boxes, mirrored sign boards, and weapons eliminating five of eight craft a race.',\\n    'About 7 were critical: the menu crash, the Academy crash on entry, the hub session never starting (ready() never called), replays desyncing (two separate causes), the team screen\\\\\\\\'s CONFIRM button not drawn or clickable, and unbound keys not leaving the attract mode.',\\n    'The scripted playthrough of the whole game (attract, academy, all ten season events with briefings and promotions, the four-race Grand Prix, the ending, then every other mode, a replay and dev mode): it caught balance problems, drill limits and state leaking between modes that no unit test would. The AI Hub mock was a close second: it found the round that never started.',\\n    'The pixel-brightness check of screenshots: it mostly flagged the deliberately black Overclock skin. Real visual problems (mirrored boards, the cluttered hangar, missing glyphs) were found by looking at the screenshots.'\\n  ],\\n  engineFeedback: [\\n    'Everything around the game came for free and worked: fixed 1/120 s steps, headless game.advance for tests, the boot screen, pause menu, settings, key rebinding, saves, per-player input with half keyboards and split screen. World3D let me add my own three.js meshes and cameras under the same pixel HUD, fonts, dialog boxes and character portraits.',\\n    'Yes. Scene objects\\\\\\\\' own fields named view and res are read as scene options (a warning, then wrong behaviour); game.go takes the fade as a third argument; mouse movement does not change input.lastDevice; the wheel is only reported where a scene allows zoom; text planes came out mirrored through the engine-to-three axis swap; and headless WebGPU (SwiftShader) loses its device, so browser tests run on ?backend=webgl.',\\n    'Track-space hover physics on a banked spline ribbon (hover spring, grip cap, airbrakes, walls, gaps, drops, tunnels, overpasses), with the track mesh builder and the terrain carving around it. World3D\\\\\\\\'s own track and Rapier-ball vehicles cannot model Wipeout speeds, tunnels, drops, gaps or overpasses.',\\n    'Coordinate conventions: the engine\\\\\\\\'s axes (x east, y south, z up) mapped to three.js by a reflection, which flips triangle winding, the camera roll sign and texture direction; I had to verify each by screenshot.',\\n    'Five marked edits: PlayStation button symbols by default and the option moved to Display; PlayStation symbols in both pixel fonts; analog button values (input.value) for L2/R2 airbrakes; synth extensions (lowpass envelopes, unison, pan, accents, claps, sub booms, sidechain) for an electronic soundtrack; and a game-supplied particle ground in World3D so sparks land on the track deck.',\\n    'A first-class ribbon track in World3D with track-space queries (s, u, h), arbitrary banking, tunnels, gaps and overpasses. Or, smaller: keep scene options in their own object so a scene\\\\\\\\'s game state can never collide with them.'\\n  ],\\n  promptFeedback: [\\n    'The done criteria are concrete and testable: one file, no stubs, a dev mode with sliders, attract after 10 s, touch-only behaviour, controller-first prompts with an Xbox option, hub integration with a harness to prove it. The testing rules (one command, failures only, a one-line count) kept the feedback loop fast.',\\n    'Where the 3D add-on stands: the brief says to build on dist/handoff, whose 2D views cannot show a banked, looping 3D track, while the add-on that can lives outside that folder. Also the plan was written for another run\\\\\\\\'s folder and file names, so TASK.md\\\\\\\\'s names had to override it.',\\n    'The breadth in one pass: eleven modes, a season with a Grand Prix and an ending, the academy, attract, dev mode, split screen and AI Hub sessions, each tested, while judging a 3D picture only from screenshots.',\\n    'Say how to weigh scope against polish when time is short, and name a reference screen size and refresh rate for the 10-foot UI. State plainly whether add-ons from the engine repository count as part of the engine.'\\n  ],\\n'''\\ns=s[:a]+new+s[b:]\\ns=s.replace(\\\"    research: 'None beyond the plan; the engine docs and the AI Hub README were read',\\\",\\\"    research: 'None beyond the plan: PLAN.md, the engine\\\\\\\\'s API card and the World3D header, and the AI Hub README',\\\")\\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\\nEOF\\nnode --check src/11-data-about.js && node tools/exit-interview.mjs\",\"description\":\"Write the final feedback answers; regenerate the exit interview\"},\"caller\":{\"type\":\"direct\"}}],\"container\":null,\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":1312,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":727700,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":1312},\"output_tokens\":6,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"global\",\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"input_transformations\":[],\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"f4eed361-ef26-4b83-9819-20dffd5cdae7\",\"uuid\":\"61dcc43d-ea60-447b-bab3-3e6e7620d566\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-04T03:05:02.547Z\",\"request_id\":\"req_011Cgh9TMYvQqopjisdd2jtu\",\"wire_tool_inputs\":{\"toolu_01CqtfgKMQb9ixvv7BNKgQAU\":{\"command\":\"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261103-184648__xa320fb/work/SnipeoutHD-WipeoutHD-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261103-184648 && python3 - <<'EOF'\\np='src/11-data-about.js'; s=open(p).read()\\na=s.index(\\\"  testingFeedback: [\\\"); b=s.index(\\\"  engineChanges: [\\\")\\nnew='''  testingFeedback: [\\n    'About 27 real issues, caught by the headless suites, the bot-driven scripts and the screenshot reviews (plus a few bugs in the tests themselves). Examples: two scene fields named view and res that the engine silently treats as scene options, a crash entering the menu, replays drifting out of sync (quantised controls, the intro skip, a test bot sharing the autopilot\\\\\\\\'s AI state), the AI Hub round never calling ready() after a rename, craft popping up onto the far side of the gorge instead of crashing into it, the railshot missing at range, mouse hover not moving the focus, menu buttons losing their hit boxes, mirrored sign boards, and weapons eliminating five of eight craft a race.',\\n    'About 7 were critical: the menu crash, the Academy crash on entry, the hub session never starting (ready() never called), replays desyncing (two separate causes), the team screen\\\\\\\\'s CONFIRM button not drawn or clickable, and unbound keys not leaving the attract mode.',\\n    'The scripted playthrough of the whole game (attract, academy, all ten season events with briefings and promotions, the four-race Grand Prix, the ending, then every other mode, a replay and dev mode): it caught balance problems, drill limits and state leaking between modes that no unit test would. The AI Hub mock was a close second: it found the round that never started.',\\n    'The pixel-brightness check of screenshots: it mostly flagged the deliberately black Overclock skin. Real visual problems (mirrored boards, the cluttered hangar, missing glyphs) were found by looking at the screenshots.'\\n  ],\\n  engineFeedback: [\\n    'Everything around the game came for free and worked: fixed 1/120 s steps, headless game.advance for tests, the boot screen, pause menu, settings, key rebinding, saves, per-player input with half keyboards and split screen. World3D let me add my own three.js meshes and cameras under the same pixel HUD, fonts, dialog boxes and character portraits.',\\n    'Yes. Scene objects\\\\\\\\' own fields named view and res are read as scene options (a warning, then wrong behaviour); game.go takes the fade as a third argument; mouse movement does not change input.lastDevice; the wheel is only reported where a scene allows zoom; text planes came out mirrored through the engine-to-three axis swap; and headless WebGPU (SwiftShader) loses its device, so browser tests run on ?backend=webgl.',\\n    'Track-space hover physics on a banked spline ribbon (hover spring, grip cap, airbrakes, walls, gaps, drops, tunnels, overpasses), with the track mesh builder and the terrain carving around it. World3D\\\\\\\\'s own track and Rapier-ball vehicles cannot model Wipeout speeds, tunnels, drops, gaps or overpasses.',\\n    'Coordinate conventions: the engine\\\\\\\\'s axes (x east, y south, z up) mapped to three.js by a reflection, which flips triangle winding, the camera roll sign and texture direction; I had to verify each by screenshot.',\\n    'Five marked edits: PlayStation button symbols by default and the option moved to Display; PlayStation symbols in both pixel fonts; analog button values (input.value) for L2/R2 airbrakes; synth extensions (lowpass envelopes, unison, pan, accents, claps, sub booms, sidechain) for an electronic soundtrack; and a game-supplied particle ground in World3D so sparks land on the track deck.',\\n    'A first-class ribbon track in World3D with track-space queries (s, u, h), arbitrary banking, tunnels, gaps and overpasses. Or, smaller: keep scene options in their own object so a scene\\\\\\\\'s game state can never collide with them.'\\n  ],\\n  promptFeedback: [\\n    'The done criteria are concrete and testable: one file, no stubs, a dev mode with sliders, attract after 10 s, touch-only behaviour, controller-first prompts with an Xbox option, hub integration with a harness to prove it. The testing rules (one command, failures only, a one-line count) kept the feedback loop fast.',\\n    'Where the 3D add-on stands: the brief says to build on dist/handoff, whose 2D views cannot show a banked, looping 3D track, while the add-on that can lives outside that folder. Also the plan was written for another run\\\\\\\\'s folder and file names, so TASK.md\\\\\\\\'s names had to override it.',\\n    'The breadth in one pass: eleven modes, a season with a Grand Prix and an ending, the academy, attract, dev mode, split screen and AI Hub sessions, each tested, while judging a 3D picture only from screenshots.',\\n    'Say how to weigh scope against polish when time is short, and name a reference screen size and refresh rate for the 10-foot UI. State plainly whether add-ons from the engine repository count as part of the engine.'\\n  ],\\n'''\\ns=s[:a]+new+s[b:]\\ns=s.replace(\\\"    research: 'None beyond the plan; the engine docs and the AI Hub README were read',\\\",\\\"    research: 'None beyond the plan: PLAN.md, the engine\\\\\\\\'s API card and the World3D header, and the AI Hub README',\\\")\\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\\nEOF\\nnode --check src/11-data-about.js && node tools/exit-interview.mjs\",\"description\":\"Write the final feedback answers; regenerate the exit interview\"}}}"," {\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01CqtfgKMQb9ixvv7BNKgQAU\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"exit-interview.json written and parses\\n[This command modified 1 file you've previously read: src/11-data-about.js. Call Read before editing.]\",\"is_error\":false}]},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"f4eed361-ef26-4b83-9819-20dffd5cdae7\",\"uuid\":\"0ef5d0f3-fd46-4f34-b2b1-4004e7d0aadd\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-04T03:05:02.645Z\",\"tool_use_result\":{\"stdout\":\"exit-interview.json written and parses\",\"stderr\":\"\",\"interrupted\":false,\"isImage\":false,\"noOutputExpected\":false,\"staleReadFileStateHint\":\"[This command modified 1 file you've previously read: src/11-data-about.js. Call Read before editi