{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\n<system-reminder>\n<tools-used-before-summary>Bash, Edit, Read, Write</tools-used-before-summary>\n</system-reminder>\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The only user message was the `/goal` command: \"Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says (TASK.md describes the game). Done when: the bundled single .html file exists in this folder's root, every feature in TASK.md is implemented with no TODOs, placeholders or stubs, exit-interview.json in this folder's root parses as JSON and answers every field, and your final reply contains the Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback sections.\" A Stop hook enforces this.\n   - STAGE.md: read TASK.md (what to build) and PLAN.md (how, by claude-opus-5-5 max); build it with the title the plan gives; where they disagree TASK.md wins; deliver TASK.md's file name and the reply sections.\n   - TASK.md (key constraints, preserved): source Wipeout HD; single html `[GameTitle-SOURCE-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261103-184630].html` in root; dev subfolder `[GameTitle-SOURCE-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261103-184630]`; build on my-3d2dge handoff (may change engine); engine-native art/animation plus new assets; all audio in code, Animalese/Simlish gibberish voices; AI Hub (ai-hub lib/hub) multiplayer plus the game on its own; \"Do not read files outside what you need - other agents share this directory. They share this machine's ports and processes too. Prefer file:// and the engine's headless tools. If you need a server (the AI Hub harness does), bind 127.0.0.1 on a port the OS picks (`python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1` prints it) and confirm the page is your game before trusting a result. Stop only processes you started, by their PID: never pkill, killall, fuser -k, or kill whatever holds a port.\"; testing behind one command printing only failures and a one-line count; \"Don't use subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit.\"; dev mode from the pause menu with live sliders + reset; attract mode after 10 s idle, any input exits; 10-foot controller-first UI (DualSense standard mapping; PlayStation glyphs default, Settings option for Xbox; keyboard/mouse native, hover moves focus; prompts follow last device); touch-only: \"Controller or keyboard required\" + settings button, attract runs, no touch controls; no TODOs/placeholders/stubs; Source Information/Testing/Engine/Prompt Feedback in chat reply AND in-game About/Credits (\"unknown\" where unconfirmable); exit-interview.json in exact shape beside the html.\n   - Commit/push only if asked (not asked; do not commit).\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - my-3D2dge v0.85.2 handoff engine (E.Game fixed step 1/120, scenes, boot steps, standard HTML pause menu with `menu.items` as a function, settings, input.label, game.saves, E.Dialog, E.font, px.*, splitScreen/addPlayer/halfKeys) + World3D 3D add-on (three.js r182 WebGPURenderer→WebGL2 fallback, Rapier 0.19.3 via CDN import map, terrain streaming, 'fixed' camera with step interpolation, world.pen, world.glow, world.project, addCamera for split screen, node materials only).\n   - Engine axes x east, y south, z up (left-handed); toThree (x/16, z/16, y/16); right = cross(up, forward); bank>0 lowers right edge; camera rollSign = -1 (verified by Karakum spiral screenshot).\n   - Track-space physics (s, u, h), centripetal Catmull-Rom slices every 2 m, local Newton locate (overpass-safe), drops/gaps/tunnels/open edges/pit/pads, racing line by multiscale elastic band, per-team speed profiles.\n   - Deterministic sim (no Math.random/Date.now in sim), quantised controls recorded per step, FNV hash, replay re-sim.\n   - AI Hub protocol 1 client 1.4.0, ghost mode, own card, ready() without key, progress/result/time-up/end.\n   - Tests: Node vm harness, Playwright browser on bundle from file://, real hub harness on python http.server port 0 killed by PID; TMPDIR=$PWD/.tmp because /tmp is full.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections (dev folder: /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261103-184630__xa320fb/work/SnipeoutHD-WipeoutHD-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261103-184630/):\n   - engine/my-3d2dge.js (edits marked `// SNIPEOUT EDIT:`): glyphs setting default 'playstation', group 'Display', options PS/Xbox, apply to all players; addPlayer copies glyphs; font glyphs ✕ ○ □ △ ◀ ▶ ↺ ✓ ° · – (5x7 G57) and ✕ ○ □ △ · – ▸ ◀ ▶ ↺ ✓ (3x5 GLYPHS); input.value(action) analog (padValues, _valueOverride); synth _voice lp/uni/det/pan/accent, DRUMS p (clap) and b (boom), _note accent '!' and sidechain duck via t._side gain; last change: comment \"a placeholder in the repo that tools/stamp\" reworded to \"a stand-in value in the repo that tools/stamp\".\n   - engine/my-3d2dge-3d.js: `g.particles.ground = this.o.particleGround || (...)`.\n   - vendor/aihub-session.js (pinned, byte-identical); tests/hub/{harness.html,bridge.js,round.js,README.md}.\n   - src/manifest.json order: 00-core, 01-input, 05-data-teams, 06-data-weapons, 07-data-tracks, 08-data-season, 09-data-story, 10-data-music, 11-data-about, 20-track, 25-ship, 27-collide, 30-weapons, 35-ai, 40-race, 45-replay, 50-audio, 55-glyphs, 60-render, 62-shipkit, 64-trackmesh, 66-scenery, 68-fx, 70-hud, 75-ui, 78-season-ui, 80-dev, 85-attract, 90-hub, 95-main.\n   - src/00-core.js: SN namespace, vectors SN.v, SN.frame, SN.rng/hashString/hashNumbers, SN.Tune registry (37 sliders in groups HANDLING, HANDLING 2, HOVER, WALLS & ENERGY, PADS & WEAPONS, AI, CAMERA), SN.cheats, SN.flags, event bus, formatting helpers.\n   - src/01-input.js: SN.INPUT preset (thrust W/Pad0, fire Space/Mouse0/Pad2, absorb ShiftLeft/Mouse2/Pad1, brakeL Q/Pad6, brakeR E/Pad7, camera C/Pad3, shiftL Z/Pad4, shiftR X/Pad5, brake S, lookBack B/Pad11, tabL, tabR, more Tab/M/Pad3); SN.Controls (ramped keys, stick passthrough, double-tap Q/E side-shift, flick), SN.vpad, SN.wheel, SN.touchOnly (SN._fakeTouchOnly in Node).\n   - src/05-data-teams.js: 6 teams, designs, 12 pilots, principals, ORACLE, classes (SPARK 1440, FLARE 1840, STORM 2240, SINGULARITY 2720 u/s), DIFFICULTY now `Easy { skill: .60, aggression: .6, rb: 1.5, hurt: .55 }, Normal { skill: .78, aggression: 1.0, rb: 1.0, hurt: .75 }, Hard { skill: .93, aggression: 1.3, rb: .3, hurt: 1 }`, SN.craftStats.\n   - src/07-data-tracks.js: 4 tracks verbatim from plan; SN.MEDAL_TIMES written by tools/medals.mjs (32 sets, e.g. solenne/SPARK/hotlap [46.3,49,53.4]).\n   - src/08/09/10: season (tiers t1-t4, events e1-e10, gp), story lines, songs (zero, solenne, karakum, meridian, borealis, overclock; ≥16 bars, named layers) + stings.\n   - src/11-data-about.js: SN.ABOUT source fields, Q lists, testingFeedback(4), engineFeedback(6), promptFeedback(4), engineChanges, credits, aiHub. usage now \"Cost and tokens unknown (no usage meter was available inside this session). Session time about 2 h 45 min of wall-clock time (2026-11-03 18:46 to about 21:30)...\"; testing field updated with 634 checks description.\n   - src/20-track.js: Track.build, frameAt, surface, locate, dS, point, query, groundBelow, _line, profile(top, alatK, gripMax), profileFor(key, top, gripMax) cache, vline, idealLap, minimap, validate. Lengths verified 3.844/4.595/4.177/5.030 km; overpasses 25.0 m and 31.9 m.\n   - src/25-ship.js: Ship class (method putOn, field place), Ship.damage (with difficulty hurt for humans), Ship.step physics, land, wallStep, padStep, startRescue (now moves set-down past a gap's far edge if within 350 m run-up), rescueStep.\n   - src/27-collide.js: sphere pairs, per-pair 0.5 s bump-damage cooldown.\n   - src/30-weapons.js: Weapons class (roll by position/pickupLuck, give, use, absorb, fire for 10 weapons, railTrace, targetAhead, hit, siphon, step); cannon dmg 1.25, tremor 15, mine 9, pop 450.\n   - src/35-ai.js: brain per key (o.brain), uAt option (lateral target override), per-team profile via profileFor, skillK = .80 + .2*skill, eager option for attract, weapon logic.\n   - src/40-race.js: MODES, Race (states intro/grid/countdown/racing/finished/results, quantised controls via Race.encode/decode recorded every step, skip recorded, _lapStep, positions (target modes sort by points), eliminate/respawn, zoneUp, endRun, seal, results, hash), \"all humans done while racing → _playerDone\", SN.field, DRILLS & SN.Academy (gates 100 m apart u ±4 m tolerance 3.5 m; mine line `for (const f of [-.78, -.33, .11]) ... u: gapSide * f * hw`).\n   - src/45-replay.js: SN.Replay.play/verify (tune & cheats snapshot, skip), SN.Ghost (20 Hz Int16 base64), SN.Records.\n   - src/50-audio.js: SFX catalogue, SN.Voice gibberish, announce/radio/subtitles, music director (layers), engine hums, event→sound mapping.\n   - src/55-glyphs.js: SN.glyph draw/pad/key/mouse/dir/bar/rich/richLines/richWidth.\n   - src/60-render.js: SN.poseFrom (now returns `wide: true`), ChaseCam (chase/far/cockpit/lookBack), FreeCam, spotsFor, TVDirector (fixed stale-shot bug: uses this.shot / S2), introPose, R.trackWorld, R.attach(tw, race, {prepare}), hangarWorld (40x30 hall, turntable at (20,7) tiles, podium rows 16-17), showCraft, onDraw, poseCrafts (trail dimmer/shorter for human).\n   - src/62-shipkit.js, 64-trackmesh.js, 66-scenery.js, 68-fx.js: craft meshes, track meshes (pit colors '#103a26'/'#144a30'), themes/terrain/scenery, effects (seeded flakes).\n   - src/70-hud.js: SN.hud views/callouts/draw (LAP max 1, name tags limited to 4 non-overlapping, cockpit dash H.dash, academy card wraps via richLines), minimap, radioBox, weapon icons, SN.portrait, SN.rigFor.\n   - src/75-ui.js: UI kit (UI.layout computes rects in update for mouse; UI.tick; hover counts newly appearing pointer), screens main/challenges/options/cls/track/team (exit clears SET.onTeam)/confirm/versus/versusTeams/howto/records/about.\n  